window.__LIZZWORD_DEEP_SHARD && window.__LIZZWORD_DEEP_SHARD("0094", [{"word":"territorial behavior","ipa_uk":"/ˌterɪˈtɔːriəl bɪˈheɪvjə/","ipa_us":"/ˌterɪˈtɔːriəl bɪˈheɪvjər/","definition_zh":"领地行为；动物划定、标记并守卫一片专属区域的行为","definition_en":"the behavior by which an animal claims a particular area, marks its boundary and keeps other individuals out","core_image":"一只鸟每天停在树篱的同一根枝条上鸣叫，把整片灌木丛划成自己的地盘","scene":"清晨的树篱边，一只雄鸟反复停在同一个枝头高声鸣唱，把这片灌木丛当成自己的地盘。A male songbird returns to the same twig each dawn and sings, a pattern that biologists record as territorial behavior.","sceneCN":"这里 territorial behavior 指「动物划定并守卫专属区域的行为」（第 1 个义项：用固定边界把同类排除在外）；句意为一只雄鸟每天清晨回到同一根枝条鸣唱，生物学家把这种规律性举动记录为领地行为。图中可辨识物件：树篱、同一根枝条、鸣唱的雄鸟、靠近的同类、看不见的边界线。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"领地行为（动物对一片区域的占有、标记与防卫；作不可数名词，指具体类型时可有复数）"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"territorial behavior in birds","zh":"鸟类的领地行为"},{"phrase":"display territorial behavior","zh":"表现出领地行为"},{"phrase":"aggressive territorial behavior","zh":"攻击性领地行为"},{"phrase":"seasonal territorial behavior","zh":"季节性领地行为"},{"phrase":"study territorial behavior","zh":"研究领地行为"},{"phrase":"territorial behavior patterns","zh":"领地行为模式"}],"forms":[{"label":"复数（不同物种或类型）","form":"territorial behaviors"},{"label":"相关形容词","form":"territorial"},{"label":"相关名词（领地性）","form":"territoriality"},{"label":"相关名词（领地）","form":"territory"},{"label":"相关名词（行为）","form":"behavior"},{"label":"相关形容词（行为的）","form":"behavioral"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"territoriality","pos":"n.","zh":"领地性；对空间的排他性占有倾向"},{"word":"territory","pos":"n.","zh":"领地；领土；势力范围"},{"word":"territorial","pos":"adj.","zh":"领地的；领土的"},{"word":"behavior","pos":"n.","zh":"行为；举止"},{"word":"territorialize","pos":"v.","zh":"把某片区域划为领地；使领地化"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Claim and hold an exclusive area","titleCN":"划定并独占一片区域","definition":"to claim a particular area as one's own and keep other individuals out of it","definitionCN":"把某片区域认作自己的地盘，并把其他个体排除在外","example":"The pair defends the same stretch of bank from spring to autumn.","exampleCN":"这一对鸟从春天到秋天守着同一段河岸。","why":"territorial draws a boundary around land, and behavior supplies the acts that enforce it; together they name the whole claim-and-exclude pattern.","whyCN":"territorial 划出土地的边界，behavior 提供执行边界的动作；合起来命名「宣称并排除」的整套模式。"},{"no":"02","title":"Drive intruders away","titleCN":"把入侵者赶走","definition":"to chase or attack individuals that enter the claimed area","definitionCN":"追赶或攻击进入所占地盘的同类个体","example":"The male chases every rival that crosses the hedge.","exampleCN":"雄鸟会追赶每一只越过树篱的对手。","why":"once a line is drawn, enforcement is the visible part of the behavior: pursuit, threat and contact are how the boundary is made real.","whyCN":"边界一旦划出，执法就是行为中看得见的部分：追击、威胁与身体接触让这条边界真正成立。"},{"no":"03","title":"Mark the boundary by signals","titleCN":"用鸣唱、气味或视觉标记标出边界","definition":"to advertise ownership through song, scent, calls or visual displays","definitionCN":"用鸣唱、气味、叫声或视觉展示宣告占有","example":"The warbler sings from the same post every morning.","exampleCN":"这只莺每天清晨在同一根木桩上鸣唱。","why":"a boundary is invisible unless it is broadcast, so marking is the cheap alternative to fighting: the signal says the owner is present and ready.","whyCN":"边界本身看不见，必须被广播出去；标记因此是打斗之外的低成本手段——信号说明主人就在附近且随时应战。"},{"no":"04","title":"Defend food, nests and mates","titleCN":"守住食物、巢址与配偶等资源","definition":"to protect the resources inside an area from being used by others","definitionCN":"保护区域内的资源不被其他个体使用","example":"Each pair keeps the insects near its nest for its own chicks.","exampleCN":"每一对鸟都把巢边的昆虫留给自己的雏鸟。","why":"territory is usually worth defending because it contains something scarce; the area is a container, and the resource is the reason for the container.","whyCN":"领地之所以值得守卫，通常因为其中装着稀缺资源；区域是容器，资源才是容器存在的理由。"},{"no":"05","title":"Seasonal territory in the breeding season","titleCN":"繁殖季出现的临时领地","definition":"a territory held only for part of the year, typically while breeding","definitionCN":"只在一年中某段时间、通常繁殖期才占有的领地","example":"The males arrive in April, claim a reed patch, and leave in July.","exampleCN":"雄鸟四月到达，占下一片芦苇，七月离开。","why":"when the young are reared and gone, the reason for the boundary disappears with them, so the territory can be given up without loss.","whyCN":"雏鸟养大离巢后，边界存在的理由也随之消失，因此领地可以毫无损失地放弃。"},{"no":"06","title":"Space individuals apart","titleCN":"把同类个体在空间上隔开","definition":"a spacing mechanism that keeps members of a population at a distance from one another","definitionCN":"一种把种群成员相互隔开的间距调节机制","example":"Density falls because singing males keep their neighbours at a distance.","exampleCN":"鸣唱的雄鸟让邻居保持距离，密度因此下降。","why":"seen from the population level, the same boundary works like a valve: it limits how many individuals can settle in one place.","whyCN":"从种群层面看，同一条边界像一道阀门：它限制了多少个体能在同一处落脚。"},{"no":"07","title":"Applied to human space","titleCN":"借用于人对空间与座位的占有","definition":"the human tendency to claim a seat, desk or corner and resent intrusion","definitionCN":"人占据座位、书桌或角落并反感他人侵入的倾向","example":"Office workers show territorial behavior over their desks.","exampleCN":"办公室职员对自己的书桌表现出领地行为。","why":"the word moved from animals to people because the same geometry appears in offices: a marked spot, a habitual user stream, and a sense of trespass.","whyCN":"这个词从动物扩展到人，是因为办公室里出现同样的几何关系：被标记的位置、惯常使用者，以及被侵犯的感觉。"},{"no":"08","title":"A measurable category in field studies","titleCN":"野外研究中可观察、可计数的行为类别","definition":"a recorded class of actions such as patrols, songs and chases used in behavioral research","definitionCN":"行为研究中记录的一类动作，如巡逻、鸣唱与追赶","example":"The observer logs every chase as one bout of territorial behavior.","exampleCN":"观察者把每一次追赶记为一次领地行为。","why":"science needs countable units; naming the whole pattern lets a field worker turn scattered actions into a column of numbers.","whyCN":"科学需要可计数的单位；给整套模式命名，野外工作者才能把零散动作变成一列数字。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Territorial comes from Latin terra 'earth' through territorium, while behavior is a native English formation from be- plus have. The full phrase is a twentieth-century ethological term. Dates are approximate.","cn":"territorial 经 territorium 源自拉丁 terra「土地」；behavior 是英语本土构造，由 be- 加 have 构成。整个短语是 20 世纪的动物行为学术语。年代为约数。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN TERRA","en":"Terra meant 'earth, dry land'; from it Latin built territorium, the land lying around a town and subject to its control.","cn":"terra 意为「土地、干地」；拉丁语由此构成 territorium，指城邦周边受其控制的土地。"},{"era":"LATIN TERRITORIALIS","en":"Late Latin territorialis 'of a territory' passed through French and entered English as territorial in the early seventeenth century.","cn":"晚期拉丁 territorialis 意为「领地所属的」，经法语进入英语，17 世纪初形成 territorial。"},{"era":"OLD ENGLISH AND MIDDLE ENGLISH BEHAVE","en":"Behavior derives from behave, formed in Middle English from be- plus have (Old English habban 'to hold'); to behave is literally to hold or bear oneself in a certain way.","cn":"behavior 来自 behave；behave 是中古英语由 be- 加 have（古英语 habban「持有」）构成，字面义是「以某种方式持住自己」。"},{"era":"ETHOLOGY, TWENTIETH CENTURY","en":"Territorial behavior became a standard label in animal behavior studies in the early twentieth century, when field workers began mapping areas that birds and mammals defend.","cn":"20 世纪初，野外研究者开始绘制鸟类与哺乳动物防卫的区域，territorial behavior 由此成为动物行为学的标准说法。"},{"era":"UNCERTAIN DETAILS","en":"Source uncertain (first dates): the earliest use of the exact phrase territorial behavior is not precisely recorded, and the boundary between territory and home range is defined differently across schools.","cn":"来源不确定（首见年代）：territorial behavior 这一确切短语的最早书证没有精确记录；不同学派对「领地」与「活动范围」的界线定义也不一致。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"Group one holds forms from the same territorial family that are easily swapped; group two holds spatial and behavioral terms with overlapping meanings.","cn":"第一组是同一 territorial 词族里容易被混用的形式；第二组是含义有重叠的空间与行为术语。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"territoriality","ipa":"/ˌterɪtɔːriˈæləti/","tag":"the abstract noun","definition":"The tendency or system of holding and defending a territory; it names the principle, not the observable acts.","definitionCN":"占有并防卫领地的倾向或制度；指原则本身，而非可观察的动作。"},{"word":"territory","ipa":"/ˈterətri/","tag":"the place, not the acts","definition":"The area itself that is claimed; territory can exist on a map even when no animal is currently patrolling it.","definitionCN":"被宣称占有的那块地方；即使当下没有动物巡逻，领地在图上仍可存在。"},{"word":"territorial","ipa":"/ˌterɪˈtɔːriəl/","tag":"adjective only","definition":"Pertaining to a territory; it needs a noun such as behavior, waters or dispute to complete it.","definitionCN":"意为「领地的」；必须搭配 behavior、waters 或 dispute 之类名词才完整。"},{"word":"territorial waters","ipa":"/ˌterɪˈtɔːriəl ˈwɔːtəz/","tag":"legal compound","definition":"A belt of sea under a state's jurisdiction; the same adjective, but the boundary is legal rather than behavioral.","definitionCN":"受国家管辖的近海带；形容词相同，但边界是法律划定的，不是行为划出的。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"home range","ipa":"/ˈhəʊm reɪndʒ/","tag":"used, not defended","definition":"The area an animal routinely uses for feeding and shelter; unlike a territory, it is not actively defended against all rivals.","definitionCN":"动物日常觅食与栖居所用的区域；与领地不同，它并不主动排除所有同类。"},{"word":"dominance behavior","ipa":"/dəˈmɪnəns bɪˈheɪvjə/","tag":"rank, not space","definition":"Actions that establish rank within a group; dominance is about who yields, territory is about where others may not go.","definitionCN":"在群体中确立等级的动作；dominance 关乎谁让步，territory 关乎别人不能去哪里。"},{"word":"aggression","ipa":"/əˈɡreʃn/","tag":"the force used","definition":"Attacking or threatening; it is one tool of territorial defense, not the whole pattern.","definitionCN":"攻击或威胁；它只是领地防卫的一种手段，并不等于整套模式。"},{"word":"spacing behavior","ipa":"/ˈspeɪsɪŋ bɪˈheɪvjə/","tag":"the population view","definition":"Any behavior that regulates distance between individuals; territorial defense is one form of it.","definitionCN":"任何调节个体间距的行为；领地防卫是其中一种形式。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Normal associations: real morphemes, real collocations and real relatives, not invented rhymes.","cn":"正常联想：真实的构词成分、真实搭配与真实同族词，而非编造的顺口溜。"},"normal":[{"en":"terra 'land' gives territorium 'land around a town', then territorial 'of a territory'; add behavior and you have the acts that hold that land.","cn":"terra「土地」构成 territorium「城郊土地」，再形成 territorial「领地的」；加上 behavior，就是守住那片土地的动作。"},{"en":"The family runs territory, territorial, territoriality, territorialize and behavior.","cn":"同族词包括 territory、territorial、territoriality、territorialize 与 behavior。"},{"en":"Fixed phrases mark the core: defend a territory, mark a boundary, drive off intruders, hold a home range.","cn":"固定搭配标出核心：守卫领地、标出边界、赶走入侵者、占据活动范围。"},{"en":"A territory is defended; a home range is merely used. The pair of terms is a standard exam distinction.","cn":"领地要被守卫，活动范围只是被使用；这一对术语是常见的考试区分点。"},{"en":"The adjective territorial is almost always followed by a noun, so the phrase itself is the unit to memorize.","cn":"形容词 territorial 后面几乎总要跟名词，因此要记的单位正是整个短语。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture a fence drawn in scent rather than wire, invisible to us but sharp to a dog.","cn":"想象一道用气味而不是铁丝画出的篱笆，人看不见，狗却分得清。"},{"en":"Picture a singer returning to the same post every dawn, not for the song but for the line it draws.","cn":"想象一只鸟每天清晨回到同一根木桩，不为唱歌，而为歌声划出的那条线。"},{"en":"Picture a crowded beach where every group leaves one empty towel-width between itself and the next.","cn":"想象拥挤的海滩上，每一群人都与邻座留出一条毛巾宽的空隙。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"Wolves scent-mark the pack's boundary throughout the year.","cn":"狼群全年都在用气味标记群体的边界。"},{"en":"Bluebirds defend a nest box against other pairs of the same species.","cn":"蓝鸲会守卫巢箱，不让同种的其他配对进入。"},{"en":"The term territorial behavior appears in almost every field guide to animal behavior.","cn":"几乎所有动物行为野外指南都会出现 territorial behavior 这一术语。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"拆词记忆 · 非词源","text":"territory（地盘）+ behavior（行为）——把一片地划成自己的，再守住它 → 领地行为","word":"territorial behavior"},"root":"territorial 源自拉丁 terra「土地」，经 territorium「城郊土地」；behavior 源自中古英语 behaven，由 be- 加古英语 habban「持有」构成。合指「守住一片土地的行为」。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses follow one loop: a boundary is claimed, broadcast, enforced, and then read either as a resource defence, a seasonal arrangement, a spacing valve, a human habit or a research unit.","cn":"八个义项沿一个循环展开：先宣称边界，再广播边界、执行边界，随后可读作资源防卫、季节性安排、间距阀门、人类习惯或研究单位。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a line around land, drawn once and then kept by signal and chase.","cn":"核心意象：绕着一片土地画一条线，画定之后靠信号与追赶维持。"},"chain":["CLAIM LAND","MARK THE EDGE","WATCH FOR RIVALS","DRIVE THEM OFF","HOLD THE RESOURCES","SPACE THE GROUP"],"branches":[{"senses":"01 · 02","en":"CLAIM AND ENFORCE: the claim exists only while it is backed by pursuit.","cn":"宣称与执行：宣称只有在追赶的支撑下才存在。"},{"senses":"03","en":"BROADCAST: song and scent make the invisible line public.","cn":"广播：鸣唱与气味把看不见的线变成公开信息。"},{"senses":"04 · 05","en":"WHY HOLD IT: scarce food and a seasonal nest are the reasons a line is worth defending.","cn":"为何守住：稀缺食物与季节性巢址，是这条线值得守的理由。"},{"senses":"06","en":"POPULATION VALVE: many private lines together set the distance between all individuals.","cn":"种群阀门：许多条私人界线合起来，决定了所有个体之间的间距。"},{"senses":"07 · 08","en":"TRANSFER: the same geometry appears in an office desk and in a researcher's tally sheet.","cn":"迁移：同样的几何关系出现在办公桌与研究者的记录表上。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Territorial behavior joins a Latin land-word to an English manner-word; each half keeps its own family, so the phrase is best read in two parts.","cn":"territorial behavior 把一个拉丁土地词与一个英语方式词连在一起；两半各自保留词族，因此最好分两部分读。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Latin terra 'earth' yields territorium and territorialis; the English adjective territorial and the noun territoriality continue that line. Behavior has no Latin cognate and comes from Germanic have.","cn":"拉丁 terra「土地」衍生 territorium 与 territorialis；英语形容词 territorial 与名词 territoriality 延续这条线。behavior 没有拉丁同族词，来自日耳曼语的 have。"},"items":[{"word":"terra","structure":"terra (Latin noun, first declension)","meaning":"earth, dry land","meaningCN":"土地；干地","example":"Terra is the base of territory and terrestrial.","exampleCN":"terra 是 territory 与 terrestrial 的基础。"},{"word":"territorium","structure":"territorium (Latin noun, second declension)","meaning":"land around a town, a district under control","meaningCN":"城郊土地；受管辖的区域","example":"The Roman district gave its name to every later territory.","exampleCN":"罗马的辖区把名字留给了后世每一种 territory。"},{"word":"territorialis","structure":"territorium + -alis (of or belonging to)","meaning":"pertaining to a territory","meaningCN":"属于领地的","example":"The Late Latin adjective passed into French and English.","exampleCN":"这个晚期拉丁形容词经法语进入英语。"},{"word":"territorial","structure":"territorialis + English -al","meaning":"of or relating to a territory","meaningCN":"领地的；领土的","example":"Territorial claims are marked on the map.","exampleCN":"领地主张被标在地图上。"},{"word":"-ial","structure":"-ial (adjective suffix from Latin -alis)","meaning":"relating to, belonging to","meaningCN":"与……有关的；属于……的","example":"The suffix turns a noun of place into an adjective of place.","exampleCN":"这个后缀把表示地点的名词变成表示地点的形容词。"},{"word":"-ity","structure":"-ity (noun suffix from Latin -itas)","meaning":"the state or quality of","meaningCN":"……的状态或性质","example":"Territorial plus -ity names the tendency itself.","exampleCN":"territorial 加 -ity 命名这种倾向本身。"},{"word":"territoriality","structure":"territorial + -ity","meaning":"the state of holding and defending a territory","meaningCN":"占有并防卫领地的状态","example":"Territoriality keeps neighbouring pairs apart.","exampleCN":"领地性使相邻的配对保持距离。"},{"word":"behavior","structure":"behave + -ior (noun of manner)","meaning":"the way a person or animal acts","meaningCN":"人或动物的行为方式","example":"Behavior is what an observer can actually record.","exampleCN":"行为是观察者真正能记录下来的东西。"},{"word":"be-","structure":"be- (Old English verb prefix, 'about, around')","meaning":"around, thoroughly, or making a verb transitive","meaningCN":"围绕、彻底，或使动词及物","example":"Be- turns have into behave, to hold oneself.","exampleCN":"be- 把 have 变成 behave，即「持住自己」。"},{"word":"behavioral","structure":"behavior + -al (relating to)","meaning":"relating to behavior","meaningCN":"与行为有关的","example":"Behavioral ecology studies these boundary patterns.","exampleCN":"行为生态学研究这类边界模式。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"terra","structure":"terra, terrae (f., first declension)","meaning":"earth, land, ground","meaningCN":"土地；大地；地面"},{"word":"territorium","structure":"territorium, territorii (n., second declension)","meaning":"land around a town; a district","meaningCN":"城郊土地；辖区"},{"word":"territorialis","structure":"territorialis, territoriale (adj., third declension)","meaning":"of a territory","meaningCN":"领地的；领土的"}]}},{"word":"social behavior","ipa_uk":"/ˈsəʊʃl bɪˈheɪvjə/","ipa_us":"/ˈsoʊʃl bɪˈheɪvjər/","definition_zh":"社会行为；同种个体彼此影响、彼此回应的行为","definition_en":"the behavior by which members of the same species act on one another and respond to one another","core_image":"两只动物面对面交换信号，一个动作引来另一个动作","scene":"午后草地上，两只幼犬互相追逐，轮流咬住对方的颈毛又松开。The two puppies chase and mouth each other in turn, and ethologists treat this exchange as social behavior.","sceneCN":"这里 social behavior 指「同种个体之间彼此作用的行为」（第 1 个义项：一方的动作引起另一方的回应）；句意为两只幼犬轮流追逐、轻咬，行为学家把这种一来一往视为社会行为。图中可辨识物件：草地、两只幼犬、扬起的尾巴、来回的奔跑路线。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"社会行为（同种个体之间的相互作用；作不可数名词，指具体类型时可有复数）"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"social behavior patterns","zh":"社会行为模式"},{"phrase":"complex social behavior","zh":"复杂的社会行为"},{"phrase":"social behavior of animals","zh":"动物的社会行为"},{"phrase":"human social behavior","zh":"人类的社会行为"},{"phrase":"observe social behavior","zh":"观察社会行为"},{"phrase":"social behavior research","zh":"社会行为研究"}],"forms":[{"label":"复数（不同物种或类型）","form":"social behaviors"},{"label":"相关形容词（社会的）","form":"social"},{"label":"相关形容词（可交际的）","form":"sociable"},{"label":"相关名词（社会性）","form":"sociality"},{"label":"相关名词（行为）","form":"behavior"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"social","pos":"adj.","zh":"社会的；社交的"},{"word":"sociality","pos":"n.","zh":"社会性；群居倾向"},{"word":"sociable","pos":"adj.","zh":"好交际的；合群的"},{"word":"socialize","pos":"v.","zh":"使社会化；交往"},{"word":"behavior","pos":"n.","zh":"行为；举止"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Interaction between members of one species","titleCN":"同种个体之间的相互作用","definition":"actions directed at other members of the same species that invite or provoke a response","definitionCN":"指向同种其他个体、并引起对方回应的动作","example":"The two puppies chase and mouth each other in turn.","exampleCN":"两只幼犬轮流追逐、轻咬对方。","why":"social names the partner, and behavior names the act; together the phrase marks any act whose meaning depends on another individual's response.","whyCN":"social 指明对象是同伴，behavior 指明动作；合起来标记的是「意义取决于对方回应」的动作。"},{"no":"02","title":"Cooperation and mutual aid","titleCN":"合作与互助","definition":"behavior in which individuals work together and share the benefit","definitionCN":"个体共同做事并分享好处的行为","example":"The pair takes turns incubating the eggs so both can feed.","exampleCN":"这一对鸟轮流孵卵，使双方都能外出觅食。","why":"living in a group forces cooperation: one animal's action must fit another's, and the fit itself becomes a recognizable pattern.","whyCN":"群居迫使个体合作：一只动物的动作必须与另一只配合，而这种配合本身成为可辨认的模式。"},{"no":"03","title":"Affiliative behavior: bonding and play","titleCN":"亲近行为：结盟、梳理与玩耍","definition":"behavior that builds and maintains friendly bonds, such as grooming, play and contact","definitionCN":"建立并维持友好关系的动作，如梳理、玩耍与身体接触","example":"Young monkeys groom one another for hours after a quarrel.","exampleCN":"小猴子争吵之后会互相梳理毛发好几个小时。","why":"a group needs more than cooperation; it needs glue, and grooming and play are the visible glue.","whyCN":"群体不只需要合作，还需要黏合剂；梳理与玩耍就是看得见的黏合剂。"},{"no":"04","title":"Agonistic behavior: rivalry and rank","titleCN":"竞争行为：争胜与等级","definition":"behavior used in contests over resources, mates or rank, including threat and submission","definitionCN":"为资源、配偶或等级而竞争的行为，包括威胁与退让","example":"Two stags lower their antlers before either charges.","exampleCN":"两只雄鹿在冲撞之前先低下头角。","why":"the same social channel carries conflict; a threat is still an act aimed at another animal and still waits for its answer.","whyCN":"同一条社会通道也承载冲突；威胁仍然是针对另一只动物的动作，仍然等待对方回答。"},{"no":"05","title":"Communication through signals","titleCN":"通过信号进行交流","definition":"the exchange of calls, displays or scents that carries information between individuals","definitionCN":"个体之间传递信息的叫声、展示或气味交换","example":"A sentinel bird calls and the flock moves into cover.","exampleCN":"一只警戒鸟发出叫声，鸟群随即躲进遮蔽处。","why":"interaction requires a channel; communication is the part of social behavior that carries the message rather than the action itself.","whyCN":"相互作用需要通道；交流是社会行为中传递信息的部分，而非动作本身。"},{"no":"06","title":"Group living and division of labour","titleCN":"群体生活与分工","definition":"the organized behavior of a group, including coordinated movement, sentinels and division of labour","definitionCN":"群体的组织化行为，包括协同移动、警戒与劳动分工","example":"The colony sends foragers out while others guard the entrance.","exampleCN":"蚁群派觅食者外出，另一些则守卫入口。","why":"when many individuals act as one unit, the unit itself has behavior; the phrase scales from two animals to a colony.","whyCN":"当许多个体像一个单位那样行动时，这个单位本身就有行为；短语因此可从两只动物扩大到整个群体。"},{"no":"07","title":"Human social conduct","titleCN":"人际关系中的举止与规范","definition":"the way people act toward others, including politeness, cooperation and social norms","definitionCN":"人对待他人的方式，包括礼貌、合作与社会规范","example":"Guests greet the host before finding a seat.","exampleCN":"客人先向主人问好，再找位置坐下。","why":"people also respond to one another under learned rules, so the term crosses from ethology into sociology without changing its shape.","whyCN":"人也在习得规则之下彼此回应，因此这个术语从动物行为学进入社会学时并未改变形状。"},{"no":"08","title":"A research category","titleCN":"行为研究中的可观察类别","definition":"a class of observable actions recorded in studies of groups, from grooming bouts to chase sequences","definitionCN":"群体研究中记录的一类可观察动作，从梳理时段到追逐序列","example":"The observer scores every grooming bout as social behavior.","exampleCN":"观察者把每个梳理时段记为社会行为。","why":"to compare species or groups, the researcher must cut the stream of action into named units, and this phrase is one such unit.","whyCN":"要比较物种或群体，研究者必须把连续的动作切成有名字的单位，而这个短语就是这样一个单位。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Social comes from Latin socius 'companion' through socialis, while behavior is a native English formation from be- plus have. The phrase is used in both ethology and sociology. Dates are approximate.","cn":"social 经 socialis 源自拉丁 socius「同伴」；behavior 是英语本土构造，由 be- 加 have 构成。这个短语同时用于动物行为学与社会学。年代为约数。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN SOCIUS","en":"Socius meant 'companion, associate, ally'; it named a person one travelled or acted with, not a crowd in general.","cn":"socius 意为「同伴、伙伴、盟友」，指与自己同行或共同行动的人，而不是泛指人群。"},{"era":"LATIN SOCIALIS","en":"Socialis 'of companions, allied' was formed from socius and gave English social through Old French.","cn":"socialis 意为「同伴的、结盟的」，由 socius 构成，经古法语进入英语成为 social。"},{"era":"OLD ENGLISH AND MIDDLE ENGLISH BEHAVE","en":"Behavior derives from behave, Middle English be- plus have (Old English habban 'to hold'); the noun first meant a manner of bearing oneself.","cn":"behavior 来自 behave，即中古英语 be- 加 have（古英语 habban「持有」）；名词最初指持守自己的方式。"},{"era":"TWENTIETH-CENTURY SCIENCES","en":"Social behavior became a shared term in sociology and in animal behavior studies in the twentieth century, where it covers everything from grooming to group defence.","cn":"20 世纪，social behavior 成为社会学与动物行为学的共用术语，涵盖从梳理到群体防卫的各种动作。"},{"era":"UNCERTAIN DETAILS","en":"Source uncertain (first dates): the earliest use of the compound in either discipline is not precisely dated, and the line between social and merely gregarious behavior is drawn differently by different authors.","cn":"来源不确定（首见年代）：这一复合词在两个学科中的最早用法都没有精确年代；不同作者对「社会行为」与「仅仅群聚」的界线划分不一。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"Group one holds words built on the same social stem; group two holds neighboring concepts that are often used as if they were synonyms.","cn":"第一组是同一 social 词干构成的词；第二组是常被当作同义词使用的邻近概念。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"social","ipa":"/ˈsəʊʃl/","tag":"adjective, not the acts","definition":"Relating to society or companionship; it describes the setting, while social behavior names what is actually done.","definitionCN":"意为「社会的、社交的」；描述场景，而 social behavior 才指实际做出的动作。"},{"word":"sociable","ipa":"/səʊˈsiːəbl/","tag":"friendly disposition","definition":"Fond of company and easy in conversation; it describes a temperament, not a recorded pattern of action.","definitionCN":"喜欢与人相处、谈吐自在；描述性情，而非被记录的动作模式。"},{"word":"sociality","ipa":"/səʊʃiˈæləti/","tag":"the abstract property","definition":"The degree to which a species lives in groups; it is a property of a species, not a single observable act.","definitionCN":"一个物种群居的程度；是物种的属性，而非单个可观察的动作。"},{"word":"societal","ipa":"/səˈsaɪətl/","tag":"whole-society adjective","definition":"Relating to society as a whole, as in societal change; it does not describe individual interaction.","definitionCN":"意为「整个社会的」，如社会变迁；不描述个体之间的互动。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"social interaction","ipa":"/ˈsəʊʃl ɪnˈtærækʃn/","tag":"the exchange itself","definition":"A single episode of mutual action; social behavior is the broader class of such episodes and their patterns.","definitionCN":"一次相互作用的片段；social behavior 是这类片段及其模式的更大类别。"},{"word":"communication","ipa":"/ˌkɒmjuːnɪˈkeɪʃn/","tag":"the channel","definition":"The transfer of information by signals; it is one component of social behavior, not its whole span.","definitionCN":"通过信号传递信息；是社会行为的一个组成部分，而非全部。"},{"word":"group behavior","ipa":"/ɡruːp bɪˈheɪvjə/","tag":"the collective level","definition":"The behavior of a whole group as a unit; social behavior can also describe two individuals.","definitionCN":"整个群体作为一个单位的行为；social behavior 也可以只描述两个个体。"},{"word":"solitary behavior","ipa":"/ˈsɒlətri bɪˈheɪvjə/","tag":"the opposite","definition":"Action carried out alone, without response from others; it is the contrast case that defines the social one.","definitionCN":"独自完成、没有他人回应的动作；它是对照项，用来界定社会行为。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Normal associations: real morphemes, real collocations and real relatives, not invented rhymes.","cn":"正常联想：真实的构词成分、真实搭配与真实同族词，而非编造的顺口溜。"},"normal":[{"en":"socius 'companion' gives socialis and social; social behavior is literally the behavior of companions.","cn":"socius「同伴」构成 socialis 与 social；social behavior 字面上就是「同伴之间的行为」。"},{"en":"The family runs social, sociable, sociality, socialize and societal.","cn":"同族词包括 social、sociable、sociality、socialize 与 societal。"},{"en":"Fixed phrases mark the field: grooming, play, threat, sentinel call, division of labour.","cn":"固定说法标出领域：梳理、玩耍、威胁、警戒叫声、劳动分工。"},{"en":"Ask two questions: is another individual involved, and does the act depend on that individual's response?","cn":"问两个问题：是否涉及另一个个体？这个动作是否取决于对方的回应？"},{"en":"Social behavior is studied at two scales: the pair and the group.","cn":"社会行为在两个尺度上研究：一对个体与整个群体。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture two dancers who must each read the other's weight before moving.","cn":"想象两个舞者，每次移动前都要读懂对方的重心。"},{"en":"Picture a flock turning as one body because each bird watches its neighbour.","cn":"想象鸟群像一个身体那样转向，因为每只鸟都在看邻居。"},{"en":"Picture a room where every greeting is an answer to the greeting before it.","cn":"想象一个房间，每声问候都是对前一声问候的回答。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"Grooming is the most reliable measure of social behavior in many primates.","cn":"梳理在许多灵长类中是衡量社会行为最可靠的指标。"},{"en":"Play teaches young animals the rules they will need in a group.","cn":"玩耍让幼兽学会群体中将要用到的规则。"},{"en":"A sentinel's call changes the whole flock's behavior within seconds.","cn":"警戒鸟的一声叫能在几秒内改变整群鸟的行为。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"拆词记忆 · 非词源","text":"social（同伴的）+ behavior（行为）——同伴之间你来我往的动作 → 社会行为","word":"social behavior"},"root":"social 源自拉丁 socius「同伴」，经 socialis 进入英语；behavior 源自中古英语 behaven，由 be- 加古英语 habban「持有」构成。合指「同伴之间相互作用的行为」。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses move outward from one exchange: two individuals respond, then cooperate, bond, compete, signal, form a group, follow human rules, and finally become a unit in a researcher's notebook.","cn":"八个义项从一次交换向外扩展：两个个体回应、合作、结盟、竞争、传信号、组成群体、遵循人的规范，最后成为研究者笔记里的一个单位。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: action aimed at another, answered by that other, so the loop closes.","cn":"核心意象：指向另一个个体的动作，被对方回应，于是闭环成立。"},"chain":["ONE ACTS","THE OTHER ANSWERS","THEY COOPERATE","THEY BOND","THEY CONTEST","THE GROUP ACTS"],"branches":[{"senses":"01","en":"THE LOOP: a social act is defined by the reply it expects.","cn":"闭环：社会动作由它所期待的回应来定义。"},{"senses":"02 · 03","en":"GLUE: cooperation and grooming hold the pair together in two different ways.","cn":"黏合：合作与梳理以两种不同方式把一对个体维系在一起。"},{"senses":"04 · 05","en":"TENSION AND SIGNAL: rivalry and communication are the same channel under different loads.","cn":"张力与信号：竞争与交流是同一条通道在不同负荷下的状态。"},{"senses":"06","en":"SCALE: when the loop repeats many times, a group acquires behavior of its own.","cn":"尺度：当闭环多次重复，群体便获得属于自己的行为。"},{"senses":"07 · 08","en":"TWO READINGS: the same acts can be judged as conduct or counted as data.","cn":"两种读法：同样的动作既可被评判为举止，也可被计为数据。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Social behavior joins a Latin companionship word to an English manner-word; the social half carries the borrowed family, the behavior half the native one.","cn":"social behavior 把一个拉丁「同伴」词与一个英语「方式」词连起来；social 一半承载借词族，behavior 一半承载本族词。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Latin socius 'companion' yields socialis and societas; English draws social, sociable, sociality and societal from that line. Behavior is Germanic and has no Latin cognate.","cn":"拉丁 socius「同伴」衍生 socialis 与 societas；英语由此得到 social、sociable、sociality 与 societal。behavior 属日耳曼语，没有拉丁同族词。"},"items":[{"word":"socius","structure":"socius (Latin noun, second declension)","meaning":"companion, ally, associate","meaningCN":"同伴；盟友；伙伴","example":"Socius named the person one acted with.","exampleCN":"socius 指与自己共同行动的人。"},{"word":"socialis","structure":"socius + -alis (belonging to)","meaning":"of companions, allied","meaningCN":"同伴的；结盟的","example":"Socialis is the direct source of English social.","exampleCN":"socialis 是英语 social 的直接来源。"},{"word":"societas","structure":"socius + -tas (state, body)","meaning":"fellowship, association, company","meaningCN":"伙伴关系；社团；团体","example":"Societas survives in the word society.","exampleCN":"societas 留在 society 一词中。"},{"word":"social","structure":"socialis through Old French social","meaning":"relating to companions or society","meaningCN":"与同伴或社会有关的","example":"Social insects live in organized groups.","exampleCN":"社会性昆虫生活在有组织的群体中。"},{"word":"-ity","structure":"-ity (noun suffix from Latin -itas)","meaning":"the state or quality of","meaningCN":"……的状态或性质","example":"Social plus -ity gives sociality.","exampleCN":"social 加 -ity 得到 sociality。"},{"word":"sociality","structure":"social + -ity","meaning":"the quality of living in groups","meaningCN":"群居的性质","example":"Sociality varies widely among mammals.","exampleCN":"哺乳动物的社会性差异很大。"},{"word":"behavior","structure":"behave + -ior (noun of manner)","meaning":"a way of acting","meaningCN":"行为方式","example":"Behavior is the observable side of social life.","exampleCN":"行为是社会生活中可观察的一面。"},{"word":"be-","structure":"be- (Old English verb prefix)","meaning":"about, around; makes a verb transitive","meaningCN":"围绕；使动词及物","example":"Be- plus have yields behave.","exampleCN":"be- 加 have 构成 behave。"},{"word":"behavioral","structure":"behavior + -al (relating to)","meaning":"relating to behavior","meaningCN":"与行为有关的","example":"Behavioral studies count grooming bouts.","exampleCN":"行为研究会计数梳理时段。"},{"word":"sociable","structure":"social + -able (capable of, inclined to)","meaning":"inclined to be with others","meaningCN":"喜欢与他人相处的","example":"A sociable animal seeks company.","exampleCN":"合群的动物会主动寻找同伴。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"socius","structure":"socius, socii (m., second declension)","meaning":"companion, ally","meaningCN":"同伴；盟友"},{"word":"socialis","structure":"socialis, sociale (adj., third declension)","meaning":"of companions; allied","meaningCN":"同伴的；结盟的"},{"word":"societas","structure":"societas, societatis (f., third declension)","meaning":"fellowship; association","meaningCN":"伙伴关系；社团"},{"word":"sociare","structure":"sociare, sociavi, sociatum (verb, first conjugation)","meaning":"to join, unite, associate","meaningCN":"联结；联合；结交"}]}},{"word":"cooperation","ipa_uk":"/kəʊˌɒpəˈreɪʃn/","ipa_us":"/koʊˌɑːpəˈreɪʃn/","definition_zh":"合作；为共同目标一起行动，也指愿意配合他人的态度","definition_en":"the act of working together toward a shared goal, or the willingness to help when asked","core_image":"两个人各抬一端，把同一件重物搬到同一处","scene":"实验室里，两名研究人员一人扶住支架、一人拧紧螺丝，几分钟就把装置装好。One researcher steadies the frame while the other tightens the bolts, and the job is finished through cooperation.","sceneCN":"这里 cooperation 指「为共同目标一起行动」（第 1 个义项：各方分担同一任务的不同部分）；句意为一名研究者扶住支架、另一名拧紧螺丝，装置靠合作很快装好。图中可辨识物件：支架、螺丝、两只手、装配好的装置。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"合作；协作；配合（不可数；具体合作项目可用复数）"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"close cooperation","zh":"紧密合作"},{"phrase":"international cooperation","zh":"国际合作"},{"phrase":"in cooperation with","zh":"与……合作"},{"phrase":"full cooperation","zh":"全力配合"},{"phrase":"economic cooperation","zh":"经济合作"},{"phrase":"a cooperation agreement","zh":"合作协议"}],"forms":[{"label":"复数（具体的合作项目）","form":"cooperations"},{"label":"动词","form":"cooperate"},{"label":"现在分词","form":"cooperating"},{"label":"过去式","form":"cooperated"},{"label":"形容词","form":"cooperative"},{"label":"副词","form":"cooperatively"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"cooperate","pos":"v.","zh":"合作；配合"},{"word":"cooperative","pos":"adj./n.","zh":"合作的；合作社"},{"word":"cooperatively","pos":"adv.","zh":"合作地"},{"word":"cooperator","pos":"n.","zh":"合作者；协作者"},{"word":"cooperativeness","pos":"n.","zh":"合作意愿；配合性"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Working together toward one goal","titleCN":"为共同目标一起行动","definition":"the act of working with others toward a shared aim","definitionCN":"与他人一起为共同目标做事","example":"One researcher steadies the frame while the other tightens the bolts.","exampleCN":"一名研究者扶住支架，另一名拧紧螺丝。","why":"co- 'together' plus operari 'to work' says exactly what the word does: two or more agents put their work into one result.","whyCN":"co-「一起」加 operari「做事」，正好说出这个词的动作：两个或更多行动者把自己的劳动放进同一个结果。"},{"no":"02","title":"Willingness to help when asked","titleCN":"被请求时愿意配合","definition":"the readiness to assist someone who asks for help or permission","definitionCN":"愿意帮助提出请求或需要许可的人","example":"Thank you for your cooperation during the inspection.","exampleCN":"感谢您在检查期间的配合。","why":"the same word names the attitude behind joint work; a request for cooperation asks for access and effort rather than a formal partnership.","whyCN":"同一个词也指共同做事背后的态度；请求 cooperation 要的是配合与便利，而不是正式合伙关系。"},{"no":"03","title":"Mutual aid in nature","titleCN":"自然界的互利互助","definition":"behavior in which organisms act together in ways that benefit both partners","definitionCN":"生物共同行动、双方都获益的行为","example":"Ants and acacia trees cooperate: shelter for defence.","exampleCN":"蚂蚁与金合欢合作：住所换防卫。","why":"biology borrowed the word because two species can also divide a job, and the shared benefit is measurable in survival and offspring.","whyCN":"生物学借用了这个词，因为两个物种也能分担同一件事，而共同收益可以用存活与后代来衡量。"},{"no":"04","title":"Partnership between organizations","titleCN":"机构之间的协作","definition":"joint work between institutions, departments or agencies that keep their own identities","definitionCN":"保持各自身份的机构、部门或机关之间的共同工作","example":"The museum works in cooperation with the local school.","exampleCN":"博物馆与当地学校合作。","why":"organizations cooperate rather than merge; each keeps its boundary but contributes a part, which is why the phrase in cooperation with is so common.","whyCN":"机构是合作而不是合并；各方保留边界却各出一部分，因此「与……合作」这一说法极为常见。"},{"no":"05","title":"International and economic cooperation","titleCN":"国际与经贸合作","definition":"coordinated action between countries or firms on trade, aid, research or security","definitionCN":"国家或企业在贸易、援助、研究或安全上的协调行动","example":"The two countries signed a cooperation agreement on clean energy.","exampleCN":"两国签署了一项清洁能源合作协议。","why":"the modern political sense scales the same division of labour up to states, where no one can compel the other and agreement must be negotiated.","whyCN":"现代政治义把同一种分工放大到国家层面：任何一方都无法强迫对方，合作必须通过协商达成。"},{"no":"06","title":"Coordination of parts in a system","titleCN":"系统各部分的协同","definition":"the way parts of a body, machine or system work together so that the whole functions","definitionCN":"身体、机器或系统的各部分协同运作，使整体发挥功能","example":"Walking depends on the cooperation of muscles and joints.","exampleCN":"行走依赖肌肉与关节的协同。","why":"once the word leaves people, it can describe any set of parts whose combined action produces an effect none could produce alone.","whyCN":"一旦离开人，这个词就能描述任何一组部件：它们的联合动作产生单个部件无法产生的效果。"},{"no":"07","title":"Compliance with authority","titleCN":"对执法或管理方的配合","definition":"the act of following instructions or allowing an official procedure to proceed","definitionCN":"遵从指示或允许官方程序顺利进行","example":"The driver's cooperation helped the officers clear the road.","exampleCN":"司机的配合帮助警员清理了道路。","why":"cooperation here is one-sided compliance; the word softens a demand by presenting it as shared work.","whyCN":"这里的 cooperation 是单方面的顺从；这个词把一项要求说成共同工作，从而缓和了语气。"},{"no":"08","title":"A cooperative strategy in game theory","titleCN":"博弈论中的合作策略","definition":"a strategy in which players choose actions that raise the joint outcome instead of competing for the larger share","definitionCN":"参与者选择提高联合收益、而非争夺更大份额的策略","example":"In the repeated game, cooperation pays only if the other side also keeps its promise.","exampleCN":"在重复博弈中，只有当对方也守约时，合作才划算。","why":"game theory makes the word technical: cooperation is not goodwill but a strategy that survives only under conditions of repeated contact and observable behaviour.","whyCN":"博弈论把这个词技术化：合作不是善意，而是在重复接触与可观察行为条件下才存活的策略。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Cooperation comes from Late Latin cooperari, built on com- 'together' and operari 'to work', itself from opus 'work'. It reached English through French. Dates are approximate.","cn":"cooperation 来自晚期拉丁 cooperari，由 com-「一起」与 operari「做事」构成，而 operari 又源自 opus「工作」。它经法语进入英语。年代为约数。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN OPUS","en":"Opus meant 'work, a piece of work'; its stem oper- supplies the verb operari 'to work, labour'.","cn":"opus 意为「工作、一件作品」；其词干 oper- 构成动词 operari「做事、劳作」。"},{"era":"LATE LATIN COOPERARI","en":"Cooperari combined com- 'together' with operari, meaning 'to work together, collaborate'. The prefix assimilated to co- before the vowel.","cn":"cooperari 把 com-「一起」与 operari 组合，意为「共同做事、协作」；前缀在元音前同化为 co-。"},{"era":"FRENCH AND ENGLISH","en":"French coopération carried the noun into English in the sixteenth or seventeenth century; cooperate followed in the same period.","cn":"法语 coopération 在 16 或 17 世纪把名词带入英语；动词 cooperate 也在同一时期进入。"},{"era":"MODERN EXTENSIONS","en":"The economic and international senses date mainly from the nineteenth and twentieth centuries, when firms, unions and states began to sign standing agreements.","cn":"经济与国际义主要形成于 19 与 20 世纪，当时公司、工会与国家开始签订长期协议。"},{"era":"UNCERTAIN DETAILS","en":"Source uncertain (first dates): the earliest English citation of cooperation is not firmly fixed, and dictionaries differ on whether the noun came straight from Latin or through French.","cn":"来源不确定（首见年代）：cooperation 在英语中的最早书证没有确切年代；词典对名词是直接来自拉丁还是经法语而来也有分歧。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"Group one holds forms from the same co- plus oper- family; group two holds words that also describe joint work but differ in emphasis.","cn":"第一组是同一 co- 加 oper- 词族的词；第二组同样描述共同工作，但侧重不同。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"cooperative","ipa":"/kəʊˈɒpərətɪv/","tag":"adjective or organization","definition":"Willing to help, or a member-owned business; it describes a quality or an entity, not the activity itself.","definitionCN":"愿意配合的，或成员共有的企业；描述性质或实体，而非活动本身。"},{"word":"operate","ipa":"/ˈɒpəreɪt/","tag":"same root, no co-","definition":"To run or work a machine or system; without co- there is no second agent.","definitionCN":"操作机器或运行系统；没有 co- 就没有第二个行动者。"},{"word":"operation","ipa":"/ˌɒpəˈreɪʃn/","tag":"one agent's work","definition":"The act of running something, or a surgical procedure; it does not require a partner.","definitionCN":"运行某物，或外科手术；不需要伙伴。"},{"word":"co-owner","ipa":"/ˌkəʊˈəʊnə/","tag":"co- but not oper-","definition":"A joint owner; the prefix is the same, but the root is own, not work.","definitionCN":"共同所有人；前缀相同，但词根是 own（拥有），而非 work（工作）。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"collaboration","ipa":"/ˌkɒləˈreɪʃn/","tag":"shared creation","definition":"Working jointly, especially on a creative or intellectual project; it stresses the shared product more than the shared labour.","definitionCN":"共同工作，尤指创意或学术项目；更强调共同成果而非共同劳动。"},{"word":"coordination","ipa":"/ˌkɔːdɪˈneɪʃn/","tag":"timing and fit","definition":"Organizing separate efforts so that they fit together; cooperation supplies the will, coordination the schedule.","definitionCN":"把各自的努力组织到合适的位置；cooperation 提供意愿，coordination 提供时序。"},{"word":"teamwork","ipa":"/ˈtiːmwɜːk/","tag":"the everyday word","definition":"The combined effort of a team; it is warmer and less formal than cooperation.","definitionCN":"团队的合力；比 cooperation 更口语、更亲切。"},{"word":"mutualism","ipa":"/mjuːˈtjuːəlɪzəm/","tag":"the biological term","definition":"A biological relationship in which both species benefit; the technical name for cooperation across species.","definitionCN":"两个物种都获益的生物学关系；是跨物种合作的技术名称。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Normal associations: real morphemes, real collocations and real relatives, not invented rhymes.","cn":"正常联想：真实的构词成分、真实搭配与真实同族词，而非编造的顺口溜。"},"normal":[{"en":"co- 'together' + operari 'work' = work together; the same root appears in operate and opera.","cn":"co-「一起」+ operari「做事」= 共同做事；同一词根也出现在 operate 与 opera 中。"},{"en":"The family runs cooperate, cooperative, cooperation, cooperator and cooperatively.","cn":"同族词包括 cooperate、cooperative、cooperation、cooperator 与 cooperatively。"},{"en":"Fixed phrases mark the senses: close cooperation, international cooperation, in cooperation with, full cooperation.","cn":"固定搭配标出各义项：紧密合作、国际合作、与……合作、全力配合。"},{"en":"The preposition matters: in cooperation with means two parties, while with the cooperation of means one party assisting another.","cn":"介词很关键：说「与……合作」时指双方，说「在某方的配合下」时指一方协助另一方。"},{"en":"Biology has its own word, mutualism, for cooperation between species.","cn":"生物学有专门术语「互利共生」指物种之间的合作。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture two people carrying one heavy table, each holding a different end.","cn":"想象两个人抬一张重桌，各自抓住不同的一端。"},{"en":"Picture a rowing crew whose oars enter the water on the same beat.","cn":"想象赛艇队员的桨在同一拍入水。"},{"en":"Picture a machine whose parts each do one motion so that the whole moves.","cn":"想象一台机器，每个部件各做一个动作，整体才动起来。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The project succeeded through close cooperation between the two labs.","cn":"这个项目靠两个实验室的紧密合作而成功。"},{"en":"Police thanked the public for its cooperation during the search.","cn":"警方感谢公众在搜寻期间的配合。"},{"en":"Clean-energy cooperation between the two countries began in the 1990s.","cn":"两国的清洁能源合作始于 20 世纪 90 年代。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"拆词记忆 · 非词源","text":"co（一起）+ operation（操作）——几个人一起操作同一件事 → 合作","word":"cooperation"},"root":"拉丁晚期 cooperari「共同做事」= com-（一起）+ operari「工作」（源自 opus「工作」）。英语经法语借入。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses keep the same division of labour but change the setting: a task, a request, a species pair, two institutions, two states, a body's parts, an authority, a game.","cn":"八个义项保持同一种分工，只更换场景：一项任务、一次请求、一对物种、两个机构、两个国家、身体各部、一个执法方、一场博弈。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: one load, two pairs of hands, each taking a different end.","cn":"核心意象：一件重物，两双手，各自抬住不同的一端。"},"chain":["SHARED GOAL","DIVIDE THE WORK","ACT IN STEP","HELP ON REQUEST","POOL RESOURCES","SHARED RESULT"],"branches":[{"senses":"01","en":"THE CORE: a shared aim is what turns separate efforts into one act.","cn":"核心：共同目标把分散的努力变成同一个动作。"},{"senses":"02","en":"THE ATTITUDE: willingness is the door through which help enters.","cn":"态度：意愿是帮助得以进入的那道门。"},{"senses":"03","en":"ACROSS SPECIES: biology measures the shared benefit in survival.","cn":"跨物种：生物学用存活来衡量共同收益。"},{"senses":"04 · 05","en":"ACROSS BORDERS: institutions and states cooperate without merging.","cn":"跨越边界：机构与国家合作而不合并。"},{"senses":"06 · 07 · 08","en":"OTHER SHAPES: parts, compliance and strategy all keep the same division of labour.","cn":"其他形态：部件、顺从与策略都保持同一种分工。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Cooperation is a prefix-root noun: co- 'together' plus operari 'to work' plus -ation. The same root family runs through operate, operation and opera.","cn":"cooperation 是前缀加词根的名词：co-「一起」加 operari「做事」，再加 -ation。同一词根族贯穿 operate、operation 与 opera。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Latin opus 'work' gives operari and, with com-, cooperari; English takes cooperate, cooperation, cooperative and cooperator from this line.","cn":"拉丁 opus「工作」生成 operari，并与 com- 合成 cooperari；英语由此得到 cooperate、cooperation、cooperative 与 cooperator。"},"items":[{"word":"com- / co-","structure":"com- (Latin prefix, 'together, with')","meaning":"together, jointly","meaningCN":"一起；共同","example":"Before a vowel the prefix shortens to co-.","exampleCN":"在元音前这个前缀缩为 co-。"},{"word":"opus","structure":"opus, operis (Latin noun, third declension)","meaning":"work, labour, a work","meaningCN":"工作；劳作；作品","example":"Opus is the noun behind the whole family.","exampleCN":"opus 是整个词族背后的名词。"},{"word":"operari","structure":"operari, operatus sum (Latin deponent verb)","meaning":"to work, labour, perform","meaningCN":"工作；劳作；执行","example":"Operari supplies the verbal idea of labour.","exampleCN":"operari 提供「劳作」的动词含义。"},{"word":"cooperari","structure":"co- + operari","meaning":"to work together","meaningCN":"共同做事","example":"The Late Latin verb named joint labour.","exampleCN":"这个晚期拉丁动词命名共同劳动。"},{"word":"-ation","structure":"-ation (noun suffix from Latin -atio)","meaning":"the act or process of","meaningCN":"……的动作或过程","example":"Cooperari plus -ation names the activity.","exampleCN":"cooperari 加 -ation 命名这项活动。"},{"word":"cooperation","structure":"cooperari + -ation","meaning":"the act of working together","meaningCN":"共同做事的行为","example":"Cooperation requires a shared aim.","exampleCN":"合作需要一个共同目标。"},{"word":"cooperate","structure":"co- + operari (English verb)","meaning":"to work together with others","meaningCN":"与他人一起工作","example":"The two teams agreed to cooperate.","exampleCN":"两个团队同意合作。"},{"word":"cooperative","structure":"cooperat- + -ive (tending to)","meaning":"tending to work together; a jointly owned business","meaningCN":"倾向于合作的；共同所有的企业","example":"A cooperative shop is owned by its members.","exampleCN":"合作社商店由成员共有。"},{"word":"cooperator","structure":"cooperat- + -or (one who)","meaning":"a person who cooperates","meaningCN":"合作者","example":"Every cooperator received a share of the harvest.","exampleCN":"每位合作者都分到了一份收成。"},{"word":"operate","structure":"operari + English -ate","meaning":"to work, run or perform an operation","meaningCN":"运作；操作；施行","example":"She operates the machine alone.","exampleCN":"她独自操作这台机器。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"opus","structure":"opus, operis (n., third declension)","meaning":"work, labour","meaningCN":"工作；劳作"},{"word":"operari","structure":"operari, operatus sum (deponent verb, first conjugation)","meaning":"to work, labour","meaningCN":"工作；劳作"},{"word":"cooperari","structure":"co- + operari (deponent verb, first conjugation)","meaning":"to work together","meaningCN":"共同做事"},{"word":"cooperatio","structure":"cooperatio, cooperationis (f., third declension)","meaning":"a working together","meaningCN":"共同劳作"}]}},{"word":"cooperative","ipa_uk":"/kəʊˈɒpərətɪv/","ipa_us":"/koʊˈɑːpərətɪv/","definition_zh":"合作的；愿意配合的；合作社（成员共有、共同经营的组织或场所）","definition_en":"willing to work with others, involving joint effort, or a business owned and run by its members","core_image":"几位成员围坐一圈，各出一份力，也各分一份收益","scene":"小区门口，住户们轮流值守新开的共享菜园，收成按工时分配。Neighbours take turns tending the shared garden and divide the harvest by hours worked, an arrangement they describe as cooperative.","sceneCN":"这里 cooperative 指「成员共同出力、共同分享的」（第 2 个义项：合作式的安排）；句意为住户轮流照看共享菜园、按工时分配收成，他们把这种安排称作合作式的。图中可辨识物件：菜园、值班表、收成筐、按工时记录的本子。","pos":[{"tag":"adj.","zh":"合作的；愿意配合的；合作性质的"},{"tag":"n.","zh":"合作社；合作商店；合作公寓"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"a cooperative agreement","zh":"合作协议"},{"phrase":"a cooperative society","zh":"合作社团"},{"phrase":"cooperative learning","zh":"合作学习"},{"phrase":"cooperative breeding","zh":"合作育幼"},{"phrase":"a cooperative bank","zh":"合作银行"},{"phrase":"be cooperative with","zh":"对……予以配合"}],"forms":[{"label":"比较级","form":"more cooperative"},{"label":"最高级","form":"most cooperative"},{"label":"复数（合作社）","form":"cooperatives"},{"label":"副词","form":"cooperatively"},{"label":"名词（合作）","form":"cooperation"},{"label":"动词","form":"cooperate"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"cooperate","pos":"v.","zh":"合作；配合"},{"word":"cooperation","pos":"n.","zh":"合作；协作"},{"word":"cooperatively","pos":"adv.","zh":"合作地"},{"word":"cooperativeness","pos":"n.","zh":"合作意愿；配合性"},{"word":"co-op","pos":"n.","zh":"合作社；合作公寓（口语缩略）"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Willing to help or agree","titleCN":"愿意配合的","definition":"willing to do what is asked and to work with others without resistance","definitionCN":"愿意按要求做事、与他人配合而不抵触","example":"The witness was cooperative and answered every question.","exampleCN":"证人很配合，回答了每一个问题。","why":"the adjective turns joint work into a personal disposition: a cooperative person is one whose work can be joined to yours.","whyCN":"这个形容词把共同工作变成个人性情：配合的人，其劳动能与你的劳动接上。"},{"no":"02","title":"Done by sharing the work","titleCN":"由共同分担完成的","definition":"describing an activity or arrangement in which several people share the effort","definitionCN":"描述由若干人分担努力的活动或安排","example":"Neighbours tend the shared garden in a cooperative arrangement.","exampleCN":"邻居们以合作的方式共同照看菜园。","why":"here the word modifies the arrangement rather than the person; the sharing is built into the structure, not into anyone's mood.","whyCN":"这里修饰的是安排而非人；共享被写进结构里，而不取决于谁的心情。"},{"no":"03","title":"A member-owned business","titleCN":"成员共有的合作社","definition":"a business owned and run by its members, who share the profits","definitionCN":"由成员共有共营并分享利润的企业","example":"The farmers sell milk through a local cooperative.","exampleCN":"农民通过当地合作社出售牛奶。","why":"the nineteenth-century cooperative movement turned the adjective into a noun: an enterprise whose ownership is itself the joint work.","whyCN":"19 世纪的合作社运动把这个形容词变成名词：一种所有权本身就是共同劳动的企业。"},{"no":"04","title":"A jointly owned apartment building","titleCN":"共同产权公寓","definition":"a building owned jointly by its residents, who share costs and decisions","definitionCN":"由住户共同拥有、共同承担费用与决策的住宅","example":"They bought a two-bedroom cooperative in the old town.","exampleCN":"他们在老城买了一套两居室的合作公寓。","why":"housing repeats the same structure as a shop: many owners, one property, shared rules. In speech it shortens to co-op.","whyCN":"住房重复了商店的同一种结构：多个业主、一处房产、共享规则；口语中缩为「合作公寓」的简称。"},{"no":"05","title":"Cooperative breeding in animals","titleCN":"动物的合作育幼","definition":"a system in which individuals other than the parents help raise the young","definitionCN":"由父母以外的个体帮助抚养幼崽的体系","example":"In cooperative breeding, older offspring feed their younger siblings.","exampleCN":"在合作育幼中，较大的后代喂养更小的弟妹。","why":"biology applies the adjective to a reproductive system, where help is measurable as extra surviving young.","whyCN":"生物学把这个形容词用于繁殖体系，其中的帮助可用多存活的幼崽来衡量。"},{"no":"06","title":"Cooperative learning in class","titleCN":"课堂合作学习","definition":"an instructional method in which students work in small groups on a shared task","definitionCN":"学生在小组中共同完成一项任务的教学方法","example":"The teacher sets a cooperative learning task for mixed pairs.","exampleCN":"老师给混合搭配的小组布置合作学习任务。","why":"education borrowed the word for structured sharing: the group is arranged so that each member must contribute a part.","whyCN":"教育学借用这个词来指有结构的共享：小组被安排成每个成员都必须贡献一部分。"},{"no":"07","title":"A cooperative patient or subject","titleCN":"配合治疗的病人或受试者","definition":"a person who follows instructions during treatment or an experiment","definitionCN":"在治疗或实验中遵从指示的人","example":"The nurse noted that the patient was calm and cooperative.","exampleCN":"护士记录病人平静且配合。","why":"clinical use narrows the word to compliance: the patient's work is to accept the procedure without obstructing it.","whyCN":"临床用法把词义收窄为顺从：病人的「工作」就是不阻碍地接受程序。"},{"no":"08","title":"The shortened form co-op","titleCN":"口语缩略形式：合作社的简称","definition":"the informal short form for a cooperative shop, farm or apartment","definitionCN":"合作社商店、合作农场或合作公寓的口语简称","example":"She picks up vegetables at the co-op every Friday.","exampleCN":"她每周五在合作社买蔬菜。","why":"frequent use wears the long word down; co-op keeps the first and last pieces and drops the middle.","whyCN":"高频使用让长词变短；缩略形式保留头尾、丢掉中间。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Cooperative is built from cooperari 'to work together' plus the adjective suffix -ive. The noun sense grew out of nineteenth-century cooperative societies. Dates are approximate.","cn":"cooperative 由 cooperari「共同做事」加形容词后缀 -ive 构成。名词义从 19 世纪的合作社团发展而来。年代为约数。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN COOPERARI","en":"Cooperari 'to work together' joins com- 'together' to operari 'to work', from opus 'work'.","cn":"cooperari「共同做事」把 com-「一起」与 operari「做事」结合，后者源自 opus「工作」。"},{"era":"LATE LATIN COOPERATIVUS","en":"Late Latin cooperativus 'tending to work together' added -ivus to the participial stem; English took the adjective in the seventeenth century.","cn":"晚期拉丁 cooperativus 意为「倾向于共同做事的」，在分词词干后加 -ivus；英语在 17 世纪借入该形容词。"},{"era":"NINETEENTH-CENTURY MOVEMENT","en":"From the 1820s onward cooperative societies spread in Britain and Europe, and the adjective became a noun for the shop or farm itself.","cn":"从 19 世纪 20 年代起，合作社团在英国与欧洲传播，这个形容词逐渐变成指商店或农场本身的名词。"},{"era":"TWENTIETH-CENTURY USES","en":"Cooperative learning, cooperative breeding and cooperative housing are all twentieth-century extensions of the same idea of shared effort.","cn":"合作学习、合作育幼与合作住房都是 20 世纪对「共同出力」这一相同观念的延伸。"},{"era":"UNCERTAIN DETAILS","en":"Source uncertain (first dates): the exact date of the first noun use in English is not agreed, and the older cooperative society is often dated only by its first recorded rulebook.","cn":"来源不确定（首见年代）：英语中名词义的最早年代没有定论；较早的「合作会社」这一说法常只能按最早留存的章程年代推定。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"Group one holds words that look close to cooperative; group two holds near-synonyms with different grammar or emphasis.","cn":"第一组是外形接近 cooperative 的词；第二组是语法或侧重不同的近义词。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"cooperation","ipa":"/kəʊˌɒpəˈreɪʃn/","tag":"noun of the act","definition":"The activity of working together; cooperative is the adjective or the organization, not the activity.","definitionCN":"共同做事的活动；cooperative 是形容词或组织，不是活动本身。"},{"word":"operate","ipa":"/ˈɒpəreɪt/","tag":"verb without co-","definition":"To run a machine or carry out a procedure; there is no second agent in the word.","definitionCN":"操作机器或施行程序；词中没有第二个行动者。"},{"word":"operative","ipa":"/ˈɒpərətɪv/","tag":"one letter different","definition":"Functioning or effective, as in the operative clause; it comes from the same root but means 'working', not 'working together'.","definitionCN":"运作的、有效的，如生效条款；同词根，但意为「在运作」，不是「一起运作」。"},{"word":"co-op","ipa":"/ˈkəʊɒp/","tag":"clipping","definition":"The spoken short form of cooperative; it is the same entity with its middle syllables cut away.","definitionCN":"cooperative 的口语缩略；指同一实体，只是中间音节被省掉。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"collaborative","ipa":"/kəˈlæbərətɪv/","tag":"joint creation","definition":"Describing work shared on a project, often intellectual; it stresses the shared product rather than a willingness to obey.","definitionCN":"描述项目上的共同工作，常指智力项目；强调共同成果，而非服从意愿。"},{"word":"helpful","ipa":"/ˈhelpfl/","tag":"personal attitude","definition":"Willing to be useful; it is warmer and more general than cooperative and carries no organizational sense.","definitionCN":"愿意提供帮助；比 cooperative 更亲切、更一般，也没有组织含义。"},{"word":"collective","ipa":"/kəˈlektɪv/","tag":"ownership emphasis","definition":"Shared by a whole group; it describes ownership or identity, while cooperative also implies joint work.","definitionCN":"由整个群体共有；描述所有权或身份，而 cooperative 还隐含共同劳动。"},{"word":"mutual","ipa":"/ˈmjuːtʃuəl/","tag":"two-way","definition":"Felt or done by both sides toward each other; mutual describes the direction of a relation, not its organization.","definitionCN":"双方彼此做出的；描述关系的方向，而非组织形式。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Normal associations: real morphemes, real collocations and real relatives, not invented rhymes.","cn":"正常联想：真实的构词成分、真实搭配与真实同族词，而非编造的顺口溜。"},"normal":[{"en":"cooperat- 'work together' + -ive 'tending to': a person or arrangement that tends to share the work.","cn":"cooperat-「共同做事」+ -ive「倾向于」：倾向于分担工作的人或安排。"},{"en":"The family runs cooperate, cooperation, cooperative, cooperatively and co-op.","cn":"同族词包括 cooperate、cooperation、cooperative、cooperatively 与 co-op。"},{"en":"Fixed phrases cover the senses: cooperative witness, cooperative society, cooperative learning, cooperative breeding.","cn":"固定搭配覆盖各义项：配合的证人、合作社团、合作学习、合作育幼。"},{"en":"As a noun, cooperative usually means a business; as an adjective, it usually means willing.","cn":"作名词时通常指合作社；作形容词时通常指愿意配合。"},{"en":"The short form co-op is informal and appears mainly in speech and shop signs.","cn":"缩略形式 co-op 偏口语，主要出现在口语与店招中。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture a circle of members each putting one coin into the same box and each taking one share out.","cn":"想象一圈成员各往同一个箱子里放一枚硬币，又各取一份出来。"},{"en":"Picture a class where every student holds one piece of the only map.","cn":"想象一个班级，每个学生只拿到唯一那张地图的一块。"},{"en":"Picture a hive where no single bee could build the comb alone.","cn":"想象一个蜂巢，没有哪只蜜蜂能独自造出整片巢脾。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The staff were cooperative even though the request came at midnight.","cn":"尽管请求是在午夜提出的，工作人员仍然很配合。"},{"en":"The cooperative sells coffee grown by its own members.","cn":"这家合作社出售成员自己种植的咖啡。"},{"en":"Cooperative breeding means that helpers raise chicks that are not their own.","cn":"合作育幼意味着帮手抚养并非自己的雏鸟。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"拆词记忆 · 非词源","text":"cooperate（合作）+ ive（……的）——愿意一起做事的；由成员共有的组织 → 合作的；合作社","word":"cooperative"},"root":"拉丁晚期 cooperativus「倾向于共同做事的」= cooperari（com- 一起 + operari 工作）+ -ivus；名词义由 19 世纪合作社团而来。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses split into two branches: an attitude or arrangement that shares work, and the organizations or methods built on that sharing.","cn":"八个义项分成两支：一是分担工作的态度或安排，二是建立在这种分担之上的组织或方法。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: members around one table, each contributing a part and receiving a share.","cn":"核心意象：成员围着一张桌子，各贡献一部分，也各分得一份。"},"chain":["WILLING TO HELP","SHARE THE WORK","SHARE OWNERSHIP","SHARE THE RETURNS","SHARE THE TASK","SHORTEN THE NAME"],"branches":[{"senses":"01 · 07","en":"THE PERSON: willingness measured as compliance in a clinic or a witness box.","cn":"人：在诊室或证人席上以顺从程度衡量的意愿。"},{"senses":"02 · 06","en":"THE ARRANGEMENT: a structure in which each member must contribute a part.","cn":"安排：一种要求每个成员贡献一部分的结构。"},{"senses":"03 · 04","en":"THE PROPERTY: shop and apartment turn shared ownership into a noun.","cn":"财产：商店与公寓把共同所有权变成名词。"},{"senses":"05","en":"THE BIOLOGY: help measured in extra surviving young.","cn":"生物学：以多存活的幼崽衡量的帮助。"},{"senses":"08","en":"THE CLIPPING: use wears the long word down to co-op.","cn":"缩略：高频使用把长词磨成短形式。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Cooperative is cooperari plus the adjective suffix -ive; the noun sense adds no new morpheme, only a new grammatical role.","cn":"cooperative 是 cooperari 加形容词后缀 -ive；名词义没有新增语素，只是换了语法角色。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Latin opus 'work' gives operari, then cooperari and cooperativus; English forms cooperate, cooperation, cooperative, cooperator and the clipping co-op.","cn":"拉丁 opus「工作」生成 operari，再生成 cooperari 与 cooperativus；英语构成 cooperate、cooperation、cooperative、cooperator 与缩略 co-op。"},"items":[{"word":"co-","structure":"co- (Latin prefix, 'together')","meaning":"together, jointly","meaningCN":"一起；共同","example":"Co- marks the second agent in the word.","exampleCN":"co- 标记词中的第二个行动者。"},{"word":"opus","structure":"opus, operis (Latin noun)","meaning":"work, a piece of work","meaningCN":"工作；一件作品","example":"Opus is the source of the oper- stem.","exampleCN":"opus 是 oper- 词干的来源。"},{"word":"operari","structure":"operari (Latin deponent verb)","meaning":"to work, labour","meaningCN":"工作；劳作","example":"Operari supplies the verb 'to work'.","exampleCN":"operari 提供「做事」这一动词义。"},{"word":"cooperari","structure":"co- + operari","meaning":"to work together","meaningCN":"共同做事","example":"The partners cooperated on the survey.","exampleCN":"伙伴们共同完成这项调查。"},{"word":"-ive","structure":"-ive (adjective suffix from Latin -ivus)","meaning":"tending to, having the quality of","meaningCN":"倾向于……的；具有……性质的","example":"The suffix turns cooperation into a disposition.","exampleCN":"这个后缀把「合作」变成一种倾向。"},{"word":"cooperative","structure":"cooperat- + -ive","meaning":"tending to work together; a jointly owned business","meaningCN":"倾向于合作的；共同所有的企业","example":"A cooperative shop is owned by its members.","exampleCN":"合作社商店由成员共有。"},{"word":"cooperation","structure":"cooperat- + -ion","meaning":"the act of working together","meaningCN":"共同做事的行为","example":"Cooperation made the harvest possible.","exampleCN":"合作使这次收成成为可能。"},{"word":"cooperator","structure":"cooperat- + -or","meaning":"one who cooperates","meaningCN":"合作者","example":"Each cooperator shares the profit.","exampleCN":"每位合作者分享利润。"},{"word":"co-op","structure":"cooperative clipped to co-op","meaning":"a cooperative shop or building","meaningCN":"合作社商店或合作公寓","example":"The co-op opens at seven.","exampleCN":"合作社七点开门。"},{"word":"operate","structure":"operari + -ate","meaning":"to work or run something","meaningCN":"运作；操作","example":"Two people are needed to operate the lift.","exampleCN":"操作这部升降机需要两个人。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"opus","structure":"opus, operis (n., third declension)","meaning":"work, labour","meaningCN":"工作；劳作"},{"word":"operari","structure":"operari, operatus sum (deponent verb)","meaning":"to work, labour","meaningCN":"工作；劳作"},{"word":"cooperari","structure":"co- + operari (deponent verb)","meaning":"to work together","meaningCN":"共同做事"},{"word":"cooperativus","structure":"cooperativus, cooperativa, cooperativum (adj.)","meaning":"tending to work together","meaningCN":"倾向于共同做事的"}]}},{"word":"learning","ipa_uk":"/ˈlɜːnɪŋ/","ipa_us":"/ˈlɜːrnɪŋ/","definition_zh":"学习；通过学习获得知识与技能的过程，也可指所获得的学问","definition_en":"the process of gaining knowledge or skill, or the knowledge so gained","core_image":"一个人把反复试错的结果留在手上，下一次动作更稳","scene":"琴房里，孩子一遍遍纠正指法，几周后同一段曲子终于不再出错。The child corrects her fingering again and again until the passage comes out right, and that slow change is learning.","sceneCN":"这里 learning 指「通过反复练习获得技能的过程」（第 1 个义项：练习带来行为上的稳定改变）；句意为孩子一遍遍纠正指法，直到同一段曲子不再出错。图中可辨识物件：琴键、节拍器、翻开的乐谱、反复移动的手。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"学习；学问；学习活动（不可数）"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"the learning process","zh":"学习过程"},{"phrase":"learning environment","zh":"学习环境"},{"phrase":"lifelong learning","zh":"终身学习"},{"phrase":"machine learning","zh":"机器学习"},{"phrase":"learning curve","zh":"学习曲线"},{"phrase":"a learning experience","zh":"一次学习经历"}],"forms":[{"label":"动词","form":"learn"},{"label":"三单","form":"learns"},{"label":"过去式（英式常用）","form":"learnt"},{"label":"过去式（美式常用）","form":"learned"},{"label":"过去分词","form":"learnt / learned"},{"label":"施动者名词","form":"learner"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"learn","pos":"v.","zh":"学习；学会"},{"word":"learner","pos":"n.","zh":"学习者"},{"word":"learned","pos":"adj.","zh":"有学问的（另作「学习」的过去式）"},{"word":"learnable","pos":"adj.","zh":"可学会的"},{"word":"unlearn","pos":"v.","zh":"忘掉（已学的东西）；改掉旧习"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"The process of acquiring knowledge or skill","titleCN":"获得知识与技能的过程","definition":"the process by which a person or animal gains knowledge, understanding or skill","definitionCN":"人或动物获得知识、理解或技能的过程","example":"The child corrects her fingering until the passage comes out right.","exampleCN":"孩子不断纠正指法，直到这段曲子不再出错。","why":"the -ing form names the activity itself, not one finished result: learning is what happens while the skill is still being built.","whyCN":"-ing 形式命名活动本身，而不是某个完成的结果：learning 是技能仍在形成时发生的事。"},{"no":"02","title":"Knowledge that has been gained","titleCN":"已获得的学问与知识","definition":"the body of knowledge a person has acquired through study","definitionCN":"一个人通过学习积累起来的知识总体","example":"Her learning was obvious in the range of sources she cited.","exampleCN":"她引用的资料范围之广，显露出她的学识。","why":"an activity can also name its product; what has been learned stays as a store that others can recognize.","whyCN":"活动也可以命名其产物；学到的东西留成一份储备，旁人能够辨认。"},{"no":"03","title":"Change of behavior through experience","titleCN":"经验带来的行为改变","definition":"a lasting change in behavior produced by experience rather than by instinct or maturation","definitionCN":"由经验而非本能或成熟带来的持久行为改变","example":"The rat avoids the gate after one mild shock.","exampleCN":"老鼠被轻微电击一次后就避开那道门。","why":"psychology defined learning operationally: if experience changes what an animal does, learning has occurred, whatever the inner state.","whyCN":"心理学从操作上定义学习：只要经验改变了动物的行为，就算发生了学习，不论内部状态如何。"},{"no":"04","title":"Machine learning","titleCN":"机器学习","definition":"the field in which computer systems improve their performance by finding patterns in data","definitionCN":"计算机系统通过从数据中发现模式而改进性能的领域","example":"The model improves its predictions after seeing more examples.","exampleCN":"模型看过更多样本后，预测变得更准。","why":"the metaphor is exact enough to be technical: a machine adjusts its internal parameters from experience, as an animal adjusts behavior.","whyCN":"这个比喻精确到足以成为术语：机器像动物调整行为那样，从经验中调整内部参数。"},{"no":"05","title":"School study and instruction","titleCN":"学校里的学习活动","definition":"organized study within a course, curriculum or training programme","definitionCN":"课程、教学大纲或培训项目中的有组织学习","example":"The school measures learning through projects, not only tests.","exampleCN":"这所学校通过项目而不只是考试来衡量学习。","why":"institutions need a countable domain, so the general process is narrowed to what happens inside a programme.","whyCN":"机构需要一个可管理的领域，于是把一般过程收窄为课程之内发生的事。"},{"no":"06","title":"Memorization by repetition","titleCN":"靠重复记诵","definition":"the act of fixing facts in memory through repeated study or recitation","definitionCN":"通过反复学习或背诵把事实固定在记忆中","example":"Learning the dates took three evenings of repetition.","exampleCN":"记住这些年代花了三个晚上的反复背诵。","why":"repetition is the oldest method of learning, and in ordinary speech the word often narrows to this visible, countable effort.","whyCN":"重复是最古老的学习方法；在日常说法中，这个词常收窄为这种看得见、可计数的努力。"},{"no":"07","title":"Learning ability or difficulty","titleCN":"学习能力或学习困难","definition":"the capacity to learn, or a diagnosed obstacle to it, as in learning disability","definitionCN":"学习的能力，或被诊断出的学习障碍，如学习障碍症","example":"The assessment distinguishes a language barrier from a learning difficulty.","exampleCN":"这项评估把语言障碍与学习困难区分开来。","why":"when used attributively, learning names the capacity being measured, which is why learning disability is about ability, not about effort.","whyCN":"作定语时，learning 指被测量的能力，因此「学习障碍」这一说法关乎能力，而非努力程度。"},{"no":"08","title":"A lesson drawn from experience","titleCN":"从经验中吸取的教训","definition":"the understanding gained from an event, especially a mistake","definitionCN":"从事件、尤指错误中获得的认识","example":"The failed launch taught the team a costly lesson.","exampleCN":"那次失败的发射给团队上了昂贵的一课。","why":"experience can teach without a teacher; the word extends to any change in understanding that comes from what happened.","whyCN":"经验可以没有老师也教人；这个词扩展到因发生的事情而产生的任何认识改变。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Learning is native English: Old English leornung 'study' from leornian 'to learn', with no Latin cognate. Dates are approximate.","cn":"learning 是英语本族词：古英语 leornung「学习」来自 leornian「学」，没有拉丁同族词。年代为约数。"},"items":[{"era":"OLD ENGLISH LEORNIAN","en":"Leornian meant 'to get knowledge, study, read, think about'; the noun leornung named the activity and its result.","cn":"leornian 意为「获得知识、学习、阅读、思考」；名词 leornung 指这项活动及其结果。"},{"era":"PROTO-GERMANIC","en":"The verb goes back to a reconstructed Proto-Germanic form usually written *liznojan, also the source of German lernen and Dutch leren.","cn":"这个动词可追溯到原始日耳曼语的重构形式，通常写作 *liznojan，也是德语 lernen 与荷兰语 leren 的来源。"},{"era":"PROTO-INDO-EUROPEAN","en":"The deeper root is reconstructed as *leis- 'track, furrow'; learning would then be pictured as following a track until it is known.","cn":"更早的词根被重构为 *leis-「痕迹、犁沟」；按此设想，学习就是循着痕迹走到熟悉为止。"},{"era":"MIDDLE AND MODERN ENGLISH","en":"Middle English kept learning for study and also for the knowledge gained; the modern gerund simply continues the same noun.","cn":"中古英语用 learning 既指学习也指所得的学问；现代英语的动名词只是延续同一个名词。"},{"era":"MACHINE LEARNING","en":"The technical sense dates from the mid-twentieth century, when programmers began to speak of machines that improve from data.","cn":"技术义形成于 20 世纪中期，当时程序员开始谈论能从数据中改进的机器。"},{"era":"UNCERTAIN DETAILS","en":"Source uncertain (first dates): the exact transition from 'the act of studying' to 'the knowledge possessed' is not dated, and the pre-Germanic reconstruction *leis- remains a hypothesis.","cn":"来源不确定（首见年代）：从「学习这一动作」到「拥有的学问」的确切转变没有年代记录；印欧语前的 *leis- 重构仍属假说。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"Group one holds forms of the same verb that are easily confused; group two holds words about gaining knowledge with different emphases.","cn":"第一组是同一动词的易混形式；第二组是同样关于获取知识、但侧重不同的词。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"learn","ipa":"/lɜːn/","tag":"the verb","definition":"To gain knowledge or skill; learning is the noun made from it, so the two cannot replace each other in a sentence.","definitionCN":"获得知识或技能；learning 是由它构成的名词，二者在句中不能互换。"},{"word":"learned","ipa":"/ˈlɜːnɪd/","tag":"adjective or participle","definition":"As an adjective, 'having much knowledge', pronounced with two syllables; as a participle, 'having learned', pronounced as one.","definitionCN":"作形容词意为「有学问的」，读两个音节；作分词意为「已学会的」，读一个音节。"},{"word":"learner","ipa":"/ˈlɜːnə/","tag":"the person","definition":"A person who is learning; the -er suffix names the agent, while -ing names the activity.","definitionCN":"正在学习的人；-er 后缀命名施动者，-ing 命名活动。"},{"word":"lesson","ipa":"/ˈlesn/","tag":"related by sound, not by -ing","definition":"A period of teaching or a piece of instruction; historically from Latin lectio 'a reading', not from learn.","definitionCN":"一堂课或一段教学内容；历史上来自拉丁 lectio「诵读」，并非由 learn 派生。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"education","ipa":"/ˌedjuˈkeɪʃn/","tag":"the organized system","definition":"The whole process and system of teaching, usually formal; learning can happen without any system.","definitionCN":"教学的全过程与制度，通常指正规教育；learning 可以在没有任何制度的情况下发生。"},{"word":"study","ipa":"/ˈstʌdi/","tag":"the effort","definition":"The activity of reading and working to learn; it names the effort, while learning names the change that results.","definitionCN":"阅读与用功以求得知识的活动；指付出的努力，而 learning 指由此产生的改变。"},{"word":"training","ipa":"/ˈtreɪnɪŋ/","tag":"skill practice","definition":"Instruction aimed at a specific skill or job; it is narrower and more practical than learning.","definitionCN":"针对某项技能或工作的训练；比 learning 更窄、更实用。"},{"word":"knowledge","ipa":"/ˈnɒlɪdʒ/","tag":"the store","definition":"The information and understanding a person holds; learning is the process or the acquired body of it.","definitionCN":"一个人掌握的信息与理解；learning 是过程或所获得的那部分学问。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Normal associations: real morphemes, real collocations and real relatives, not invented rhymes.","cn":"正常联想：真实的构词成分、真实搭配与真实同族词，而非编造的顺口溜。"},"normal":[{"en":"learn + -ing: the suffix turns the verb into the ongoing activity and its accumulated result.","cn":"learn + -ing：后缀把动词变成正在进行的活动及其积累的结果。"},{"en":"The family runs learn, learner, learned, learnable and unlearn.","cn":"同族词包括 learn、learner、learned、learnable 与 unlearn。"},{"en":"Fixed phrases mark the range: learning process, learning environment, lifelong learning, machine learning.","cn":"固定搭配标出范围：学习过程、学习环境、终身学习、机器学习。"},{"en":"Old English leornian is unrelated to Latin, so do not look for a Latin root.","cn":"古英语 leornian 与拉丁语无关，因此不要去找拉丁词根。"},{"en":"Learned as an adjective has two syllables; as a past participle it has one.","cn":"learned 作形容词时读两个音节，作过去分词时读一个音节。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture a path worn into grass by feet that keep taking the same route.","cn":"想象一条被反复踩出的草径，脚总走同一条路线。"},{"en":"Picture a hand that fumbles a knot ten times and then ties it without looking.","cn":"想象一只手打了十次都打不好的结，后来不看也能系上。"},{"en":"Picture a machine that adjusts one number after every mistake.","cn":"想象一台机器，每犯一次错就调整一个数字。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"Learning a language takes regular contact, not one long session.","cn":"学一门语言需要经常接触，而不是一次长时间的苦学。"},{"en":"The programme measures learning through real tasks.","cn":"该项目通过真实任务来衡量学习。"},{"en":"Machine learning models improve as they see more data.","cn":"机器学习模型随着看到更多数据而改进。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"「勒宁」——把知识勒进脑子里，留下痕迹 → 学习、学问","word":"learning"},"root":"古英语 leornung「学习」源自 leornian「学」，属日耳曼语族；更早可重构为原始日耳曼语 *liznojan，无拉丁同族词。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses move from the activity to its product: studying, the knowledge stored, the behavior changed, the machine that improves, the classroom, the repetition, the ability and the lesson.","cn":"八个义项从活动走向产物：学习、积累的学问、被改变的行为、会改进的机器、课堂、重复、能力，以及教训。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a repeated attempt that leaves a trace, so the next attempt is steadier.","cn":"核心意象：反复的尝试留下痕迹，于是下一次尝试更稳。"},"chain":["TRY","NOTICE","REPEAT","CORRECT","RETAIN","APPLY"],"branches":[{"senses":"01","en":"THE LOOP: trying, noticing and repeating is the minimal unit of learning.","cn":"循环：尝试、察觉与重复构成学习的最小单位。"},{"senses":"02","en":"THE STORE: what remains after the loop becomes knowledge one can show.","cn":"储备：循环之后留下的东西，成为可以展示的学问。"},{"senses":"03 · 06","en":"BEHAVIOR AND REPETITION: psychology measures the change; recitation is its oldest method.","cn":"行为与重复：心理学测量改变，背诵是最古老的方法。"},{"senses":"04 · 05","en":"TRANSFER: the same loop is given to machines and to classrooms.","cn":"迁移：同一条循环被交给机器，也被交给课堂。"},{"senses":"07 · 08","en":"CAPACITY AND LESSON: learning can be measured as ability or remembered as a warning.","cn":"能力与教训：学习既可作为能力被测量，也可作为警示被记住。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Learning is a Germanic root plus the productive -ing suffix; because the root has no Latin relative, the borrowed side of the family is empty.","cn":"learning 是日耳曼语词根加能产的 -ing 后缀；由于该词根没有拉丁同族词，借词一侧的词族为空。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"There is no reliable Latin cognate for learn, so latinEntries is left empty. Latin discere 'to learn' and studere 'to strive' belong to different families.","cn":"learn 没有可靠的拉丁同族词，因此拉丁词条留空。拉丁 discere「学习」与 studere「努力」属于不同词族。"},"items":[{"word":"learn","structure":"learn (Old English leornian, weak verb)","meaning":"to gain knowledge or skill","meaningCN":"获得知识或技能","example":"Children learn by copying and correcting.","exampleCN":"孩子通过模仿与纠正来学习。"},{"word":"-ing","structure":"-ing (Old English verbal noun suffix)","meaning":"the act, process or result of an action","meaningCN":"动作、过程或结果","example":"The suffix turns learn into a name for the activity.","exampleCN":"这个后缀把 learn 变成活动的名称。"},{"word":"learner","structure":"learn + -er (one who does)","meaning":"a person who learns","meaningCN":"学习者","example":"A learner needs feedback, not only input.","exampleCN":"学习者需要反馈，而不只是输入。"},{"word":"learned","structure":"learn + -ed (having undergone)","meaning":"having much knowledge (adjective)","meaningCN":"有学问的（形容词）","example":"A learned judge cites many sources.","exampleCN":"博学的法官会引用许多资料。"},{"word":"learnable","structure":"learn + -able (can be)","meaning":"able to be learned","meaningCN":"可学会的","example":"Most skills are learnable with practice.","exampleCN":"大多数技能都能通过练习学会。"},{"word":"unlearn","structure":"un- (reverse) + learn","meaning":"to discard a learned habit or belief","meaningCN":"忘掉已学的东西；改掉旧习","example":"Drivers must unlearn the old habit.","exampleCN":"司机必须改掉旧习惯。"},{"word":"lore","structure":"lore (Old English lār, related noun)","meaning":"traditional knowledge passed by word of mouth","meaningCN":"口耳相传的传统知识","example":"Folk lore preserves what schools do not teach.","exampleCN":"民间传说保存了学校不教的东西。"},{"word":"leornian","structure":"leornian (Old English verb)","meaning":"to learn, study","meaningCN":"学习；研读","example":"Leornian is the direct ancestor of learn.","exampleCN":"leornian 是 learn 的直接祖词。"}],"latinEntries":[]}},{"word":"cognition","ipa_uk":"/kɒɡˈnɪʃn/","ipa_us":"/kɑːɡˈnɪʃn/","definition_zh":"认知；知觉、记忆、推理等心理过程的总称，也指一次认识活动","definition_en":"the mental processes by which people perceive, remember, reason and know, or a single act of knowing","core_image":"脑中同时亮起感知、记忆与推理几盏灯，合起来照亮一个判断","scene":"志愿者看一张图三秒后回忆细节，再比较两种图案的差异。The volunteer recalls the details of a picture and then compares two patterns in the mind, a task designed to measure cognition.","sceneCN":"这里 cognition 指「知觉、记忆、推理等心理过程的总称」（第 1 个义项：把各种心智活动合在一起看）；句意为志愿者回忆图中细节并比较两种图案，这项任务用来测量认知。图中可辨识物件：图片、屏幕上的两种图案、秒表、记录表。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"认知；认识过程（不可数；指一次具体的认识活动时可数）"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"human cognition","zh":"人类认知"},{"phrase":"social cognition","zh":"社会认知"},{"phrase":"cognition and memory","zh":"认知与记忆"},{"phrase":"study cognition","zh":"研究认知"},{"phrase":"impair cognition","zh":"损害认知"},{"phrase":"a theory of cognition","zh":"一种认知理论"}],"forms":[{"label":"复数（具体的认识活动）","form":"cognitions"},{"label":"形容词","form":"cognitive"},{"label":"副词","form":"cognitively"},{"label":"动词（认识）","form":"cognize"},{"label":"名词（认知主义）","form":"cognitivism"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"cognitive","pos":"adj.","zh":"认知的；与思维有关的"},{"word":"cognitively","pos":"adv.","zh":"在认知上"},{"word":"cognize","pos":"v.","zh":"认识到；感知到"},{"word":"cognizant","pos":"adj.","zh":"知晓的；认识到的"},{"word":"cognitivism","pos":"n.","zh":"认知主义（认为心智可作信息加工来研究）"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"The whole set of mental processes","titleCN":"心理过程的总称","definition":"the collective name for perception, memory, reasoning, judgment and other ways of knowing","definitionCN":"知觉、记忆、推理、判断等认识方式的集合名称","example":"The volunteer recalls details and compares patterns in one task.","exampleCN":"志愿者在一项任务中回忆细节并比较图案。","why":"cognition gathers several faculties under one word because they cooperate in every real judgment; the noun names the team, not one player.","whyCN":"cognition 把几种官能收在一个词下，因为真实的判断总由它们协作完成；这个名词命名的是整支队伍，而不是单个队员。"},{"no":"02","title":"Cognitive ability","titleCN":"认知能力","definition":"the capacity to perceive, remember and reason, measured in tests","definitionCN":"在测验中衡量的知觉、记忆与推理能力","example":"The test scores cognition separately from language.","exampleCN":"这项测验把认知与语言分开计分。","why":"a faculty can be measured like a muscle, so the same noun shifts from the process to the capacity that supports it.","whyCN":"官能可以像肌肉一样被测量，因此同一个名词从「过程」转为支撑过程的「能力」。"},{"no":"03","title":"A single act of knowing","titleCN":"一次具体的认识活动","definition":"one instance of coming to know or noticing something, countable in philosophy","definitionCN":"一次得知或察觉某事的行为，在哲学中可数","example":"Each cognition begins with a distinction between self and object.","exampleCN":"每一次认识都始于自我与对象的区分。","why":"philosophy counts acts rather than faculties, so the mass noun gains a plural and a beginning and an end.","whyCN":"哲学计数的是行为而非官能，因此这个不可数名词获得了复数，也有了开头与结尾。"},{"no":"04","title":"Perception as the entry gate","titleCN":"作为入口的知觉","definition":"the part of cognition that takes in sensory information","definitionCN":"认知中接收感官信息的那一部分","example":"Colour cognition starts with the eye but does not end there.","exampleCN":"颜色认知始于眼睛，却不止于眼睛。","why":"nothing enters the mind without a sense channel, so perception is cognition at its boundary with the world.","whyCN":"没有感官通道，任何东西都进不了心智，因此知觉是认知与世界相接的边界。"},{"no":"05","title":"Memory and mental representation","titleCN":"记忆与心理表征","definition":"the storing and reactivating of information inside the mind","definitionCN":"信息在心内储存并被重新调用的过程","example":"Recalling the picture depends on memory as much as on perception.","exampleCN":"回忆那张图既依赖知觉，也依赖记忆。","why":"once information is taken in, it must be kept in some form; representation is the internal stand-in for the absent thing.","whyCN":"信息一旦被接收，就必须以某种形式保存；表征就是缺席之物在心内的替身。"},{"no":"06","title":"Reasoning and judgment","titleCN":"推理与判断","definition":"the manipulation of representations to reach a conclusion","definitionCN":"对表征进行操作以得出一个结论","example":"Comparing the two patterns requires reasoning about difference.","exampleCN":"比较两种图案需要对差异进行推理。","why":"cognition is not only storage; it also transforms what is stored, and that transformation is what we call thinking.","whyCN":"认知不只是储存，它还会改造所存之物，而这种改造就是我们所说的思考。"},{"no":"07","title":"The field of cognitive science","titleCN":"认知科学的研究领域","definition":"the interdisciplinary study of mind, spanning psychology, linguistics, neuroscience and computation","definitionCN":"跨越心理学、语言学、神经科学与计算的心智交叉研究","example":"Cognition is the central object of the new institute.","exampleCN":"认知是这家新研究所的核心研究对象。","why":"a phenomenon can name a discipline: what is studied becomes the label on the door of the department that studies it.","whyCN":"一种现象可以命名一门学科：被研究的东西，最终成了研究它的那间办公室门上的标签。"},{"no":"08","title":"Social and situated cognition","titleCN":"社会认知与情境认知","definition":"knowing as it happens in interaction with other people and with a setting","definitionCN":"在与他人的互动及具体环境中发生的认识","example":"Social cognition explains why a frown changes our judgment.","exampleCN":"社会认知解释了为什么一个皱眉会改变我们的判断。","why":"the mind rarely works alone; when researchers looked at real settings, the unit of study grew from one head to a pair and a room.","whyCN":"心智很少独自工作；研究者转向真实情境后，研究单位便从一个脑袋扩大为一对人和一个房间。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Cognition comes from Latin cognitio 'a getting to know', from cognoscere 'to get to know', itself com- plus gnoscere 'to know'. Dates are approximate.","cn":"cognition 来自拉丁 cognitio「得知、认识」，源自动词 cognoscere「认识、了解」，后者由 com- 加 gnoscere「知道」构成。年代为约数。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN GNOSCERE","en":"Gnoscere meant 'to know, recognize'; it belongs to the old root for knowing that also appears in English know and in Greek gnosis.","cn":"gnoscere 意为「知道、认出」；它属于古老的「知」词根，英语 know 与希腊语 gnosis 也在此列。"},{"era":"LATIN COGNOSCERE","en":"Com- 'thoroughly, together' plus gnoscere produced cognoscere, 'to get to know, learn, recognize'; the prefix here intensifies rather than adds a partner.","cn":"com-「彻底、一起」加 gnoscere 构成 cognoscere，意为「得知、了解、认出」；这里的前缀起加强作用，而非增加一个伙伴。"},{"era":"LATIN COGNITIO","en":"The noun cognitio 'a getting to know, acquaintance, knowledge' was formed on the participle stem cognit-.","cn":"名词 cognitio「得知、认识、知识」由分词词干 cognit- 构成。"},{"era":"MIDDLE ENGLISH","en":"English took cognition from Latin or French in the fifteenth century; early spellings included cognicion.","cn":"英语在 15 世纪从拉丁语或法语借入 cognition；早期拼写包括 cognicion。"},{"era":"MODERN PSYCHOLOGY","en":"From the twentieth century the word names the whole information-processing side of the mind, and cognitive science was founded as a field in the 1970s.","cn":"20 世纪起，这个词命名心智中整个信息加工的一面；认知科学作为学科在 20 世纪 70 年代确立。"},{"era":"UNCERTAIN DETAILS","en":"Source uncertain (first dates): the earliest English citation is not firmly dated, and the exact force of com- in cognoscere is debated between 'thoroughly' and 'together'.","cn":"来源不确定（首见年代）：最早的英语书证没有确切年代；com- 在 cognoscere 中究竟表示「彻底」还是「一起」，学界有争论。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"Group one holds words built on the same knowing root; group two holds neighboring mental terms that are often used loosely as synonyms.","cn":"第一组是同一「知」词根构成的词；第二组是常被宽松当作同义词的心智术语。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"cognitive","ipa":"/ˈkɒɡnətɪv/","tag":"adjective","definition":"Relating to cognition; cognition is the noun, cognitive the adjective that must modify something.","definitionCN":"与认知有关的；cognition 是名词，cognitive 是必须修饰某物的形容词。"},{"word":"recognition","ipa":"/ˌrekəɡˈnɪʃn/","tag":"re- plus the same root","definition":"The act of identifying something as known before; re- 'again' adds the return of a previous knowing.","definitionCN":"认出某物曾见过；re-「再次」加入「重新知道」的意思。"},{"word":"cognizance","ipa":"/ˈkɒɡnɪzəns/","tag":"French-shaped doublet","definition":"Awareness or notice, especially in law; it is the same Latin source reshaped in French, not a different root.","definitionCN":"知晓、注意，尤用于法律；同一拉丁来源经法语改形，并非不同词根。"},{"word":"cognate","ipa":"/ˈkɒɡneɪt/","tag":"same prefix, different root","definition":"A word related by descent; it joins co- with gnatus 'born', so its second element means birth, not knowing.","definitionCN":"同源词；它把 co- 与 gnatus「出生」结合，第二部分意为出生，而非知道。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"perception","ipa":"/pəˈsepʃn/","tag":"input only","definition":"The taking in of sensory information; it is one stage of cognition, not the whole chain.","definitionCN":"接收感官信息；是认知的一个阶段，而非整条链条。"},{"word":"thought","ipa":"/θɔːt/","tag":"the content","definition":"An idea or the activity of thinking; cognition is the broader scientific term for all such activity.","definitionCN":"一个想法或思考活动；cognition 是对所有此类活动的更宽泛的科学术语。"},{"word":"reasoning","ipa":"/ˈriːzənɪŋ/","tag":"stepwise inference","definition":"Thinking that moves from premises to conclusions; it is one kind of cognition with a strict order.","definitionCN":"从前提走向结论的思考；是有严格顺序的一种认知。"},{"word":"consciousness","ipa":"/kənˈsaʊsnəs/","tag":"awareness itself","definition":"The state of being awake and aware; cognition can be studied without solving the puzzle of consciousness.","definitionCN":"清醒并有所觉察的状态；认知可以在不解决意识难题的情况下被研究。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Normal associations: real morphemes, real collocations and real relatives, not invented rhymes.","cn":"正常联想：真实的构词成分、真实搭配与真实同族词，而非编造的顺口溜。"},"normal":[{"en":"com- 'thoroughly' + gnoscere 'know' = get to know thoroughly; the same root appears in know and gnosis.","cn":"com-「彻底」+ gnoscere「知道」= 彻底了解；同一词根也出现在 know 与 gnosis 中。"},{"en":"The family runs cognition, cognitive, cognitively, cognize and cognizance.","cn":"同族词包括 cognition、cognitive、cognitively、cognize 与 cognizance。"},{"en":"Fixed phrases mark the scope: human cognition, social cognition, cognition and memory.","cn":"固定搭配标出范围：人类认知、社会认知、认知与记忆。"},{"en":"Cognition is the umbrella; perception, memory and reasoning are its parts.","cn":"cognition 是伞；perception、memory 与 reasoning 是伞下的各部分。"},{"en":"Do not confuse cognition with cognate: the first root means know, the second means born.","cn":"不要把 cognition 与 cognate 混淆：前者词根意为「知」，后者意为「出生」。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture three lamps in one room: one lights the world, one keeps a copy, one rearranges the copies.","cn":"想象一间屋里三盏灯：一盏照亮世界，一盏保存副本，一盏重新排列副本。"},{"en":"Picture a hand that receives an object, stores it, and then turns it over to inspect it.","cn":"想象一只手接过物件、收好它，再把它翻过来检查。"},{"en":"Picture a library with an entrance desk, a shelf and a reading table.","cn":"想象一座图书馆，有入口前台、书架与阅览桌。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The study compares cognition in children and adults.","cn":"这项研究比较儿童与成人的认知。"},{"en":"Sleep loss impairs cognition more than it impairs mood.","cn":"睡眠不足对认知的损害甚于对情绪的影响。"},{"en":"Social cognition looks at how we read other people's intentions.","cn":"社会认知研究我们如何解读他人的意图。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"「可个尼神」——脑子里几盏灯一起亮，才认得清 → 认知","word":"cognition"},"root":"拉丁 cognitio「认识」← cognoscere「得知」= com-（彻底）+ gnoscere「知道」；与 know、gnosis 同出古老的「知」词根。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses separate what is usually bundled: the faculty, its measurable strength, a single act, perception, memory, reasoning, the science, and knowing in company.","cn":"八个义项把平日捆在一起的东西分开：官能、可测的强度、单次行为、知觉、记忆、推理、学科，以及与他人共处的认识。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: several lamps lit at once, each showing a different face of the same object.","cn":"核心意象：几盏灯同时亮起，各自照出同一对象的不同侧面。"},"chain":["SENSE","NOTICE","REPRESENT","COMPARE","INFER","KNOW"],"branches":[{"senses":"01 · 02","en":"THE WHOLE AND ITS STRENGTH: the team of faculties, then the muscle measured by a test.","cn":"整体与强度：先是一组官能，再是被测验衡量的那块肌肉。"},{"senses":"03","en":"ONE ACT: philosophy cuts the stream into countable moments of knowing.","cn":"单次行为：哲学把连续流切成可计数的「知」的瞬间。"},{"senses":"04 · 05","en":"ENTRY AND STORE: perception lets the world in, memory keeps it.","cn":"入口与储存：知觉让世界进来，记忆把它留住。"},{"senses":"06","en":"TRANSFORM: reasoning rearranges what perception and memory supply.","cn":"改造：推理重新排列知觉与记忆提供的东西。"},{"senses":"07 · 08","en":"LABEL AND SETTING: the process becomes a department, and the lone mind becomes a pair.","cn":"标签与情境：过程变成学科，孤单的心智变成一对人。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Cognition is a Latin prefix-root noun: com- plus gnoscere plus -tion. The root carries the idea of knowing, the prefix the idea of thoroughness.","cn":"cognition 是拉丁前缀加词根的名词：com- 加 gnoscere 再加 -tion。词根承载「知」，前缀承载「彻底」。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Latin gnoscere 'to know' gives cognoscere and cognitio; English draws cognition, cognitive, cognizance and recognize from the same line.","cn":"拉丁 gnoscere「知道」生成 cognoscere 与 cognitio；英语由此得到 cognition、cognitive、cognizance 与 recognize。"},"items":[{"word":"com-","structure":"com- (Latin prefix, 'together, thoroughly')","meaning":"together; completely","meaningCN":"一起；彻底","example":"Before n the prefix is written com-, not con-.","exampleCN":"在 n 之前，这个前缀写作 com-，不是 con-。"},{"word":"gnoscere","structure":"gnoscere (Latin verb, variant of noscere)","meaning":"to know, recognize","meaningCN":"知道；认出","example":"The root survives in gnosis and diagnosis.","exampleCN":"这个词根留在 gnosis 与 diagnosis 中。"},{"word":"cognoscere","structure":"com- + gnoscere","meaning":"to get to know, learn, recognize","meaningCN":"得知；了解；认出","example":"Cognoscere is the source of the whole English family.","exampleCN":"cognoscere 是整个英语词族的来源。"},{"word":"-tion","structure":"-tion (noun suffix from Latin -tio)","meaning":"the act or result of","meaningCN":"……的动作或结果","example":"The suffix turns the verb of knowing into a noun.","exampleCN":"这个后缀把「知」的动词变成名词。"},{"word":"cognition","structure":"cognit- + -ion","meaning":"the act or faculty of knowing","meaningCN":"认识的行为或官能","example":"Cognition covers perception, memory and reasoning.","exampleCN":"认知涵盖知觉、记忆与推理。"},{"word":"cognitive","structure":"cognit- + -ive","meaning":"relating to knowing","meaningCN":"与认识有关的","example":"Cognitive tests measure more than memory.","exampleCN":"认知测验测量的不止记忆。"},{"word":"cognizance","structure":"cognit- through Old French conoissance","meaning":"awareness, notice","meaningCN":"知晓；注意","example":"The court took cognizance of the report.","exampleCN":"法院注意到了这份报告。"},{"word":"recognize","structure":"re- (again) + cognoscere","meaning":"to identify as previously known","meaningCN":"认出；承认","example":"She recognized the melody at once.","exampleCN":"她立刻认出了这段旋律。"},{"word":"cognate","structure":"co- + gnatus (born)","meaning":"related by descent","meaningCN":"同源的","example":"Cognate words share an ancestor, not a meaning.","exampleCN":"同源词共享祖词，而非共享词义。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"noscere","structure":"noscere, novi, notum (verb, third conjugation)","meaning":"to know, recognize","meaningCN":"知道；认出"},{"word":"cognoscere","structure":"cognoscere, cognovi, cognitum (verb, third conjugation)","meaning":"to get to know, learn","meaningCN":"得知；了解"},{"word":"cognitio","structure":"cognitio, cognitionis (f., third declension)","meaning":"a getting to know; knowledge","meaningCN":"认识；知识"}]}},{"word":"cognitive","ipa_uk":"/ˈkɒɡnətɪv/","ipa_us":"/ˈkɑːɡnətɪv/","definition_zh":"认知的；与知觉、记忆、推理等思维过程有关的","definition_en":"relating to the mental processes of perceiving, remembering, reasoning and knowing","core_image":"一张脑内地图上标着看、记、想三个相连的节点","scene":"老师让学生先记住一串数字，再做一道逻辑题，比较两种任务的表现。The teacher asks students to memorize a string of digits and then solve a logic puzzle, comparing their performance on two cognitive tasks.","sceneCN":"这里 cognitive 指「与思维过程有关的」（第 1 个义项：知觉、记忆、推理这类活动）；句意为老师让学生记数字再做逻辑题，比较两种认知任务的表现。图中可辨识物件：数字串、逻辑题、两块答题板、计时器。","pos":[{"tag":"adj.","zh":"认知的；与思维过程有关的"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"cognitive development","zh":"认知发展"},{"phrase":"cognitive science","zh":"认知科学"},{"phrase":"cognitive psychology","zh":"认知心理学"},{"phrase":"cognitive bias","zh":"认知偏差"},{"phrase":"cognitive load","zh":"认知负荷"},{"phrase":"cognitive therapy","zh":"认知疗法"}],"forms":[{"label":"比较级","form":"more cognitive"},{"label":"最高级","form":"most cognitive"},{"label":"副词","form":"cognitively"},{"label":"名词（认知）","form":"cognition"},{"label":"名词（认知主义）","form":"cognitivism"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"cognition","pos":"n.","zh":"认知；认识过程"},{"word":"cognitively","pos":"adv.","zh":"在认知上"},{"word":"cognitivism","pos":"n.","zh":"认知主义"},{"word":"cognitivist","pos":"n./adj.","zh":"认知主义者（的）"},{"word":"metacognitive","pos":"adj.","zh":"元认知的（对自己的思考进行思考）"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Relating to thinking processes","titleCN":"与思维过程有关的","definition":"concerning perception, memory, reasoning or other mental processes","definitionCN":"关乎知觉、记忆、推理或其他心理过程","example":"The teacher compares performance on two cognitive tasks.","exampleCN":"老师比较两项认知任务的表现。","why":"the adjective adds -ive 'tending to' to the noun stem, so it describes anything that belongs to the business of knowing.","whyCN":"这个形容词在名词词干后加 -ive「倾向于」，描述一切属于「认识」这件事的东西。"},{"no":"02","title":"Of cognitive psychology","titleCN":"认知心理学的","definition":"belonging to the branch of psychology that studies mental processes","definitionCN":"属于研究心理过程的心理学分支","example":"The lab runs a cognitive psychology experiment on attention.","exampleCN":"实验室做了一项关于注意的认知心理学实验。","why":"a discipline needs an adjective for its own subject matter, and this word supplies it.","whyCN":"一门学科需要为本学科的研究对象配一个形容词，这个词正好补上。"},{"no":"03","title":"Cognitive development","titleCN":"认知发展","definition":"the growth of perception, memory and reasoning from infancy onward","definitionCN":"从婴儿期起知觉、记忆与推理的发展","example":"Picture books support cognitive development in toddlers.","exampleCN":"图画书有助于幼儿的认知发展。","why":"development adds time to cognition; the adjective marks which line of growth is being measured.","whyCN":"发展给认知加上时间；这个形容词标明被测量的是哪一条成长线。"},{"no":"04","title":"Cognitive bias and cognitive load","titleCN":"认知偏差与认知负荷","definition":"used in fixed terms for systematic errors of judgment and for the mental effort a task demands","definitionCN":"用于固定术语，指判断的系统性偏差以及任务所需的心智努力","example":"Long instructions raise cognitive load before the task begins.","exampleCN":"冗长的说明在任务开始前就提高了认知负荷。","why":"once a field finds regular failure modes, it names them with the same adjective: bias in judging, load in working memory.","whyCN":"一个领域发现规律性的失败模式后，就用同一个形容词命名它们：判断中的偏差、工作记忆中的负荷。"},{"no":"05","title":"Cognitive linguistics","titleCN":"认知语言学的","definition":"relating to the approach that treats language as shaped by general mental processes","definitionCN":"属于把语言视为一般心智过程之产物的研究取向","example":"Cognitive linguistics treats metaphor as ordinary thought.","exampleCN":"认知语言学把隐喻视为日常思维。","why":"the adjective lets a whole school declare its base: language is not a separate module but part of cognition.","whyCN":"这个形容词让整个学派声明自己的立足点：语言不是独立模块，而是认知的一部分。"},{"no":"06","title":"Cognitive therapy","titleCN":"认知疗法的","definition":"relating to treatment that works on thought patterns rather than only on behavior","definitionCN":"属于针对思维模式而非只针对行为的治疗","example":"Cognitive therapy asks the patient to test a fearful belief.","exampleCN":"认知疗法要求病人检验一个恐惧信念。","why":"if distorted thinking maintains distress, then changing the thinking is a route to changing the distress.","whyCN":"如果扭曲的思维维持着痛苦，那么改变思维就是改变痛苦的一条路径。"},{"no":"07","title":"Belonging to cognitive science","titleCN":"认知科学的","definition":"relating to the interdisciplinary study of mind, information and computation","definitionCN":"属于心智、信息与计算的交叉研究","example":"The programme combines cognitive and computational methods.","exampleCN":"该项目结合认知方法与计算方法。","why":"the adjective becomes a badge of a field that borrows from psychology, linguistics, neuroscience and computing at once.","whyCN":"这个形容词成了一个领域的徽章，它同时借用心理学、语言学、神经科学与计算。"},{"no":"08","title":"Cognitive meaning in language","titleCN":"语言中的认知意义","definition":"the conceptual content a word carries, as opposed to its emotional colouring","definitionCN":"词语承载的概念内容，与情感色彩相对","example":"The cognitive meaning of home is a dwelling, not a feeling.","exampleCN":"「家」这个词的认知意义是住所，而不是一种情感。","why":"linguists split meaning into what it denotes and what it evokes; the adjective labels the denotative half.","whyCN":"语言学家把意义分为「指什么」与「唤起什么」；这个形容词标记前者。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Cognitive is Medieval Latin cognitivus, built on the participle stem of cognoscere 'to get to know' plus -ivus. It entered English in the sixteenth century. Dates are approximate.","cn":"cognitive 是晚期拉丁 cognitivus，由 cognoscere「得知」的分词词干加 -ivus 构成。它在 16 世纪进入英语。年代为约数。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN COGNOSCERE","en":"Cognoscere 'to get to know' joins com- 'thoroughly' to gnoscere 'to know'; its participle stem is cognit-.","cn":"cognoscere「得知」把 com-「彻底」与 gnoscere「知道」结合；其分词词干为 cognit-。"},{"era":"MEDIEVAL LATIN COGNITIVUS","en":"Scholastic Latin formed cognitivus 'having the power of knowing' from cognit- plus the adjective suffix -ivus.","cn":"经院拉丁语由 cognit- 加形容词后缀 -ivus 构成 cognitivus，意为「具有认识能力的」。"},{"era":"ENGLISH, SIXTEENTH CENTURY","en":"English borrowed the adjective in the sixteenth century, at first in philosophical writing about the powers of the mind.","cn":"英语在 16 世纪借入这个形容词，最初用于讨论心智能力的哲学著作。"},{"era":"TWENTIETH-CENTURY SCIENCES","en":"Cognitive psychology, cognitive science and cognitive therapy all took their names in the twentieth century, when the mind was studied as an information processor.","cn":"认知心理学、认知科学与认知疗法都在 20 世纪得名，当时心智被当作信息加工系统来研究。"},{"era":"UNCERTAIN DETAILS","en":"Source uncertain (first dates): the earliest English citation is not precisely fixed, and the medieval coinage may have been influenced by Greek-derived models in scholastic Latin.","cn":"来源不确定（首见年代）：最早的英语书证没有精确年代；这一中世纪新造词可能受经院拉丁语中希腊式构词模式的影响。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"Group one holds forms from the same knowing stem; group two holds adjectives about mental life with different scope.","cn":"第一组是同一「知」词干的形式；第二组是范围不同的心智形容词。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"cognition","ipa":"/kɒɡˈnɪʃn/","tag":"noun","definition":"The processes themselves; cognitive is the adjective that describes them or the tasks that measure them.","definitionCN":"指过程本身；cognitive 是描述这些过程或测量任务的形容词。"},{"word":"cognizant","ipa":"/ˈkɒɡnɪzənt/","tag":"aware, not mental","definition":"Knowing that something is the case; it means 'aware of', not 'relating to thinking processes'.","definitionCN":"知道某事属实；意为「知晓」，不是「与思维过程有关」。"},{"word":"intellectual","ipa":"/ˌɪntəˈlektʃuəl/","tag":"same root, different prefix","definition":"Relating to serious thought and learning; it comes from intellectus, another descendant of the same legere family.","definitionCN":"与严肃思考及学识有关的；来自 intellectus，是同一 legere 词族的另一支。"},{"word":"cognate","ipa":"/ˈkɒɡneɪt/","tag":"look-alike, different root","definition":"Related by descent in language; its second element is gnatus 'born', so it is not about thinking.","definitionCN":"语言上同源的；第二部分是 gnatus「出生」，与思维无关。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"mental","ipa":"/ˈmentl/","tag":"broader","definition":"Relating to the mind in general, including emotion and will; cognitive is narrower and points to knowing.","definitionCN":"泛指心智，包括情绪与意志；cognitive 更窄，指向「知」。"},{"word":"perceptual","ipa":"/pəˈseptʃuəl/","tag":"sensory stage","definition":"Relating to the senses and to what is taken in; perception is only the first stage of cognition.","definitionCN":"与感官及所接收之物有关；知觉只是认知的第一阶段。"},{"word":"rational","ipa":"/ˈræʃənl/","tag":"rules of inference","definition":"Following reason and logic; rational judges the quality of thinking, while cognitive only locates its domain.","definitionCN":"遵循理性与逻辑；rational 评判思考的质量，cognitive 只标出所属领域。"},{"word":"psychological","ipa":"/ˌsaɪkəˈlɒdʒɪkl/","tag":"the whole discipline","definition":"Relating to psychology, including emotion, motivation and social behavior; cognitive covers only the knowing side.","definitionCN":"与心理学有关，包含情绪、动机与社会行为；cognitive 只覆盖「知」的一面。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Normal associations: real morphemes, real collocations and real relatives, not invented rhymes.","cn":"正常联想：真实的构词成分、真实搭配与真实同族词，而非编造的顺口溜。"},"normal":[{"en":"cognit- 'know' + -ive 'tending to': anything that belongs to the work of knowing.","cn":"cognit-「知」+ -ive「倾向于」：一切属于「认识」这件事的东西。"},{"en":"The family runs cognition, cognitive, cognitively, cognitivism and metacognitive.","cn":"同族词包括 cognition、cognitive、cognitively、cognitivism 与 metacognitive。"},{"en":"Fixed phrases mark the fields: cognitive development, cognitive science, cognitive bias, cognitive load.","cn":"固定搭配标出领域：认知发展、认知科学、认知偏差、认知负荷。"},{"en":"Cognitive describes the domain, not the quality; a cognitive bias can be irrational.","cn":"cognitive 描述领域，而非质量；认知偏差可以是不理性的。"},{"en":"The adverb cognitively usually modifies verbs such as process, assess or decline.","cn":"副词形式通常修饰「加工、评估、衰退」这类动词。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture a map with three marked stops: see, store, infer.","cn":"想象一张地图标出三站：看、存、推。"},{"en":"Picture a workbench where raw sensory material is turned into a finished judgment.","cn":"想象一张工作台，把感官原料加工成判断成品。"},{"en":"Picture a light that falls only on the thinking half of a face.","cn":"想象一束光只照在脸孔中「思考」的那一半。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"Cognitive development is fastest in the first years of life.","cn":"认知发展在生命最初几年最快。"},{"en":"The test measures cognitive flexibility rather than factual recall.","cn":"这项测验衡量认知灵活性，而非事实记忆。"},{"en":"Cognitive therapy helped her question the belief that she was failing.","cn":"认知疗法帮助她质疑自己正在失败这一信念。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"拆词记忆 · 非词源","text":"cognition（认知）+ ive（……的）——属于认知活动的 → 认知的","word":"cognitive"},"root":"晚期拉丁 cognitivus「有认识能力的」← cognit-（cognoscere「得知」的分词词干）+ -ivus；与 cognition 同族。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses show the adjective attaching itself to tasks, to a discipline, to development, to named failure modes, to a school, to a therapy, to a field and to a slice of meaning.","cn":"八个义项显示这个形容词依次贴到任务、学科、发展、有名的失败模式、学派、疗法、领域，以及意义的一个切面上。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a tag marked 'knowing' pinned onto one item after another.","cn":"核心意象：一枚写着「知」的标签，被钉到一个又一个事物上。"},"chain":["PERCEIVE","STORE","COMPARE","REASON","DECIDE","KNOW"],"branches":[{"senses":"01 · 02","en":"THE DOMAIN: the adjective first marks the mental territory and the discipline that owns it.","cn":"领域：这个形容词先标出心智领地，以及拥有这片领地的学科。"},{"senses":"03","en":"TIME: development adds a growing line to the same territory.","cn":"时间：发展给同一片领地加上一条生长的线。"},{"senses":"04","en":"FAILURE MODES: bias and load are the named ways the machinery strains.","cn":"失败模式：偏差与负荷是这台机器吃力时被命名的样子。"},{"senses":"05 · 06","en":"APPLICATIONS: a linguistic school and a therapy both claim the adjective as their base.","cn":"应用：一个语言学派与一种疗法都把这个形容词当作自己的根基。"},{"senses":"07 · 08","en":"INSTITUTION AND MEANING: the adjective labels an interdisciplinary field and the denotative half of a word.","cn":"建制与意义：这个形容词既标出一个交叉学科，也标出词语意义中「指物」的一半。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Cognitive is a Latin participle stem plus the adjective suffix -ive; it has no independent prefix of its own, since com- is already inside the stem.","cn":"cognitive 是拉丁分词词干加形容词后缀 -ive；它本身没有独立前缀，因为 com- 已经含在词干里。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Cognoscere 'to get to know' yields cognit- and cognitivus; English adds cognition, cognitive, cognitively and the modern compound metacognitive.","cn":"cognoscere「得知」生成 cognit- 与 cognitivus；英语再加上 cognition、cognitive、cognitively 与现代复合词 metacognitive。"},"items":[{"word":"cognit-","structure":"cognit- (participle stem of cognoscere)","meaning":"known, having come to know","meaningCN":"已知道的；得知的","example":"The stem carries the finished act of knowing.","exampleCN":"这个词干承载已完成的「知」。"},{"word":"-ive","structure":"-ive (adjective suffix from Latin -ivus)","meaning":"tending to, having the nature of","meaningCN":"倾向于……的；具有……性质的","example":"The suffix turns the stem into a descriptive adjective.","exampleCN":"这个后缀把词干变成描述性形容词。"},{"word":"cognitive","structure":"cognit- + -ive","meaning":"relating to knowing","meaningCN":"与认识有关的","example":"Cognitive tasks test more than memory.","exampleCN":"认知任务测验的不止记忆。"},{"word":"cognition","structure":"cognit- + -ion","meaning":"the act or faculty of knowing","meaningCN":"认识的行为或官能","example":"Cognition is the noun behind the adjective.","exampleCN":"cognition 是形容词背后的名词。"},{"word":"cognitively","structure":"cognitive + -ly","meaning":"in a cognitive manner","meaningCN":"在认知方面","example":"The patient remained cognitively intact.","exampleCN":"病人在认知上保持完好。"},{"word":"cognitivism","structure":"cognitive + -ism","meaning":"the view that mind is information processing","meaningCN":"认为心智是信息加工的观点","example":"Cognitivism dominated psychology in the 1970s.","exampleCN":"认知主义在 20 世纪 70 年代主导心理学。"},{"word":"cognitivist","structure":"cognitivism + -ist","meaning":"a supporter of cognitivism","meaningCN":"认知主义者","example":"A cognitivist treats beliefs as representations.","exampleCN":"认知主义者把信念当作表征。"},{"word":"metacognitive","structure":"meta- (beyond) + cognitive","meaning":"relating to thinking about one's own thinking","meaningCN":"元认知的；对自己的思考进行思考的","example":"Metacognitive strategies help students monitor themselves.","exampleCN":"元认知策略帮助学生监控自己。"},{"word":"cognoscere","structure":"com- + gnoscere (Latin verb)","meaning":"to get to know","meaningCN":"得知；了解","example":"Cognoscere is the ultimate source of the family.","exampleCN":"cognoscere 是整个词族的最终来源。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"cognoscere","structure":"cognoscere, cognovi, cognitum (verb, third conjugation)","meaning":"to get to know, learn","meaningCN":"得知；了解"},{"word":"cognitio","structure":"cognitio, cognitionis (f., third declension)","meaning":"a getting to know; knowledge","meaningCN":"认识；知识"},{"word":"cognitivus","structure":"cognitivus, cognitiva, cognitivum (adj.)","meaning":"having the power of knowing","meaningCN":"具有认识能力的"}]}},{"word":"memory","ipa_uk":"/ˈmeməri/","ipa_us":"/ˈmeməri/","definition_zh":"记忆；记住并回想信息的能力，也可指一段回忆、纪念或计算机存储","definition_en":"the ability to remember information and experiences, a remembered event, or the part of a computer that stores data","core_image":"一间库房按编号存放过往片段，取件时按编号调出","scene":"老人闻到医院走廊的消毒水味，立刻想起多年前陪护家人的那个下午。The smell of disinfectant in the corridor brings back the afternoon years ago when she sat beside a sick relative, a sudden act of memory.","sceneCN":"这里 memory 指「唤起过往经历的能力」（第 1 个义项：把过去的片段重新调出）；句意为消毒水的气味让她立刻回到多年前陪护家人的那个下午。图中可辨识物件：医院走廊、消毒水瓶、长椅、被唤起的时间线。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"记忆；记忆力；回忆；纪念；计算机内存"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"from memory","zh":"凭记忆"},{"phrase":"in memory of","zh":"为纪念……"},{"phrase":"working memory","zh":"工作记忆"},{"phrase":"lose one's memory","zh":"丧失记忆"},{"phrase":"refresh one's memory","zh":"唤起记忆"},{"phrase":"memory loss","zh":"记忆丧失"}],"forms":[{"label":"复数（回忆）","form":"memories"},{"label":"动词（记住）","form":"memorize"},{"label":"形容词（难忘的）","form":"memorable"},{"label":"形容词（纪念的）","form":"memorial"},{"label":"副词","form":"memorably"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"memorize","pos":"v.","zh":"记住；背下来"},{"word":"memorization","pos":"n.","zh":"记忆；背诵"},{"word":"memorial","pos":"n./adj.","zh":"纪念碑；纪念的"},{"word":"memorable","pos":"adj.","zh":"难忘的"},{"word":"memorably","pos":"adv.","zh":"令人难忘地"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"The ability to remember","titleCN":"记住并回想的能力","definition":"the faculty by which information and past experiences are stored and recalled","definitionCN":"储存并调取信息与过往经历的能力","example":"The smell of disinfectant brings back that afternoon at once.","exampleCN":"消毒水的气味立刻把她带回那个下午。","why":"memory names a capacity before it names any particular content: the cupboard exists before the things put in it.","whyCN":"memory 先命名一种能力，再命名具体内容：柜子先存在，东西才放进去。"},{"no":"02","title":"A remembered event","titleCN":"一段回忆","definition":"a particular past event that one can recall","definitionCN":"能够回想起来的一件具体往事","example":"Her earliest memory is of a blue door.","exampleCN":"她最早的记忆是一扇蓝色的门。","why":"the mass noun becomes countable when a single episode is pulled out of the store and held up.","whyCN":"当单个片段被从库房里取出并举起时，不可数名词就变成可数。"},{"no":"03","title":"The content stored","titleCN":"记住的内容与印象","definition":"the information or impression retained about something","definitionCN":"关于某事物所保留的信息或印象","example":"His memory of the route was better than the map.","exampleCN":"他对路线的记忆比地图还准。","why":"what is stored is not the event but a trace of it, which is why memory can be accurate and wrong at the same time.","whyCN":"被储存的不是事件本身，而是事件的痕迹；因此记忆可以既准确又出错。"},{"no":"04","title":"Remembrance and commemoration","titleCN":"怀念与纪念","definition":"the keeping of someone or something in respectful remembrance","definitionCN":"以敬意把某人或某事留在怀念中","example":"A bench was placed in memory of the teacher.","exampleCN":"一张长椅被安放以纪念这位老师。","why":"the word widens from an individual's store to a community's shared keeping, and the phrase in memory of marks that shift.","whyCN":"这个词从个人的储存扩展到群体的共同保存；「为纪念……」这一短语标记了这种转移。"},{"no":"05","title":"Reputation after death","titleCN":"身后的名声","definition":"the way a person is remembered by later generations","definitionCN":"后人对某人的记忆与评价","example":"The engineer left a memory of honesty.","exampleCN":"这位工程师留下了诚实的名声。","why":"if memory is what survives, then a person's memory is the part of them that outlives them.","whyCN":"如果 memory 是留存下来的东西，那么一个人的 memory 就是比他活得更久的那部分。"},{"no":"06","title":"Computer memory","titleCN":"计算机内存","definition":"the electronic storage in a computer that holds data and programs for immediate use","definitionCN":"计算机中存放数据与程序以供即时使用的电子存储","example":"The program needs more memory than the laptop has.","exampleCN":"这个程序需要的内存超过这台笔记本的容量。","why":"the machine metaphor is literal: data is put in, kept, and taken out, exactly like a remembered thing.","whyCN":"机器的比喻是字面的：数据被放入、保存、取出，和记住的东西完全一样。"},{"no":"07","title":"Storage capacity","titleCN":"存储容量","definition":"the amount of data a device or medium can hold","definitionCN":"设备或介质能够容纳的数据量","example":"The phone has sixty-four gigabytes of memory.","exampleCN":"这部手机有六十四吉字节的存储。","why":"once storage is a place, it can be measured like shelf space, so the noun shifts from the place to its size.","whyCN":"存储一旦成为场所，就能像货架空间那样被计量，于是名词从场所转为容量。"},{"no":"08","title":"A memorial object or rite","titleCN":"纪念物或纪念仪式","definition":"an object, day or ceremony that keeps someone or something in mind","definitionCN":"把某人或某事留在心上的物品、日子或仪式","example":"The village holds a memory ceremony every spring.","exampleCN":"这个村庄每年春天举行纪念仪式。","why":"a memorial is memory externalized, made visible so that forgetting becomes harder.","whyCN":"纪念物是记忆的外化，被做成看得见的东西，使遗忘更困难。"},{"no":"09","title":"A type of memory system","titleCN":"记忆系统的类型","definition":"a named subsystem such as working, short-term or long-term memory","definitionCN":"被命名的子系统，如工作记忆、短时记忆或长时记忆","example":"Working memory holds a phone number just long enough to dial.","exampleCN":"工作记忆把电话号码保留到拨完为止。","why":"research splits the cupboard into compartments, and each compartment inherits the same word.","whyCN":"研究把柜子分成隔间，每个隔间都继承同一个词。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Memory comes from Latin memoria, from memor 'mindful', and reached English through Old French. The computing sense is twentieth-century. Dates are approximate.","cn":"memory 来自拉丁 memoria，源自 memor「记得的」，经古法语进入英语。计算义是 20 世纪的延伸。年代为约数。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN MEMOR","en":"Memor was an adjective meaning 'mindful, remembering'; it described a person who keeps something in mind.","cn":"memor 是形容词，意为「记得的、留心的」，描述把某事放在心上的人。"},{"era":"LATIN MEMORIA","en":"Memoria 'memory, remembrance, the faculty of remembering' was built on memor and named both the capacity and its content.","cn":"memoria「记忆、怀念、记忆力」由 memor 构成，同时命名能力与内容。"},{"era":"OLD FRENCH MEMORIE","en":"Old French memorie carried the word into English in the thirteenth century; the ending settled as -y.","cn":"古法语 memorie 在 13 世纪把词带入英语；词尾最终固定为 -y。"},{"era":"PROTO-INDO-EUROPEAN","en":"The deeper root is reconstructed as *men- 'to think', also present in mind and in Greek mnēmē 'memory'.","cn":"更早的词根被重构为 *men-「思考」，也出现在英语的「心智」一词与希腊语 mnēmē「记忆」中。"},{"era":"COMPUTING","en":"Memory in the machine sense dates from the 1940s, when early computers stored instructions electronically.","cn":"机器义的 memory 形成于 20 世纪 40 年代，当时早期计算机以电子方式存储指令。"},{"era":"UNCERTAIN DETAILS","en":"Source uncertain (first dates): the exact first English use of the computing sense is not fixed, and the pre-Latin history of memor is reconstructed rather than directly attested.","cn":"来源不确定（首见年代）：计算义的最早英语用法没有确切年代；memor 在拉丁语之前的历史属于重构，而非直接书证。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"Group one holds words from the same memor family that are easily swapped; group two holds words about bringing the past back.","cn":"第一组是同一 memor 词族里容易混用的词；第二组是关于把过去重新带回的词。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"memorize","ipa":"/ˈmeməraɪz/","tag":"verb","definition":"To commit something to memory deliberately; memory is the store, memorize is the act of putting something in.","definitionCN":"有意把某物记入记忆；memory 是库房，memorize 是放入的动作。"},{"word":"memorial","ipa":"/məˈmɔːriəl/","tag":"object or service","definition":"Something built or held to remember a person or event; it externalizes memory rather than naming the faculty.","definitionCN":"为纪念某人或某事而建或举行的东西；把记忆外化，而非命名能力。"},{"word":"memorable","ipa":"/ˈmemərəbl/","tag":"worth remembering","definition":"Worthy of being remembered; it judges the content, while memory names the container.","definitionCN":"值得记住的；评判内容，而 memory 命名容器。"},{"word":"memorandum","ipa":"/məˈrændəm/","tag":"a thing to be remembered","definition":"A note made so that something will not be forgotten; Latin memorare 'to mention' supplies it, not the noun memory directly.","definitionCN":"为防止遗忘而写的备忘；来自拉丁 memorare「提及」，并非直接由名词 memory 派生。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"recall","ipa":"/rɪˈkɔːl/","tag":"the act of retrieval","definition":"The act of bringing something back to mind; memory is the store, recall is the hand that reaches in.","definitionCN":"把某物重新带回心头的动作；memory 是库房，recall 是伸进去的手。"},{"word":"recollection","ipa":"/ˌrekəˈlekʃn/","tag":"effortful retrieval","definition":"The process of piecing a past scene together; it often implies effort and partial reconstruction.","definitionCN":"把过去场景一块块拼回来的过程；常暗示费力与部分重建。"},{"word":"remembrance","ipa":"/rɪˈmembrəns/","tag":"honouring","definition":"The act of keeping someone in mind, often with ceremony; it leans toward commemoration rather than storage.","definitionCN":"把某人留在心上的行为，常伴仪式；偏向纪念而非储存。"},{"word":"retention","ipa":"/rɪˈtenʃn/","tag":"how much stays","definition":"The degree to which learned material remains available over time; it measures memory's durability.","definitionCN":"所学材料随时间保留的程度；衡量记忆的持久性。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Normal associations: real morphemes, real collocations and real relatives, not invented rhymes.","cn":"正常联想：真实的构词成分、真实搭配与真实同族词，而非编造的顺口溜。"},"normal":[{"en":"memor 'mindful' + -y gives memory; the same stem runs through memorize, memorial and memorable.","cn":"memor「记得的」+ -y 构成 memory；同一词干贯穿 memorize、memorial 与 memorable。"},{"en":"The family runs memorize, memorization, memorial, memorable and remembrance.","cn":"同族词包括 memorize、memorization、memorial、memorable 与 remembrance。"},{"en":"Fixed phrases mark the senses: from memory, in memory of, working memory, memory loss.","cn":"固定搭配标出各义项：凭记忆、为纪念、工作记忆、记忆丧失。"},{"en":"In computing, memory is a place; in psychology, it is both a place and a capacity.","cn":"在计算机领域，memory 是场所；在心理学中，它既是场所也是能力。"},{"en":"Memory is the cupboard, recall is the act of opening it.","cn":"memory 是柜子，recall 是打开柜子的动作。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture a dark warehouse where every box is labelled by date.","cn":"想象一座昏暗的库房，每个箱子都按日期贴标签。"},{"en":"Picture a smell that opens a door you did not know was there.","cn":"想象一种气味打开了一扇你不知道存在的门。"},{"en":"Picture a stone bench that keeps saying one name without sound.","cn":"想象一张石凳无声地反复说着一个名字。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"He recited the poem from memory.","cn":"他凭记忆背诵了这首诗。"},{"en":"The garden was planted in memory of her mother.","cn":"这座花园是为纪念她母亲而种的。"},{"en":"The update needs more memory than the old tablet has.","cn":"这次更新需要的内存超过旧平板电脑的容量。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"「没魔力」——记得住不是因为魔力，而是因为反复回看 → 记忆","word":"memory"},"root":"拉丁 memoria「记忆」← memor「记得的」；更早可重构为印欧语 *men-「思考」，与 mind、希腊语 mnēmē 同源。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Nine senses follow one cupboard: the capacity, one recalled event, the stored content, communal keeping, posthumous reputation, the machine's store, its size, the visible memorial and the named subsystem.","cn":"九个义项沿同一间库房展开：能力、一段回忆、所存内容、共同保存、身后名声、机器存储、容量、可见的纪念物，以及被命名的子系统。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a numbered store from which a past piece is fetched on demand.","cn":"核心意象：一座编号库房，按需把过去的片段取出。"},"chain":["EXPERIENCE","ENCODE","STORE","RETRIEVE","RECALL","HONOUR"],"branches":[{"senses":"01 · 02 · 03","en":"THE STORE AND ITS PIECES: capacity, one event, and the trace that remains.","cn":"库房与片段：能力、单件往事，以及留下的痕迹。"},{"senses":"04 · 08","en":"OUTWARD KEEPING: memory leaves the head as a ceremony or a bench.","cn":"向外的保存：记忆以仪式或长椅的形式离开脑袋。"},{"senses":"05","en":"AFTER LIFE: what survives of a person is precisely their memory in others.","cn":"身后：一个人留下来的，正是他在别人心中的记忆。"},{"senses":"06 · 07","en":"MACHINE: the same cupboard is built in silicon and then measured in gigabytes.","cn":"机器：同一间库房用硅造出来，再以吉字节计量。"},{"senses":"09","en":"COMPARTMENTS: research divides the cupboard and names each shelf.","cn":"隔间：研究把柜子分开，并给每层架子命名。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Memory is a Latin adjective turned noun: memor plus -y. The same stem builds a large family of verbs, adjectives and monuments.","cn":"memory 是拉丁形容词变来的名词：memor 加 -y。同一词干构成一大批动词、形容词与纪念物。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Latin memor 'mindful' gives memoria and memorare; English draws memory, memorize, memorial, memorable and remembrance from this line.","cn":"拉丁 memor「记得的」生成 memoria 与 memorare；英语由此得到 memory、memorize、memorial、memorable 与 remembrance。"},"items":[{"word":"memor","structure":"memor (Latin adjective, third declension)","meaning":"mindful, remembering","meaningCN":"记得的；留心的","example":"Memor is the adjective behind the whole family.","exampleCN":"memor 是整个词族背后的形容词。"},{"word":"-y","structure":"-y (noun suffix from Latin -ia)","meaning":"the state or quality of","meaningCN":"……的状态或性质","example":"The suffix turns the adjective into a noun.","exampleCN":"这个后缀把形容词变成名词。"},{"word":"memoria","structure":"memor + -ia (Latin noun)","meaning":"memory, remembrance","meaningCN":"记忆；怀念","example":"Memoria named both the power and its content.","exampleCN":"memoria 同时命名能力与内容。"},{"word":"memory","structure":"memoria through Old French memorie","meaning":"the faculty or content of remembering","meaningCN":"记忆的能力或内容","example":"Memory can be trained but not enlarged at will.","exampleCN":"记忆可以训练，却不能随意扩容。"},{"word":"memorize","structure":"memory + -ize","meaning":"to commit to memory","meaningCN":"记住；背下","example":"Actors memorize lines for weeks.","exampleCN":"演员要花几周背台词。"},{"word":"memorization","structure":"memorize + -ation","meaning":"the act of committing to memory","meaningCN":"记入记忆的行为","example":"Rote memorization fades quickly.","exampleCN":"死记硬背忘得很快。"},{"word":"memorial","structure":"memoria + -al","meaning":"a thing that keeps a person in mind","meaningCN":"使人记住某人的事物","example":"The memorial lists every name.","exampleCN":"纪念碑上列出了每个名字。"},{"word":"memorable","structure":"memor + -able","meaning":"worth remembering","meaningCN":"值得记住的","example":"It was a memorable evening.","exampleCN":"那是一个难忘的夜晚。"},{"word":"remember","structure":"re- (again) + memor","meaning":"to bring back to mind","meaningCN":"想起；记得","example":"I remember the blue door.","exampleCN":"我记得那扇蓝色的门。"},{"word":"commemorate","structure":"com- (together) + memorare","meaning":"to honour by keeping in memory","meaningCN":"纪念；缅怀","example":"The plaque commemorates the rescue.","exampleCN":"这块铭牌纪念那次救援。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"memor","structure":"memor, memoris (adj., third declension)","meaning":"mindful, remembering","meaningCN":"记得的；留心的"},{"word":"memoria","structure":"memoria, memoriae (f., first declension)","meaning":"memory, remembrance","meaningCN":"记忆；怀念"},{"word":"memorare","structure":"memorare, memoravi, memoratum (verb, first conjugation)","meaning":"to bring to mind, mention","meaningCN":"想起；提及"}]}},{"word":"memorization","ipa_uk":"/ˌmeməraɪˈzeɪʃn/","ipa_us":"/ˌmemərəˈzeɪʃn/","definition_zh":"记忆；把信息反复记入脑中的过程，也常指死记硬背","definition_en":"the process of committing information to memory, often by repeated practice or rote learning","core_image":"一个人把卡片一张张翻过，直到不看也能复述","scene":"考前一周，学生每天抄写同一列年代，直到合上书也能按顺序说出。For a week before the exam the student writes the same list of dates until she can recite it with the book closed, a routine of pure memorization.","sceneCN":"这里 memorization 指「把信息反复记入脑中的过程」（第 1 个义项：靠重复把内容固定下来）；句意为学生一周内每天抄写同一列年代，直到合上书也能按顺序背出。图中可辨识物件：卡片、年代列表、合上的书、计时器。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"记忆；背诵；死记硬背（不可数）"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"rote memorization","zh":"死记硬背"},{"phrase":"memorization of facts","zh":"对事实的记忆"},{"phrase":"a memorization task","zh":"记忆任务"},{"phrase":"pure memorization","zh":"纯粹的死记"},{"phrase":"a memorization technique","zh":"记忆技巧"},{"phrase":"emphasize memorization","zh":"强调背诵"}],"forms":[{"label":"动词","form":"memorize"},{"label":"三单","form":"memorizes"},{"label":"过去式","form":"memorized"},{"label":"现在分词","form":"memorizing"},{"label":"英式拼写","form":"memorisation"},{"label":"施动者名词","form":"memorizer"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"memorize","pos":"v.","zh":"记住；背下来"},{"word":"memorizer","pos":"n.","zh":"记忆者；背诵者"},{"word":"memory","pos":"n.","zh":"记忆；记忆力"},{"word":"memorable","pos":"adj.","zh":"难忘的"},{"word":"memorized","pos":"adj.","zh":"已背下的"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"The process of committing to memory","titleCN":"把信息记入脑中的过程","definition":"the process of fixing information in the mind through study or repetition","definitionCN":"通过学习或重复把信息固定在心中的过程","example":"She writes the dates until she can recite them with the book closed.","exampleCN":"她把年代写到合上书也能背出的程度。","why":"the -ation suffix names an action, so memorization is the work of putting something in, not the thing stored.","whyCN":"-ation 后缀命名一个动作，因此 memorization 是「放进去」的工作，而非被存放的东西。"},{"no":"02","title":"The state of having been memorized","titleCN":"已被记住的状态","definition":"the condition of being held in memory as a result of such work","definitionCN":"因这番工夫而被保存在记忆中的状态","example":"The dates were kept in memorization for years.","exampleCN":"这些年代被记住并保留了很多年。","why":"an action noun can slide into its result; what has been done stays done, and the word names that staying.","whyCN":"动作名词可以滑向结果；做过的事保持完成状态，而这个词命名这种保持。"},{"no":"03","title":"Rote learning without understanding","titleCN":"不求理解的死记硬背","definition":"learning by repetition alone, often with the implication that meaning is neglected","definitionCN":"仅靠重复的学习，常暗示忽略了意义","example":"The course rewards memorization over explanation.","exampleCN":"这门课奖励背诵多于解释。","why":"the same process becomes a criticism when it is separated from understanding; the word carries that judgement in school talk.","whyCN":"同一种过程一旦与理解分离就变成批评；在学校话语里，这个词带着这种评判。"},{"no":"04","title":"Material that has been memorized","titleCN":"背下来的材料","definition":"the text, list or lines one has learned by heart","definitionCN":"已经熟记的文本、清单或台词","example":"The actor ran through his memorization before the scene.","exampleCN":"演员在开场前把背下的台词过了一遍。","why":"metonymy turns the act into the thing acted on, as when a recitation is called a memorization.","whyCN":"转喻把动作变成被作用之物，于是背下来的内容也被称作 memorization。"},{"no":"05","title":"A classroom exercise","titleCN":"课堂上的记诵练习","definition":"a school task in which pupils learn facts or texts by heart","definitionCN":"要求学生熟记事实或文本的课堂任务","example":"The weekly memorization test covers twenty words.","exampleCN":"每周的记忆测验覆盖二十个单词。","why":"schools need countable exercises, so the general process becomes an item on the timetable.","whyCN":"学校需要可计数的练习，于是一般过程变成课表上的一个项目。"},{"no":"06","title":"Encoding and consolidation in psychology","titleCN":"心理学中的编码与巩固","definition":"the laboratory process by which material is encoded and then stabilized in long-term memory","definitionCN":"材料被编码并在长时记忆中稳定下来的实验过程","example":"Sleep improves the memorization of new vocabulary.","exampleCN":"睡眠有助于新词汇的记忆巩固。","why":"when psychologists look inside the process, repetition splits into encoding and consolidation, and this word covers both stages.","whyCN":"心理学家看进过程内部后，重复被分成编码与巩固，而这个词覆盖两个阶段。"},{"no":"07","title":"Learning lines for performance","titleCN":"为演出背台词","definition":"the actor's or musician's work of fixing lines, cues or scores in memory","definitionCN":"演员或乐手把台词、提示或乐谱记牢的工作","example":"Her memorization of the monologue took three days.","exampleCN":"她背下那段独白用了三天。","why":"performance cannot pause for a script, so the same process becomes a professional skill with its own practice routines.","whyCN":"演出不能为剧本暂停，因此同一种过程成为有专门练法的职业技能。"},{"no":"08","title":"Recitation of sacred or traditional texts","titleCN":"宗教或传统经典的记诵","definition":"the disciplined learning by heart of scriptures, poems or oral tradition","definitionCN":"对经文、诗篇或口传传统的有纪律的熟记","example":"Monks begin memorization of the sutras at an early age.","exampleCN":"僧侣很早就开始记诵经文。","why":"where a text must survive without copying, memory is the medium, and memorization is the technology.","whyCN":"当文本必须在不靠复制的情况下流传，记忆就是媒介，而记诵就是那项技术。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Memorization joins memorize with -ation; memorize itself comes from memory, from Latin memoria. The word is a modern English formation, not a classical Latin noun. Dates are approximate.","cn":"memorization 由 memorize 加 -ation 构成；memorize 又来自 memory，源自拉丁 memoria。这是现代英语的构造，并非古典拉丁名词。年代为约数。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN MEMORIA","en":"Memoria 'memory' comes from memor 'mindful'; it supplied the noun from which the English verb was later built.","cn":"memoria「记忆」源自 memor「记得的」，为后来英语动词提供名词基础。"},{"era":"ENGLISH MEMORY AND MEMORIZE","en":"English memory appeared in the thirteenth century; the verb memorize 'commit to memory' is recorded from the sixteenth century.","cn":"英语 memory 在 13 世纪出现；动词 memorize「记入记忆」在 16 世纪有记录。"},{"era":"-ATION NOUN","en":"The suffix -ation, from Latin -atio, names an action or its result; adding it to memorize produced memorization in the nineteenth century.","cn":"后缀 -ation 源自拉丁 -atio，命名动作或结果；加在 memorize 上，于 19 世纪构成 memorization。"},{"era":"BRITISH AND AMERICAN SPELLING","en":"British English also writes memorisation with -isa-, following the same pattern as organise; both forms are current.","cn":"英式英语也写作 memorisation，用 -isa-，与 organise 的拼法一致；两种形式都在使用。"},{"era":"UNCERTAIN DETAILS","en":"Source uncertain (first dates): the first recorded use of memorization is usually placed in the nineteenth century, but the exact year is not agreed, and the boundary with memorisation is purely orthographic.","cn":"来源不确定（首见年代）：memorization 的最早书证通常定在 19 世纪，但确切年份没有定论；它与 memorisation 的差别纯属拼写。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"Group one holds look-alike forms, including a technical term from computing that is not the same word; group two holds methods and products of learning by heart.","cn":"第一组是外形相近的形式，其中含一个并非同词的计算机术语；第二组是熟记的方法与产物。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"memorisation","ipa":"/ˌmeməraɪˈzeɪʃn/","tag":"British spelling","definition":"The same word spelled with -isa-; the difference is orthographic only.","definitionCN":"同一个词的英式拼写，用 -isa-；差别只在拼写。"},{"word":"memoization","ipa":"/ˌmeməʊaɪˈzeɪʃn/","tag":"not the same word","definition":"A programming technique that caches function results; it is coined from memo, not from memory, and has nothing to do with human recall.","definitionCN":"一种缓存函数结果的编程技术；由 memo 而非 memory 造出，与人的回忆无关。"},{"word":"memorize","ipa":"/ˈmeməraɪz/","tag":"the verb","definition":"To commit something to memory; memorization is the noun naming that activity.","definitionCN":"把某物记入记忆；memorization 是命名该活动的名词。"},{"word":"memory","ipa":"/ˈmeməri/","tag":"the store","definition":"The faculty or content of remembering; memorization names the effort that fills it.","definitionCN":"记忆的能力或内容；memorization 命名填满它的那番努力。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"rote learning","ipa":"/rəʊt ˈlɜːnɪŋ/","tag":"the method","definition":"Learning by repetition without attention to meaning; memorization can be rote, but need not be.","definitionCN":"不看意义、只靠重复的学习；memorization 可以是死记，但不必然如此。"},{"word":"repetition","ipa":"/ˌrepəˈtɪʃn/","tag":"the mechanism","definition":"Doing or saying the same thing again; it is the engine that makes memorization work.","definitionCN":"重复做或说同一件事；是让记忆生效的引擎。"},{"word":"recitation","ipa":"/ˌresɪˈteɪʃn/","tag":"the performance","definition":"Saying aloud what has been learned by heart; it displays memorization rather than producing it.","definitionCN":"出声说出背下的内容；展示记忆，而非产生记忆。"},{"word":"retention","ipa":"/rɪˈtenʃn/","tag":"the outcome","definition":"How much remains available after learning; it is the measure of successful memorization.","definitionCN":"学习后还能保留多少；是记忆成功与否的度量。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Normal associations: real morphemes, real collocations and real relatives, not invented rhymes.","cn":"正常联想：真实的构词成分、真实搭配与真实同族词，而非编造的顺口溜。"},"normal":[{"en":"memory + -ize + -ation: the store, the act of filling it, and the name of that act.","cn":"memory + -ize + -ation：库房、装填的动作，以及这一动作的名称。"},{"en":"The family runs memorize, memorizer, memory, memorable and memorization.","cn":"同族词包括 memorize、memorizer、memory、memorable 与 memorization。"},{"en":"Fixed phrases mark the use: rote memorization, memorization task, memorization technique.","cn":"固定搭配标出用法：死记硬背、记忆任务、记忆技巧。"},{"en":"Memorization is the process; memory is the store; recall is the retrieval.","cn":"memorization 是过程，memory 是库房，recall 是取出。"},{"en":"Do not confuse memorization with memoization: the computing term comes from memo, not memory.","cn":"不要把 memorization 与 memoization 混淆：计算机术语来自 memo，而非 memory。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture a hand copying the same line until the line lives in the hand.","cn":"想象一只手反复抄同一行，直到那一行住进手里。"},{"en":"Picture a door closing on a full shelf and opening only when called.","cn":"想象一扇门在一排满架前关上，只在被呼唤时打开。"},{"en":"Picture a monk reciting in the dark because the book is inside him.","cn":"想象僧人在黑暗中诵经，因为书就在他体内。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The exam rewards memorization more than analysis.","cn":"这场考试奖励背诵多于分析。"},{"en":"Daily memorization of ten words beats one long session.","cn":"每天记十个词胜过一次性长时间苦背。"},{"en":"Sleep supports the consolidation that memorization requires.","cn":"睡眠支持记忆所需要的巩固过程。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"拆词记忆 · 非词源","text":"memory（记忆）+ ization（过程）——把东西一遍遍放进记忆的过程 → 记忆、背诵","word":"memorization"},"root":"memory（拉丁 memoria）+ -ize（使……化）+ -ation（过程）；19 世纪英语构造，指把信息反复记入脑中的过程。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses describe the same work from different angles: the act, its result, rote method, learned material, classroom task, laboratory encoding, stage work and sacred recitation.","cn":"八个义项从不同角度描述同一番工夫：动作、结果、死记方法、背下的材料、课堂任务、实验编码、舞台功夫，以及经文记诵。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: the same line written again and again until it can be said without the page.","cn":"核心意象：同一行字被反复抄写，直到不看纸也能说出。"},"chain":["INPUT","REPEAT","ENCODE","STORE","RETAIN","RECITE"],"branches":[{"senses":"01 · 02","en":"ACT AND RESULT: the work of putting in, then the state of being held.","cn":"动作与结果：先放入的工夫，再是被保存的状态。"},{"senses":"03","en":"WITHOUT MEANING: repetition alone turns the method into a criticism.","cn":"不求意义：只剩重复时，方法就成了批评对象。"},{"senses":"04 · 07","en":"MATERIAL AND STAGE: what is held can be a list for a test or lines for a scene.","cn":"材料与舞台：记住的可以是测验清单，也可以是场景台词。"},{"senses":"05 · 06","en":"INSTITUTION AND LAB: the same act becomes a timetable item and an encoding stage.","cn":"建制与实验：同一动作既成为课表项目，也成为编码阶段。"},{"senses":"08","en":"SACRED USE: where no copy exists, memory is the only medium.","cn":"神圣用法：在没有副本的地方，记忆是唯一媒介。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Memorization stacks three pieces: the Latin stem memor, the verb suffix -ize and the noun suffix -ation.","cn":"memorization 叠了三层：拉丁词干 memor、动词后缀 -ize、名词后缀 -ation。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Latin memor 'mindful' yields memoria; English memory, memorize and memorization continue the line, while the computing term memoization comes from memo instead.","cn":"拉丁 memor「记得的」生成 memoria；英语 memory、memorize、memorization 延续这条线，而计算机术语 memoization 来自 memo。"},"items":[{"word":"memor","structure":"memor (Latin adjective)","meaning":"mindful, remembering","meaningCN":"记得的；留心的","example":"Memor is the base of the whole family.","exampleCN":"memor 是整个词族的基础。"},{"word":"-ize","structure":"-ize (verb suffix from Greek -izein through Latin)","meaning":"to make, to subject to a process","meaningCN":"使……化；使经历某过程","example":"Memory plus -ize gives the verb memorize.","exampleCN":"memory 加 -ize 构成动词 memorize。"},{"word":"-ation","structure":"-ation (noun suffix from Latin -atio)","meaning":"the act or result of a process","meaningCN":"过程的动作或结果","example":"Memorize plus -ation names the activity.","exampleCN":"memorize 加 -ation 命名这项活动。"},{"word":"memorization","structure":"memorize + -ation","meaning":"the act of committing to memory","meaningCN":"把信息记入记忆的行为","example":"Memorization without meaning fades fast.","exampleCN":"没有意义的背诵忘得很快。"},{"word":"memorize","structure":"memory + -ize","meaning":"to learn by heart","meaningCN":"熟记；背下","example":"She memorized the dates in a week.","exampleCN":"她一周内背下了这些年代。"},{"word":"memorizer","structure":"memorize + -er","meaning":"one who memorizes","meaningCN":"背诵者","example":"A good memorizer still needs a schedule.","exampleCN":"擅长背诵的人仍然需要计划。"},{"word":"memory","structure":"memor + -y","meaning":"the faculty of remembering","meaningCN":"记忆的能力","example":"Memory supplies the material.","exampleCN":"记忆提供材料。"},{"word":"memorable","structure":"memor + -able","meaning":"worth remembering","meaningCN":"值得记住的","example":"A memorable fact is easier to keep.","exampleCN":"难忘的事实更容易保留。"},{"word":"memorized","structure":"memorize + -ed","meaning":"learned by heart","meaningCN":"已背下的","example":"The memorized lines sounded flat.","exampleCN":"背下的台词听起来很平。"},{"word":"commemoration","structure":"com- + memor + -ation","meaning":"a joint act of remembrance","meaningCN":"共同的纪念","example":"The day is one of commemoration, not study.","exampleCN":"这一天是纪念，不是学习。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"memor","structure":"memor, memoris (adj., third declension)","meaning":"mindful, remembering","meaningCN":"记得的；留心的"},{"word":"memoria","structure":"memoria, memoriae (f., first declension)","meaning":"memory, remembrance","meaningCN":"记忆；怀念"},{"word":"memorare","structure":"memorare, memoravi, memoratum (verb, first conjugation)","meaning":"to bring to mind, mention","meaningCN":"想起；提及"}]}},{"word":"intelligent","ipa_uk":"/ɪnˈtelɪdʒənt/","ipa_us":"/ɪnˈtelɪdʒənt/","definition_zh":"聪明的；有理解力的；智能的（机器或系统能自主处理信息）","definition_en":"able to learn, understand and reason well; also describing machines or systems that process information without step-by-step instructions","core_image":"一个人从杂乱的线索中挑出关键几条，迅速拼出答案","scene":"陌生的岔路口没有路标，同行的人看了一眼太阳和影子就选对了方向。At an unmarked fork the companion glances at the sun and the shadows and picks the right path, a quietly intelligent choice.","sceneCN":"这里 intelligent 指「能迅速理解并作出明智判断的」（第 1 个义项：有理解力、能举一反三）；句意为在没有路标的岔路口，同行者凭太阳与影子选对了方向。图中可辨识物件：岔路、太阳、影子、没有路标的木桩。","pos":[{"tag":"adj.","zh":"聪明的；有理解力的；智能的"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"highly intelligent","zh":"非常聪明的"},{"phrase":"intelligent life","zh":"有智力的生命"},{"phrase":"an intelligent system","zh":"智能系统"},{"phrase":"intelligent design","zh":"智能设计"},{"phrase":"an intelligent agent","zh":"智能体"},{"phrase":"an intelligent decision","zh":"明智的决定"}],"forms":[{"label":"比较级","form":"more intelligent"},{"label":"最高级","form":"most intelligent"},{"label":"副词","form":"intelligently"},{"label":"名词（智力）","form":"intelligence"},{"label":"形容词（可理解的）","form":"intelligible"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"intelligence","pos":"n.","zh":"智力；智能；情报"},{"word":"intelligently","pos":"adv.","zh":"聪明地；智能地"},{"word":"intelligible","pos":"adj.","zh":"可理解的；清楚的"},{"word":"unintelligent","pos":"adj.","zh":"不聪明的"},{"word":"intelligentsia","pos":"n.","zh":"知识分子群体"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Able to understand and reason","titleCN":"有理解力、能推理的","definition":"able to learn, understand and solve problems well","definitionCN":"能够很好地学习、理解并解决问题","example":"The companion reads the sun and shadows and picks the right path.","exampleCN":"同行者看懂太阳与影子，选对了路。","why":"intelligere is 'to choose between' (inter plus legere), so the adjective first describes a mind that can pick out what matters.","whyCN":"intelligere 意为「在……之间挑选」（inter 加 legere），因此这个形容词首先描述能挑出要紧之物的心智。"},{"no":"02","title":"Machine intelligence","titleCN":"机器或系统的智能","definition":"describing a machine or program that performs tasks requiring adaptation or judgment","definitionCN":"描述能完成需要适应或判断之任务的机器或程序","example":"The system adjusts the heating without being told.","exampleCN":"这个系统不用人吩咐就会调节供暖。","why":"once a machine can choose among inputs, the old word for a choosing mind is borrowed for it.","whyCN":"一旦机器能在多种输入之间选择，用来形容会挑选的心智的旧词就被借给了它。"},{"no":"03","title":"Quick to grasp","titleCN":"领悟得快的","definition":"learning or understanding quickly, with little explanation needed","definitionCN":"学得快、理解得快，几乎不需要解释","example":"An intelligent reader sees the point of the footnote at once.","exampleCN":"聪明的读者一眼就看出脚注的用意。","why":"speed is the visible sign of the choosing mind: fewer trials are needed to reach the right option.","whyCN":"速度是会挑选的心智看得见的标志：到达正确选项所需的试错更少。"},{"no":"04","title":"Sensible and well-judged","titleCN":"明智的、判断得当的","definition":"describing a choice or plan that shows good judgment","definitionCN":"描述显示出良好判断力的选择或计划","example":"Taking the earlier train was an intelligent decision.","exampleCN":"坐早一班火车是个明智的决定。","why":"the adjective can move from the person to the product; a decision is intelligent when it shows the quality of the mind behind it.","whyCN":"形容词可以从人移到产物；一个决定之所以明智，是因为它显出背后心智的品质。"},{"no":"05","title":"Conveying information","titleCN":"载有信息的","definition":"used in technical writing for reports or signals that carry useful information","definitionCN":"技术文献中用于承载有用信息的报告或信号","example":"The sensor sends an intelligent report every ten minutes.","exampleCN":"传感器每十分钟发送一份含信息的报告。","why":"a technical sense survives from the older meaning 'informed': a signal is intelligent when it tells you something you did not know.","whyCN":"一个技术义从较早的「知情的」含义延续下来：信号能告诉你原先不知道的事，就是载有信息的。"},{"no":"06","title":"Intelligent design","titleCN":"智能设计（特定主张）","definition":"the claim that some biological structures bear marks of deliberate design","definitionCN":"主张某些生物结构带有刻意设计痕迹的说法","example":"Intelligent design is debated as a scientific claim.","exampleCN":"智能设计作为一种科学主张受到争论。","why":"the phrase borrows an everyday adjective for a contested claim, which is why it must be named and discussed rather than assumed.","whyCN":"这个短语借用一个日常形容词来表达一项有争议的主张，因此必须被点名讨论，而不能当作默认前提。"},{"no":"07","title":"Intelligent life elsewhere","titleCN":"别处的有智力生命","definition":"life forms capable of thought or communication beyond Earth","definitionCN":"地球之外能够思考或交流的生命形式","example":"The telescope listens for signals from intelligent life.","exampleCN":"望远镜在监听来自有智力生命的信号。","why":"the adjective sets a threshold: not merely living, but able to choose, signal and perhaps answer.","whyCN":"这个形容词设定一道门槛：不只是活着，还要能选择、发信号，或许还能回应。"},{"no":"08","title":"An intelligent agent","titleCN":"智能体","definition":"a software entity that perceives its environment and acts toward a goal","definitionCN":"感知环境并朝目标行动的软件实体","example":"Each intelligent agent negotiates a price on its own.","exampleCN":"每个智能体自行协商价格。","why":"the technical term keeps the core of the word: perception, choice and action bound into one loop.","whyCN":"这个技术术语保留了词的核心：感知、选择与行动绑成一个循环。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Intelligent is the present participle of Latin intelligere 'to understand', from inter 'between' and legere 'to choose, pick out, read'. Dates are approximate.","cn":"intelligent 是拉丁 intelligere「理解」的现在分词，由 inter「在……之间」与 legere「挑选、读出」构成。年代为约数。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN LEGERE","en":"Legere meant 'to gather, pick out, read'; its past participle lectus underlies lecture, collect and select.","cn":"legere 意为「收集、挑出、阅读」；其过去分词 lectus 是 lecture、collect 与 select 的词根。"},{"era":"LATIN INTELLIGERE","en":"Inter 'between' plus legere produced intelligere, 'to choose between, discern, understand'; the mind is pictured as selecting among signs.","cn":"inter「在……之间」加 legere 构成 intelligere，意为「从中挑选、辨别、理解」；心智被设想为在多种迹象之间做选择。"},{"era":"LATIN INTELLIGENS","en":"The present participle intelligens 'understanding' became the English adjective intelligent in the late fifteenth century.","cn":"现在分词 intelligens「理解的」在 15 世纪末成为英语形容词 intelligent。"},{"era":"INTELLIGENCE AND ITS DOUBLE MEANING","en":"Latin intelligentia gave English intelligence, which means both the mental power and gathered information, so the adjective serves both domains.","cn":"拉丁 intelligentia 生成英语 intelligence，既指心智能力也指收集到的情报，因此形容词同时服务两个领域。"},{"era":"MACHINES AND OTHER LIFE","en":"From the twentieth century the adjective extends to calculating machines, to systems that adapt, and to hypothetical life beyond Earth.","cn":"20 世纪起，这个形容词扩展到计算机器、能自我调整的系统，以及假想的地外生命。"},{"era":"UNCERTAIN DETAILS","en":"Source uncertain (first dates): the earliest English citation is not exactly dated, and the semantic step from 'understanding' to 'clever' happened gradually rather than at one point.","cn":"来源不确定（首见年代）：最早的英语书证没有确切年代；从「理解」到「聪明」的语义转变是渐进的，而非某一点上的突变。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"Group one holds words from the same legere family that are easily confused; group two holds near-synonyms about mental ability.","cn":"第一组是同一 legere 词族里容易混淆的词；第二组是关于心智能力的近义词。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"intelligence","ipa":"/ˈɪntelɪdʒəns/","tag":"noun","definition":"The ability to learn and reason, or information gathered about an enemy; intelligent is the adjective describing the ability.","definitionCN":"学习与推理的能力，或收集到的敌情；intelligent 是描述该能力的形容词。"},{"word":"intelligible","ipa":"/ˌɪntəˈlɪdʒəbl/","tag":"can be understood","definition":"Able to be understood, said of speech or writing; it describes the message, not the mind that produced it.","definitionCN":"能被听懂的，用于言语或文字；描述信息，而非产生信息的心智。"},{"word":"intellectual","ipa":"/ˌɪntəˈlektʃuəl/","tag":"same root, different noun stem","definition":"Relating to serious thought and study; it comes from intellectus, another descendant of legere, and stresses learned reflection.","definitionCN":"与严肃思考和研究有关的；来自 intellectus，是 legere 的另一支，强调有学识的思考。"},{"word":"intelligentsia","ipa":"/ˌɪntelɪˈdʒentsiə/","tag":"Russian-shaped","definition":"The educated class taken as a group; the root is the same, but the ending came through Russian in the nineteenth century.","definitionCN":"作为一个群体的知识分子阶层；词根相同，但词尾在 19 世纪经俄语而来。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"clever","ipa":"/ˈklevə/","tag":"quick, often practical","definition":"Quick to learn and devise solutions, often with a hint of ingenuity; intelligent is broader and more neutral.","definitionCN":"学得快、办法多，常带一点机巧；intelligent 更宽、更中性。"},{"word":"smart","ipa":"/smɑːt/","tag":"informal","definition":"A conversational word for mental quickness or stylishness; it carries less scientific weight than intelligent.","definitionCN":"口语词，指反应快或衣着时髦；科学分量不及 intelligent。"},{"word":"wise","ipa":"/waɪz/","tag":"judgment from experience","definition":"Able to judge well, especially about life; wisdom adds experience and ethics, which intelligence does not require.","definitionCN":"善于判断，尤其是人生事务；智慧加上经验与伦理，而智力并不要求这些。"},{"word":"rational","ipa":"/ˈræʃənl/","tag":"following logic","definition":"Conforming to reason; it judges the process, while intelligent describes the capacity behind it.","definitionCN":"符合理性；评判过程，而 intelligent 描述背后的能力。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Normal associations: real morphemes, real collocations and real relatives, not invented rhymes.","cn":"正常联想：真实的构词成分、真实搭配与真实同族词，而非编造的顺口溜。"},"normal":[{"en":"inter 'between' + legere 'choose' = choose between signs; that is what understanding is pictured as.","cn":"inter「在……之间」+ legere「挑选」= 在多种迹象之间做选择；理解正是被这样设想的。"},{"en":"The family runs intelligence, intelligently, intelligible, unintelligent and intelligentsia.","cn":"同族词包括 intelligence、intelligently、intelligible、unintelligent 与 intelligentsia。"},{"en":"Fixed phrases mark the range: intelligent life, intelligent system, intelligent agent, intelligent design.","cn":"固定搭配标出范围：有智力的生命、智能系统、智能体、智能设计。"},{"en":"Intelligence has two senses, mental power and gathered information; the adjective serves both.","cn":"intelligence 有两义：心智能力与收集的情报；形容词两者都服务。"},{"en":"Do not confuse intelligent with intelligible: one describes a mind, the other a message.","cn":"不要把 intelligent 与 intelligible 混淆：一个描述心智，一个描述信息。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture a hand sorting many cards and laying down the three that matter.","cn":"想象一只手在众多卡片中分拣，只放下要紧的三张。"},{"en":"Picture a key that tries several locks quietly and turns at the right one.","cn":"想象一把钥匙悄悄试过几把锁，在对的那把上转动。"},{"en":"Picture a machine that changes its route when the road is blocked.","cn":"想象一台机器在道路被堵时改变路线。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"She gave an intelligent answer without any preparation.","cn":"她毫无准备却给出了聪明的回答。"},{"en":"The heating system is intelligent enough to learn the family's routine.","cn":"这套供暖系统足够智能，能学会这个家庭的作息。"},{"en":"Scientists listen for radio signals that might come from intelligent life.","cn":"科学家监听可能来自有智力生命的无线电信号。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"拆词记忆 · 非词源","text":"inter（在……之间）+ legere（挑选）——能在多条线索间挑出对的 → 聪明的、智能的","word":"intelligent"},"root":"拉丁 intelligere「理解」= inter（在……之间）+ legere「挑选、读」；intelligent 为其现在分词，字面为「能在其间挑选的」。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses follow the choosing mind outward: understanding, machine adaptation, speed, sound judgment, informative signals, a contested claim, life elsewhere, and a software agent.","cn":"八个义项顺着「会挑选的心智」向外扩展：理解、机器适应、速度、良好判断、载信息的信号、有争议的主张、地外生命，以及软件智能体。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: many clues spread out, a few chosen, one answer assembled.","cn":"核心意象：线索摊开，挑出少数几条，拼出一个答案。"},"chain":["NOTICE","SELECT","UNDERSTAND","JUDGE","DECIDE","ADAPT"],"branches":[{"senses":"01 · 03","en":"THE MIND: choosing among signs, and choosing fast.","cn":"心智：在迹象间挑选，并且挑得快。"},{"senses":"02 · 08","en":"THE MACHINE: the same loop of noticing, choosing and acting is built in silicon.","cn":"机器：同样的察觉—选择—行动循环被造进硅里。"},{"senses":"04","en":"THE PRODUCT: a good decision carries the quality of the mind that made it.","cn":"产物：好的决定带着做出它的心智的品质。"},{"senses":"05","en":"THE SIGNAL: information is intelligent when it tells you something new.","cn":"信号：能告诉你新东西的信息就是载有信息的。"},{"senses":"06 · 07","en":"THE CLAIM AND THE THRESHOLD: design argued from structure, and life defined by the ability to answer.","cn":"主张与门槛：由结构论证的设计，以及以「能否回应」定义的生命。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Intelligent is inter- plus legere plus the participle ending -ent; the prefix says 'between', the root says 'choose'.","cn":"intelligent 是 inter- 加 legere 再加分词词尾 -ent；前缀意为「在……之间」，词根意为「挑选」。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Latin legere 'to pick out, read' yields intelligere and intelligentia; English draws intelligent, intelligence, intelligible and intelligentsia from that line.","cn":"拉丁 legere「挑出、阅读」生成 intelligere 与 intelligentia；英语由此得到 intelligent、intelligence、intelligible 与 intelligentsia。"},"items":[{"word":"inter-","structure":"inter- (Latin prefix, 'between, among')","meaning":"between, among","meaningCN":"在……之间；在……之中","example":"Inter- sets the mind among competing signs.","exampleCN":"inter- 把心智放在相互竞争的迹象之间。"},{"word":"legere","structure":"legere (Latin verb, third conjugation)","meaning":"to gather, pick out, read","meaningCN":"收集；挑出；读","example":"Legere also gives collect and select.","exampleCN":"legere 也生成 collect 与 select。"},{"word":"intelligere","structure":"inter- + legere","meaning":"to choose between, discern, understand","meaningCN":"从中挑选；辨别；理解","example":"Intelligere treats understanding as selection.","exampleCN":"intelligere 把理解当作挑选。"},{"word":"-ent","structure":"-ent (present participle suffix from Latin -ens)","meaning":"doing, being","meaningCN":"正在……的；处于……的","example":"The suffix makes the verb into an adjective.","exampleCN":"这个后缀把动词变成形容词。"},{"word":"intelligent","structure":"intellig- + -ent","meaning":"understanding, able to choose well","meaningCN":"有理解力的；善于选择的","example":"An intelligent reader selects the key line.","exampleCN":"聪明的读者会挑出关键的一行。"},{"word":"intelligence","structure":"intelligentia (Latin noun)","meaning":"the power of understanding; gathered information","meaningCN":"理解的能力；收集到的情报","example":"Intelligence covers both ability and news.","exampleCN":"intelligence 兼指能力与情报。"},{"word":"intelligible","structure":"intellig- + -ible (can be)","meaning":"able to be understood","meaningCN":"可被理解的","example":"The message was barely intelligible.","exampleCN":"这条信息几乎听不清。"},{"word":"intelligently","structure":"intelligent + -ly","meaning":"in an intelligent way","meaningCN":"聪明地；智能地","example":"The system allocates power intelligently.","exampleCN":"系统智能地分配电力。"},{"word":"unintelligent","structure":"un- (not) + intelligent","meaning":"not intelligent","meaningCN":"不聪明的","example":"An unintelligent rule ignores context.","exampleCN":"不聪明的规则会忽略情境。"},{"word":"intelligentsia","structure":"intelligence + Russian -entsiya","meaning":"the educated class as a group","meaningCN":"作为群体的知识分子阶层","example":"The intelligentsia shaped public debate.","exampleCN":"知识分子群体塑造了公共讨论。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"legere","structure":"legere, legi, lectum (verb, third conjugation)","meaning":"to gather, pick out, read","meaningCN":"收集；挑出；读"},{"word":"intelligere","structure":"intelligere, intellexi, intellectum (verb, third conjugation)","meaning":"to understand, discern","meaningCN":"理解；辨别"},{"word":"intelligentia","structure":"intelligentia, intelligentiae (f., first declension)","meaning":"understanding; intelligence","meaningCN":"理解；智力"}]}},{"word":"problem-solving","ipa_uk":"/ˈprɒbləm ˌsɒlvɪŋ/","ipa_us":"/ˈprɑːbləm ˌsɑːlvɪŋ/","definition_zh":"问题解决；找出办法排除障碍、达到目标的过程或能力","definition_en":"the process or skill of finding a way around an obstacle to reach a goal","core_image":"一团缠住的线被一根根理开，直到通路出现","scene":"水管突然漏水，父亲先关阀门，再逐段检查接头，最后换上新的密封圈。The father shuts the valve, checks each joint in turn and finally fits a new seal, a calm exercise in problem-solving.","sceneCN":"这里 problem-solving 指「找出办法排除障碍的过程」（第 1 个义项：从障碍到可行方案的一串步骤）；句意为父亲先关阀、再逐段排查、最后换密封圈，冷静地把漏水问题解决掉。图中可辨识物件：水管、阀门、接头、新密封圈。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"问题解决；解题（不可数）"},{"tag":"adj.","zh":"问题解决的；用于解决问题的（作定语）"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"problem-solving skills","zh":"解决问题的能力"},{"phrase":"creative problem-solving","zh":"创造性问题解决"},{"phrase":"the problem-solving process","zh":"问题解决过程"},{"phrase":"collaborative problem-solving","zh":"协作式问题解决"},{"phrase":"a problem-solving task","zh":"问题解决任务"},{"phrase":"problem-solving ability","zh":"问题解决能力"}],"forms":[{"label":"动词","form":"problem-solve"},{"label":"三单","form":"problem-solves"},{"label":"过去式","form":"problem-solved"},{"label":"现在分词","form":"problem-solving"},{"label":"施动者名词","form":"problem-solver"},{"label":"无连字符写法","form":"problem solving"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"problem-solver","pos":"n.","zh":"善于解决问题的人"},{"word":"problem","pos":"n.","zh":"问题；难题"},{"word":"solve","pos":"v.","zh":"解决；求解"},{"word":"solution","pos":"n.","zh":"解决方案；答案"},{"word":"solvable","pos":"adj.","zh":"可解决的"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"The process of removing an obstacle","titleCN":"排除障碍的过程","definition":"the sequence of steps by which an obstacle is identified and removed","definitionCN":"识别并排除障碍的一连串步骤","example":"The father shuts the valve, checks the joints and fits a new seal.","exampleCN":"父亲关掉阀门，检查接头，再换上新的密封圈。","why":"a problem is literally something thrown in the way, so problem-solving is the work of clearing what blocks the path.","whyCN":"problem 字面上是「扔到路上的东西」，因此 problem-solving 就是清走挡路之物的工夫。"},{"no":"02","title":"Problem-solving ability","titleCN":"解决问题的能力","definition":"the capacity to find effective solutions, measured in tests and jobs","definitionCN":"找到有效解决办法的能力，在测验与工作中被衡量","example":"The interview tests problem-solving more than memory.","exampleCN":"这场面试考的是解决问题的能力，而非记忆。","why":"the same compound can name a skill because a process repeated well becomes a capacity.","whyCN":"同一复合词也能命名一种技能，因为做得好的过程会变成能力。"},{"no":"03","title":"Solving a mathematics problem","titleCN":"数学解题","definition":"working from given conditions to a required answer by valid steps","definitionCN":"从已知条件出发，用有效步骤得到所求答案","example":"The class spent an hour on problem-solving with fractions.","exampleCN":"全班花了一小时做分数解题。","why":"mathematics gives the word its clearest form: a stated obstacle, allowed moves, and a checkable end.","whyCN":"数学给了这个词最清晰的形式：明确的障碍、允许的步骤、可检验的终点。"},{"no":"04","title":"Algorithmic solving in computing","titleCN":"计算中的算法求解","definition":"designing or applying an algorithm that transforms an input into a required output","definitionCN":"设计或应用把输入变成所需输出的算法","example":"The team improved problem-solving by splitting the task into subproblems.","exampleCN":"团队把任务拆成子问题，从而改进了求解。","why":"a computer cannot improvise, so the process must be written as repeatable rules; that makes the phrase technical.","whyCN":"计算机不能临场发挥，过程必须写成可重复的规则；这使该短语成为技术用语。"},{"no":"05","title":"Troubleshooting equipment","titleCN":"设备排障","definition":"locating a fault in a machine or system and restoring it to work","definitionCN":"找出机器或系统中的故障并使其恢复运作","example":"The technician's problem-solving began with the power supply.","exampleCN":"技术员的问题解决从电源开始。","why":"engineering adds a physical object: the obstacle is a failed part, and the solution is a working machine.","whyCN":"工程加上一个物理对象：障碍是坏掉的部件，方案是运转的机器。"},{"no":"06","title":"A research topic in cognitive psychology","titleCN":"认知心理学的研究课题","definition":"the study of how people represent a goal, search a space of moves and choose a solution","definitionCN":"研究人如何表征目标、搜索可能的步骤并选择方案","example":"Problem-solving is studied through puzzles and planning tasks.","exampleCN":"问题解决通过谜题与计划任务来研究。","why":"psychologists ask what happens between reading a task and answering it, and the compound names that hidden interval.","whyCN":"心理学家追问从读到题目到给出答案之间发生了什么，这个复合词命名那段看不见的间隔。"},{"no":"07","title":"Team and organizational solving","titleCN":"团队与组织层面的问题解决","definition":"a group process for diagnosing a shared problem and agreeing on action","definitionCN":"群体诊断共同问题并就行动达成一致的过程","example":"The staff used a weekly meeting for problem-solving across departments.","exampleCN":"员工每周开会做跨部门的问题解决。","why":"when a problem belongs to no single person, the steps must be shared, and the phrase moves from a mind to a room.","whyCN":"当问题不属于任何单个人时，步骤必须共享，这个短语便从一个脑袋移到一间屋子。"},{"no":"08","title":"Resolving conflict","titleCN":"冲突调解与实际矛盾的处理","definition":"finding an arrangement that meets the interests of parties in dispute","definitionCN":"找到兼顾争议各方利益的安排","example":"The mediator's problem-solving kept the two sides talking.","exampleCN":"调解者的问题解决让双方继续谈下去。","why":"a conflict is an obstacle made of people, so the same steps apply: define the block, list options, test a solution.","whyCN":"冲突是由人构成的障碍，因此同样适用：界定阻塞、列出选项、检验方案。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Problem-solving joins Greek problēma 'a thing put forward' with Latin solvere 'to loosen'. The compound is modern English, though both halves are old. Dates are approximate.","cn":"problem-solving 把希腊 problēma「被抛到前面之物」与拉丁 solvere「松开」连在一起。复合词是现代英语构造，两半都很古老。年代为约数。"},"items":[{"era":"GREEK PROBALLEIN","en":"Problem goes back to Greek proballein 'to throw forward', from pro- 'before' plus ballein 'to throw'; a problēma was a task or riddle put in front of someone.","cn":"problem 可追溯到希腊 proballein「向前抛出」，由 pro-「在前」加 ballein「投掷」构成；problēma 就是摆在人面前的题目或谜语。"},{"era":"GREEK PROBLĒMA","en":"The noun problēma meant 'a thing put forward, a task, a question for debate'; Latin borrowed it as problema.","cn":"名词 problēma 意为「被提出之物、任务、待辩的问题」；拉丁语借作 problema。"},{"era":"LATIN SOLVERE","en":"Solvere meant 'to loosen, untie, dissolve, pay'; the metaphor of untying a knot is what solving a problem still carries.","cn":"solvere 意为「松开、解开、溶解、偿付」；「解开一个结」的比喻至今仍留在「解决问题」这一说法中。"},{"era":"ENGLISH COMPOUND","en":"Problem entered English in the sixteenth century through French; problem-solving as a fixed compound is recorded only in modern usage, especially after psychology and computing adopted it.","cn":"problem 经法语在 16 世纪进入英语；problem-solving 作为固定复合词只见于现代用法，尤其在心理学与计算领域采用之后。"},{"era":"UNCERTAIN DETAILS","en":"Source uncertain (first dates): the first use of the hyphenated compound is not precisely recorded, and Greek ballein has no reliable Latin cognate, so the Latin list covers only the solving half.","cn":"来源不确定（首见年代）：带连字符的复合词最早用法没有精确记录；希腊 ballein 没有可靠的拉丁同族词，因此拉丁词条只覆盖「解决」这一半。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"Group one holds forms and spellings that are easily confused; group two holds related activities that are not identical with solving a problem.","cn":"第一组是易混的形式与拼写；第二组是相关但并不等同于「解决问题」的活动。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"problem solving","ipa":"/ˈprɒbləm ˌsɒlvɪŋ/","tag":"spelling without hyphen","definition":"The same compound written as two words; the unhyphenated form is common when it is used as a noun.","definitionCN":"同一个复合词写成两个词；作名词时无连字符形式很常见。"},{"word":"problem-solver","ipa":"/ˈprɒbləm ˌsɒlvə/","tag":"the person","definition":"A person who solves problems; the agent noun adds -er, while problem-solving names the activity.","definitionCN":"解决问题的人；施动名词加 -er，而 problem-solving 命名活动。"},{"word":"problem","ipa":"/ˈprɒbləm/","tag":"the obstacle alone","definition":"The difficulty itself, before any solution; solving is the response to it.","definitionCN":"困难本身，尚未有方案；solving 是对它的回应。"},{"word":"solution","ipa":"/səˈluːʃn/","tag":"the product","definition":"The answer or arrangement that removes the difficulty; problem-solving is the road, solution the destination.","definitionCN":"消除困难的答案或安排；problem-solving 是路，solution 是终点。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"troubleshooting","ipa":"/ˈtrʌblʃuːtɪŋ/","tag":"fault-finding","definition":"Locating and fixing faults in equipment; it is the engineering branch of problem-solving.","definitionCN":"找出并修复设备故障；是问题解决在工程中的分支。"},{"word":"decision-making","ipa":"/dɪˈsɪʒn ˌmeɪkɪŋ/","tag":"choosing","definition":"Selecting among options; solving a problem usually includes a decision, but the two are not the same act.","definitionCN":"在选项中选择；解决问题通常包含决策，但两者不是同一动作。"},{"word":"reasoning","ipa":"/ˈriːzənɪŋ/","tag":"the inference","definition":"Moving from premises to conclusions; it is one tool used inside problem-solving.","definitionCN":"从前提走向结论；是问题解决中使用的一种工具。"},{"word":"conflict resolution","ipa":"/ˈkɒnflɪkt ˌrezəˈluːʃn/","tag":"people as the obstacle","definition":"Settling a dispute between parties; it applies problem-solving to social conflict.","definitionCN":"解决各方争议；把问题解决用于社会冲突。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Normal associations: real morphemes, real collocations and real relatives, not invented rhymes.","cn":"正常联想：真实的构词成分、真实搭配与真实同族词，而非编造的顺口溜。"},"normal":[{"en":"pro- 'before' + ballein 'throw' gives a thing thrown in your path; solvere 'untie' gives the act of clearing it.","cn":"pro-「在前」+ ballein「投掷」= 扔到你路上的东西；solvere「解开」= 清走它的动作。"},{"en":"The family runs problem, solve, solution, solvable and problem-solver.","cn":"同族词包括 problem、solve、solution、solvable 与 problem-solver。"},{"en":"Fixed phrases mark the uses: problem-solving skills, the problem-solving process, collaborative problem-solving.","cn":"固定搭配标出用法：问题解决技能、问题解决过程、协作式问题解决。"},{"en":"Mathematics and computing give the phrase its strictest form: stated input, allowed steps, checkable output.","cn":"数学与计算给出这个短语最严格的形式：明确输入、允许步骤、可检验输出。"},{"en":"A problem is the obstacle; a solution is the cleared path.","cn":"problem 是障碍，solution 是清出来的路。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture a knot in a rope, then a finger working one loop loose at a time.","cn":"想象绳上有个结，一根手指一圈圈把它挑松。"},{"en":"Picture a blocked pipe and a hand tracing the blockage joint by joint.","cn":"想象堵塞的管道，一只手一段段地摸到堵点。"},{"en":"Picture a maze where every wrong turn is marked before the right one is found.","cn":"想象一座迷宫，每个错弯都被标出之后才找到对的那条。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The course teaches problem-solving through real case studies.","cn":"这门课通过真实案例教授问题解决。"},{"en":"Good problem-solving begins with a clear statement of the goal.","cn":"好的问题解决始于对目标的清晰陈述。"},{"en":"The team's collaborative problem-solving shortened the repair by days.","cn":"团队的协作式问题解决把维修缩短了好几天。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"拆词记忆 · 非词源","text":"problem（难题）+ solving（解决）——把挡路的难题解开 → 问题解决","word":"problem-solving"},"root":"problem 源自希腊 problēma「被抛出之物」← proballein（pro- 在前 + ballein 投掷）；solving 源自拉丁 solvere「解开」。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses follow the clearing of a path: the steps, the skill, the mathematics, the algorithm, the broken machine, the hidden mental search, the shared room, and the conflict between people.","cn":"八个义项沿「清出一条路」展开：步骤、技能、数学、算法、坏掉的机器、看不见的心智搜索、共享的会议室，以及人与人之间的冲突。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a knot loosened loop by loop until the rope runs free.","cn":"核心意象：一个结被一圈圈挑松，直到绳子重新通畅。"},"chain":["GOAL","BARRIER","ANALYSE","PLAN","TRY","RESOLVE"],"branches":[{"senses":"01","en":"THE LOOP: goal, barrier, analysis, plan, trial and resolution is the minimal complete shape.","cn":"循环：目标、障碍、分析、计划、尝试与解决构成最小的完整形状。"},{"senses":"02","en":"CAPACITY: a loop repeated well becomes a skill that tests can measure.","cn":"能力：循环做得好，就成为测验可测量的技能。"},{"senses":"03 · 04","en":"FORMAL MODELS: mathematics and algorithms make the steps explicit and checkable.","cn":"形式模型：数学与算法让步骤明确且可检验。"},{"senses":"05","en":"THE BROKEN OBJECT: engineering turns the obstacle into a faulty part.","cn":"坏掉的物件：工程把障碍变成一个坏部件。"},{"senses":"06 · 07 · 08","en":"MIND, ROOM, RELATION: the same loop runs silently in a head, openly in a team, and between opposing sides.","cn":"心智、房间、关系：同一条循环在脑中无声进行，在团队中公开进行，也在对立双方之间进行。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Problem-solving is a compound of two borrowings: a Greek noun of obstruction and a Latin verb of loosening, joined by the English -ing form.","cn":"problem-solving 是两个借词的复合：一个希腊的「阻塞」名词与一个拉丁的「松开」动词，由英语 -ing 形式连接。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Latin solvere 'to loosen' supplies solve, solution, solvable and solvent; Greek problēma supplies problem. The two halves come from different languages and must not be forced into one root.","cn":"拉丁 solvere「松开」提供 solve、solution、solvable 与 solvent；希腊 problēma 提供 problem。两半来自不同语言，不能强行并成一个词根。"},"items":[{"word":"pro-","structure":"pro- (Greek prefix, 'before, forward')","meaning":"before, in front","meaningCN":"在前；向前","example":"Pro- places the task in front of the solver.","exampleCN":"pro- 把任务摆在解题者面前。"},{"word":"ballein","structure":"ballein (Greek verb, 'to throw')","meaning":"to throw, put","meaningCN":"投掷；放置","example":"Ballein also appears in ballistic.","exampleCN":"ballein 也出现在 ballistic 中。"},{"word":"problēma","structure":"pro- + ballein + -ma (result noun)","meaning":"a thing put forward, a task","meaningCN":"被提出之物；任务","example":"Problēma entered Latin as problema.","exampleCN":"problēma 以 problema 进入拉丁语。"},{"word":"solvere","structure":"solvere (Latin verb, third conjugation)","meaning":"to loosen, untie, dissolve","meaningCN":"松开；解开；溶解","example":"Solvere is the source of solve and solution.","exampleCN":"solvere 是 solve 与 solution 的来源。"},{"word":"-ing","structure":"-ing (English verbal noun suffix)","meaning":"the act or process of","meaningCN":"……的动作或过程","example":"The suffix turns the verb solve into the activity of solving.","exampleCN":"这个后缀把动词 solve 变成「解决」这项活动。"},{"word":"problem","structure":"Greek problēma through Latin problema","meaning":"a difficulty to be dealt with","meaningCN":"需要处理的困难","example":"The problem was a cracked joint.","exampleCN":"问题是一个裂开的接头。"},{"word":"solve","structure":"solvere + English verb use","meaning":"to find the answer to","meaningCN":"解决；求解","example":"She solved the puzzle in a minute.","exampleCN":"她一分钟就解开了谜题。"},{"word":"solution","structure":"solut- + -ion","meaning":"the act or result of loosening","meaningCN":"解开的行为或结果","example":"The solution was a new seal.","exampleCN":"解决办法是换一个新密封圈。"},{"word":"solvable","structure":"solve + -able","meaning":"able to be solved","meaningCN":"可解决的","example":"Not every dispute is solvable at once.","exampleCN":"并非每场争议都能立刻解决。"},{"word":"problem-solver","structure":"problem + solver (one who solves)","meaning":"a person skilled at finding solutions","meaningCN":"善于找到方案的人","example":"A good problem-solver asks what the real goal is.","exampleCN":"善于解决问题的人会先问真正的目标是什么。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"solvere","structure":"solvere, solvi, solutum (verb, third conjugation)","meaning":"to loosen, untie, dissolve","meaningCN":"松开；解开；溶解"},{"word":"solutio","structure":"solutio, solutionis (f., third declension)","meaning":"a loosening; an answer","meaningCN":"解开；解答"},{"word":"solutus","structure":"solutus, soluta, solutum (participle)","meaning":"loosened, set free","meaningCN":"已松开的；被释放的"}]}},{"word":"navigation","ipa_uk":"/ˌnævɪˈɡeɪʃn/","ipa_us":"/ˌnævɪˈɡeɪʃn/","definition_zh":"导航；航行；确定位置并找到路线的过程，也指网页或系统的导览结构","definition_en":"the process of finding a position and a route, the act of sailing, or the menu structure that guides users through a site","core_image":"船在无岸的海上凭星位与海图校正方向，一步步靠近港口","scene":"浓雾里看不见岸，船长靠罗盘方位和灯塔的间隔校正航向，慢慢贴近港口。With no shore in sight, the captain corrects the course by compass bearing and the spacing of lighthouses, a patient art of navigation.","sceneCN":"这里 navigation 指「确定位置并找到航线的过程」（第 2 个义项：靠方位与地标不断校正）；句意为浓雾中看不见岸，船长凭罗盘与灯塔间距修正航向，慢慢驶近港口。图中可辨识物件：罗盘、海图、灯塔、雾中的船首。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"航行；导航；导览结构（不可数）"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"marine navigation","zh":"海上导航"},{"phrase":"air navigation","zh":"空中导航"},{"phrase":"satellite navigation","zh":"卫星导航"},{"phrase":"a navigation system","zh":"导航系统"},{"phrase":"inland navigation","zh":"内河航运"},{"phrase":"a navigation channel","zh":"航道"}],"forms":[{"label":"动词","form":"navigate"},{"label":"三单","form":"navigates"},{"label":"过去式","form":"navigated"},{"label":"现在分词","form":"navigating"},{"label":"施动者名词","form":"navigator"},{"label":"形容词","form":"navigational"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"navigate","pos":"v.","zh":"导航；航行；找到路线"},{"word":"navigator","pos":"n.","zh":"导航员；领航员"},{"word":"navigational","pos":"adj.","zh":"导航的"},{"word":"navigable","pos":"adj.","zh":"可航行的"},{"word":"navigability","pos":"n.","zh":"可航性"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Sailing on water","titleCN":"在水上航行","definition":"the act of sailing or steering a vessel along a route","definitionCN":"驾驶船只沿航线行驶的行为","example":"Navigation on the river began before roads were built.","exampleCN":"这条路还没有修好之前，河上航行就已开始。","why":"navis 'ship' plus agere 'drive' is literally ship-driving, so the oldest sense is the movement of a hull through water.","whyCN":"navis「船」加 agere「驾驶」，字面就是「驾船」；最古老的含义正是船体在水上的移动。"},{"no":"02","title":"Position fixing and route finding","titleCN":"定位与找路","definition":"the process of determining where one is and which course leads to the destination","definitionCN":"确定自己在哪里、哪条航线通向目的地的过程","example":"The captain corrected the course by compass and lighthouses.","exampleCN":"船长凭罗盘与灯塔校正了航向。","why":"the core of navigation is two questions, where am I and where next; every instrument serves one of them.","whyCN":"导航的核心是两个问题：我在哪里、下一步往哪；每件仪器都在为其中之一服务。"},{"no":"03","title":"Website navigation","titleCN":"网页的导览结构","definition":"the menus, links and layout that let a user move through a site or app","definitionCN":"让用户在网站或应用中移动的菜单、链接与布局","example":"Clear navigation kept visitors from leaving the site.","exampleCN":"清晰的导航让访客没有离开网站。","why":"a user is also a traveller: the menu is a chart of the site, and a bad chart produces the digital equivalent of being lost.","whyCN":"用户也是行者：菜单是网站的海图，海图糟糕就会产生数字版的迷路。"},{"no":"04","title":"Animal navigation","titleCN":"动物的导航能力","definition":"the ability of animals to orient and travel toward a goal over long distances","definitionCN":"动物辨向并长距离前往目标的能力","example":"Monarch butterflies manage navigation across a continent.","exampleCN":"帝王蝶能完成跨大陆的导航。","why":"biology uses the word because the same two questions apply without instruments: where am I, and which way is home.","whyCN":"生物学使用这个词，因为同样两个问题在没有仪器时也成立：我在哪，家在哪边。"},{"no":"05","title":"Air and space navigation","titleCN":"航空与航天导航","definition":"plotting and correcting a course through the air or in orbit","definitionCN":"在空中或轨道上规划并修正航线","example":"Space navigation relies on signals from ground stations.","exampleCN":"航天导航依赖地面站信号。","why":"as the medium changes, the instruments change, but the loop of fix, compare and correct remains.","whyCN":"介质改变，仪器随之改变，但「定位、比对、修正」的循环不变。"},{"no":"06","title":"Navigation technology","titleCN":"导航技术与设备","definition":"the instruments and systems that support positioning and routing","definitionCN":"支持定位与选路的仪器与系统","example":"The app's navigation depends on four satellites.","exampleCN":"这款应用的导航依赖四颗卫星。","why":"metonymy lets the activity name its tools, so navigation can mean the equipment that makes it possible.","whyCN":"转喻让活动命名其工具，因此 navigation 也可以指使活动得以进行的设备。"},{"no":"07","title":"Inland waterway transport","titleCN":"内河航运","definition":"the movement of goods or people on rivers and canals","definitionCN":"在河流与运河上运送货物或人员","example":"Inland navigation carries coal along the canal.","exampleCN":"内河航运沿运河运送煤炭。","why":"the commercial sense narrows the old sailing sense to a transport mode counted in tonnage.","whyCN":"商业义把古老的航行义收窄为一种以吨位计量的运输方式。"},{"no":"08","title":"The science or skill of navigating","titleCN":"导航学与导航技能","definition":"the body of knowledge and technique required to find and follow a route","definitionCN":"寻找并沿路线行进所需的知识与技术总体","example":"Navigation was taught as a mathematical art.","exampleCN":"导航曾被当作一门数学技艺来教授。","why":"a practice that can be taught becomes a discipline, and the noun shifts from doing to knowing how.","whyCN":"可以教授的实践会成为一门学问，名词便从「做」转向「知道怎么做」。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Navigation comes from Latin navigatio, from navigare 'to sail', itself navis 'ship' plus agere 'to drive'. It entered English in the sixteenth century. Dates are approximate.","cn":"navigation 来自拉丁 navigatio，源自动词 navigare「航行」，而 navigare 由 navis「船」加 agere「驾驶」构成。它在 16 世纪进入英语。年代为约数。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN NAVIS","en":"Navis meant 'ship, boat'; it belongs to an old Indo-European word for a vessel and survives in navy and in naval.","cn":"navis 意为「船、舟」；它属于古老的印欧语「船」词，留在 navy 与 naval 中。"},{"era":"LATIN AGERE","en":"Agere meant 'to drive, lead, do'; it is the verb behind agent, act and agenda.","cn":"agere 意为「驾驶、引领、做」；它是 agent、act 与 agenda 背后的动词。"},{"era":"LATIN NAVIGARE","en":"Navis plus agere produced navigare, 'to sail, steer a ship'; the compound is literal, not metaphorical.","cn":"navis 加 agere 构成 navigare「航行、驾船」；这个复合是字面的，不是比喻。"},{"era":"LATIN NAVIGATIO","en":"The noun navigatio 'a sailing, a voyage' supplied the English word through French in the sixteenth century.","cn":"名词 navigatio「航行、航程」在 16 世纪经法语提供英语词形。"},{"era":"COMPUTING AND BIOLOGY","en":"In the twentieth century the word extended to animal orientation and to the menus that guide users through software, both treating travel as a path toward a goal.","cn":"20 世纪，这个词扩展到动物辨向，以及引导用户使用软件的菜单；两者都把行进当作通往目标的路径。"},{"era":"UNCERTAIN DETAILS","en":"Source uncertain (first dates): the earliest English citation is not exactly fixed, and the pre-Indo-European origin of navis is reconstructed rather than attested.","cn":"来源不确定（首见年代）：最早的英语书证没有确切年代；navis 在印欧语之前的来源属于重构，而非直接书证。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"Group one holds forms from the same navis plus agere family; group two holds related travel and guidance concepts.","cn":"第一组是同一 navis 加 agere 词族的形式；第二组是相关的行进与引导概念。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"navigational","ipa":"/ˌnævɪˈɡeɪʃənl/","tag":"adjective","definition":"Relating to navigation; it must modify a noun such as aid or system, while navigation names the activity.","definitionCN":"与导航有关的；必须修饰 aid 或 system 之类名词，而 navigation 命名活动。"},{"word":"navigable","ipa":"/ˈnævɪɡəbl/","tag":"can be sailed","definition":"Describing water or an aircraft that can be navigated; it judges the route, not the act.","definitionCN":"描述可通航的水域或可驾驶的航空器；评判路线，而非动作。"},{"word":"navigator","ipa":"/ˈnævɪɡeɪtə/","tag":"the person","definition":"A person who navigates; the -or suffix names the agent, navigation the activity.","definitionCN":"导航的人；-or 后缀命名施动者，navigation 命名活动。"},{"word":"navy","ipa":"/ˈneɪvi/","tag":"same root, different sense","definition":"A country's fleet; it comes from navis too, but names the ships as an institution, not the act of steering them.","definitionCN":"一个国家的舰队；同样来自 navis，但把船只作为建制来命名，而非驾驶动作。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"piloting","ipa":"/ˈpaɪlətɪŋ/","tag":"local guidance","definition":"Guiding a vessel through a channel by landmarks; it is one branch of navigation, often close to shore.","definitionCN":"凭地标引导船只通过航道；是导航的一支，常发生在近岸。"},{"word":"wayfinding","ipa":"/ˈweɪfaɪndɪŋ/","tag":"human-scale","definition":"Finding one's way through a building or city, often by signs; navigation is broader and includes instruments.","definitionCN":"在建筑或城市中认路，常靠标识；navigation 更宽，包含仪器。"},{"word":"seafaring","ipa":"/ˈsiːfeərɪŋ/","tag":"the occupation","definition":"Travelling and working at sea; it names a way of life, while navigation names the method.","definitionCN":"在海上旅行与劳作；命名一种生活方式，而 navigation 命名方法。"},{"word":"routing","ipa":"/ˈruːtɪŋ/","tag":"path selection","definition":"Choosing the path for data or traffic; it is the technical descendant of route finding.","definitionCN":"为数据或交通选择路径；是找路的技术后裔。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Normal associations: real morphemes, real collocations and real relatives, not invented rhymes.","cn":"正常联想：真实的构词成分、真实搭配与真实同族词，而非编造的顺口溜。"},"normal":[{"en":"navis 'ship' + agere 'drive' = drive a ship; the same two roots appear in navy and agent.","cn":"navis「船」+ agere「驾驶」= 驾船；同两个词根也出现在 navy 与 agent 中。"},{"en":"The family runs navigate, navigator, navigational, navigable and navigability.","cn":"同族词包括 navigate、navigator、navigational、navigable 与 navigability。"},{"en":"Fixed phrases mark the senses: marine navigation, satellite navigation, a navigation system, inland navigation.","cn":"固定搭配标出各义项：海上导航、卫星导航、导航系统、内河航运。"},{"en":"Navigation answers two questions: where am I, and which way next.","cn":"导航回答两个问题：我在哪里，下一步往哪。"},{"en":"Website navigation borrows the sailor's chart: a menu is a map of pages.","cn":"网页导航借用水手的海图：菜单就是页面的地图。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture a small boat with no land in sight, correcting its line by a single star.","cn":"想象一条看不见陆地的小船，靠一颗星修正航线。"},{"en":"Picture a menu bar as a row of harbour lights, each leading to one page.","cn":"想象菜单栏像一排港口灯，每盏通向一个页面。"},{"en":"Picture a monarch butterfly that has never seen the destination and still arrives.","cn":"想象一只从未见过目的地的帝王蝶，仍然抵达。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"Satellite navigation has replaced paper charts on many ships.","cn":"卫星导航在许多船上取代了纸质海图。"},{"en":"The site's navigation was redesigned so that new users could find the help page.","cn":"网站导航经过重新设计，新用户能找到帮助页面。"},{"en":"Inland navigation carries more freight than the nearby roads.","cn":"内河航运运送的货物比附近公路更多。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"拆词记忆 · 非词源","text":"navy（船队）+ action（行动）——驾船找路的行动 → 航行、导航","word":"navigation"},"root":"拉丁 navigatio「航行」← navigare「驾船」= navis（船）+ agere（驾驶）；与 navy、agent 同根。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses keep the same loop of fix, compare and correct, but change the traveller: a hull, a walker, a mouse pointer, a butterfly, a spacecraft, an app, a barge and a student of the art.","cn":"八个义项保持「定位、比对、修正」的同一循环，只更换行者：船体、行人、鼠标指针、蝴蝶、航天器、应用、驳船，以及学习这门技艺的人。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: no shore in sight, one bearing checked again and again until the harbour appears.","cn":"核心意象：看不见岸，反复校验一个方位，直到港口出现。"},"chain":["POSITION","COURSE","BEARING","CORRECTION","ROUTE","ARRIVAL"],"branches":[{"senses":"01 · 08","en":"THE ART: ship-driving as a practice and as a teachable body of knowledge.","cn":"技艺：驾船既是一项实践，也是一套可教授的知识。"},{"senses":"02 · 05","en":"THE LOOP: fix, compare, correct, whether by star, compass or ground signal.","cn":"循环：定位、比对、修正，不论靠星辰、罗盘还是地面信号。"},{"senses":"03 · 06","en":"NEW MEDIA: menus and satellite systems inherit the same chart and the same lost user.","cn":"新媒介：菜单与卫星系统继承同样的海图与同样会迷路的使用者。"},{"senses":"04","en":"WITHOUT INSTRUMENTS: the butterfly answers the two questions with senses only.","cn":"无仪器：蝴蝶只靠感官回答那两个问题。"},{"senses":"07","en":"COMMERCE: the old voyage becomes a transport mode measured in tonnage.","cn":"商业：古老的航程变成以吨位计量的运输方式。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Navigation is a Latin compound noun: navis 'ship' plus agere 'drive', then -atio. Both roots have large English families of their own.","cn":"navigation 是拉丁复合名词：navis「船」加 agere「驾驶」，再加 -atio。两个词根在英语中各自都有大词族。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Latin navis 'ship' and agere 'drive' form navigare and navigatio; English draws navigate, navigator, navigable, navigational and navy from the same stock.","cn":"拉丁 navis「船」与 agere「驾驶」构成 navigare 与 navigatio；英语由此得到 navigate、navigator、navigable、navigational 与 navy。"},"items":[{"word":"navis","structure":"navis, navis (f., third declension)","meaning":"ship, boat","meaningCN":"船；舟","example":"Navis is the source of navy and naval.","exampleCN":"navis 是 navy 与 naval 的来源。"},{"word":"agere","structure":"agere, egi, actum (Latin verb, third conjugation)","meaning":"to drive, lead, do","meaningCN":"驾驶；引领；做","example":"Agere also gives agent and agenda.","exampleCN":"agere 也生成 agent 与 agenda。"},{"word":"navigare","structure":"navis + agere","meaning":"to sail, steer a ship","meaningCN":"航行；驾船","example":"Navigare is literal ship-driving.","exampleCN":"navigare 字面上就是驾船。"},{"word":"-atio","structure":"-atio (Latin noun suffix)","meaning":"the act or process of","meaningCN":"……的动作或过程","example":"Navigare plus -atio gives navigatio.","exampleCN":"navigare 加 -atio 构成 navigatio。"},{"word":"navigation","structure":"navigatio through French navigation","meaning":"the act of sailing or finding a route","meaningCN":"航行或找路的行为","example":"Navigation requires a fix and a course.","exampleCN":"导航需要一个定位与一条航线。"},{"word":"navigate","structure":"navigare + English verb ending","meaning":"to find one's way","meaningCN":"导航；找到路线","example":"She navigated the narrow channel.","exampleCN":"她驾船穿过狭窄的航道。"},{"word":"navigator","structure":"navigate + -or","meaning":"one who navigates","meaningCN":"导航员；领航员","example":"The navigator plotted the next leg.","exampleCN":"领航员标出了下一段航程。"},{"word":"navigable","structure":"navigate + -able","meaning":"able to be sailed or steered","meaningCN":"可通航的；可驾驶的","example":"The upper river is not navigable in winter.","exampleCN":"上游河道冬季不能通航。"},{"word":"navigational","structure":"navigation + -al","meaning":"relating to navigation","meaningCN":"与导航有关的","example":"Navigational aids were placed along the coast.","exampleCN":"沿海设置了一些导航设施。"},{"word":"navy","structure":"navis through Old French navie","meaning":"a fleet, especially a war fleet","meaningCN":"舰队，尤指海军","example":"The navy patrols the strait.","exampleCN":"海军在海峡巡逻。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"navis","structure":"navis, navis (f., third declension)","meaning":"ship, boat","meaningCN":"船；舟"},{"word":"agere","structure":"agere, egi, actum (verb, third conjugation)","meaning":"to drive, lead","meaningCN":"驾驶；引领"},{"word":"navigare","structure":"navigare, navigavi, navigatum (verb, first conjugation)","meaning":"to sail, steer","meaningCN":"航行；驾船"},{"word":"navigatio","structure":"navigatio, navigationis (f., third declension)","meaning":"a sailing, a voyage","meaningCN":"航行；航程"}]}},{"word":"navigational","ipa_uk":"/ˌnævɪˈɡeɪʃənl/","ipa_us":"/ˌnævɪˈɡeɪʃənl/","definition_zh":"导航的；与航行、定位或路线引导有关的","definition_en":"relating to navigation, to the instruments used for it, or to the guidance of a route","core_image":"海图上叠着罗盘刻度与航迹线，构成一套导航用的标记","scene":"驾驶舱里，飞行员把几个定位点输入仪表，屏幕随即画出到下一站的航线。In the cockpit the pilot enters several fixes and the screen draws the route to the next stop, a routine navigational task.","sceneCN":"这里 navigational 指「与导航有关的」（第 1 个义项：属于航行与找路这件事）；句意为飞行员输入几个定位点，屏幕画出到下一站的航线。图中可辨识物件：驾驶舱、仪表屏、定位点、航线。","pos":[{"tag":"adj.","zh":"导航的；航行定位的"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"navigational aids","zh":"导航设施"},{"phrase":"a navigational system","zh":"导航系统"},{"phrase":"a navigational error","zh":"导航误差"},{"phrase":"navigational charts","zh":"导航海图"},{"phrase":"navigational skills","zh":"导航技能"},{"phrase":"navigational equipment","zh":"导航设备"}],"forms":[{"label":"名词","form":"navigation"},{"label":"动词","form":"navigate"},{"label":"施动者名词","form":"navigator"},{"label":"形容词（可通航的）","form":"navigable"},{"label":"名词（可航性）","form":"navigability"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"navigation","pos":"n.","zh":"航行；导航"},{"word":"navigate","pos":"v.","zh":"导航；航行"},{"word":"navigator","pos":"n.","zh":"导航员；领航员"},{"word":"navigable","pos":"adj.","zh":"可通航的"},{"word":"navigability","pos":"n.","zh":"可航性"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Relating to navigation","titleCN":"与导航有关的","definition":"concerning the finding of position and route","definitionCN":"关乎确定位置与路线","example":"The pilot performs a routine navigational task.","exampleCN":"飞行员完成一项常规导航任务。","why":"the adjective simply attaches -al 'relating to' to navigation, so it marks anything that belongs to the work of finding a way.","whyCN":"这个形容词就是在 navigation 后加 -al「与……有关」，标记一切属于「找路」工作的东西。"},{"no":"02","title":"Of navigational instruments","titleCN":"导航仪器的","definition":"describing devices used to fix position or steer","definitionCN":"描述用于定位或操舵的装置","example":"A navigational error came from a faulty gyroscope.","exampleCN":"一次导航误差来自一个故障陀螺仪。","why":"instruments are named by the job they serve, so the adjective works as a label on a cockpit panel.","whyCN":"仪器以它服务的任务来命名，因此这个形容词就是驾驶舱面板上的标签。"},{"no":"03","title":"For sea travel","titleCN":"航海用途的","definition":"used for sailing or for charts and lights that guide ships","definitionCN":"用于航行，或用于引导船只的海图与灯标","example":"Navigational charts mark every shoal.","exampleCN":"航海图上标出了每一处浅滩。","why":"the oldest setting still dominates the adjective: most navigational aids were built for hulls, not for hikers.","whyCN":"最古老的场景仍主导这个形容词：多数导航设施是为船体而非行人建造的。"},{"no":"04","title":"Of animal orientation","titleCN":"动物辨向的","definition":"relating to the senses and cues animals use to find a route","definitionCN":"与动物寻找路线所用的感官与线索有关","example":"Researchers study the navigational cues of migrating birds.","exampleCN":"研究者研究候鸟的导航线索。","why":"biology borrows the adjective when it wants to separate the sensory equipment from the journey itself.","whyCN":"生物学借用这个形容词，是为了把感官装备与旅程本身分开。"},{"no":"05","title":"Of website or interface structure","titleCN":"网页或界面导航的","definition":"relating to menus, links and layout that guide a user","definitionCN":"与引导用户的菜单、链接及布局有关","example":"The navigational menu sits at the top of every page.","exampleCN":"导航菜单位于每个页面的顶部。","why":"an interface is a space to be crossed, so the same adjective labels the signs that keep a user from getting lost.","whyCN":"界面是一片要穿越的空间，因此同一个形容词被用来标记防止用户迷路的路标。"},{"no":"06","title":"Of space navigation","titleCN":"航天导航的","definition":"relating to plotting and correcting a course in space","definitionCN":"与在太空中规划并修正航线有关","example":"Navigational software adjusts the probe's path.","exampleCN":"导航软件调整探测器的路径。","why":"the medium is new but the adjective travels unchanged, because the loop of fix and correct is the same.","whyCN":"介质是新的，形容词却原样迁移，因为定位与修正的循环没有变。"},{"no":"07","title":"Serving as an aid","titleCN":"辅助导航的","definition":"describing a device, mark or signal that helps someone find the way","definitionCN":"描述帮助人找到方向的装置、标记或信号","example":"Lighthouse keepers maintained the navigational lights.","exampleCN":"灯塔看守人维护导航灯。","why":"navigational aids is the standard phrase because the adjective marks function: the light exists to serve navigation.","whyCN":"「导航设施」这一固定说法成立，是因为形容词标记功能：那盏灯存在就是为了服务导航。"},{"no":"08","title":"Figurative: directional planning","titleCN":"比喻用法：方向性的规划","definition":"used figuratively for information or steps that keep a process on course","definitionCN":"比喻指使某项进程不偏离方向的信息或步骤","example":"The report offered navigational markers for the reform.","exampleCN":"这份报告为改革提供了方向标记。","why":"when a project is pictured as a voyage, any guidance becomes navigational, and the metaphor is easy to extend.","whyCN":"当项目被设想为一次航行时，任何指引都成了导航性的，这个比喻很容易延伸。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Navigational is navigation plus the adjective suffix -al; navigation itself comes from Latin navigare, navis 'ship' plus agere 'drive'. Dates are approximate.","cn":"navigational 是 navigation 加形容词后缀 -al；navigation 本身来自拉丁 navigare，即 navis「船」加 agere「驾驶」。年代为约数。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN NAVIGARE","en":"Navigare 'to sail, steer a ship' combines navis 'ship' with agere 'to drive'.","cn":"navigare「航行、驾船」把 navis「船」与 agere「驾驶」结合。"},{"era":"LATIN NAVIGATIO","en":"Navigatio 'a sailing, a voyage' is the noun of the action, built with the suffix -atio.","cn":"navigatio「航行、航程」是动作名词，由后缀 -atio 构成。"},{"era":"ENGLISH NAVIGATION","en":"English navigation entered in the sixteenth century through French; the adjective navigational followed later, when instruments and charts needed a label.","cn":"英语 navigation 在 16 世纪经法语进入；形容词 navigational 较晚出现，当时仪器与海图需要一个标签。"},{"era":"-AL SUFFIX","en":"The suffix -al, from Latin -alis 'relating to', is added to the noun stem to make the adjective.","cn":"后缀 -al 源自拉丁 -alis「与……有关」，加在名词词干后构成形容词。"},{"era":"UNCERTAIN DETAILS","en":"Source uncertain (first dates): the first English use of navigational is not precisely dated, and it may have been formed independently in technical writing rather than borrowed whole.","cn":"来源不确定（首见年代）：navigational 的最早英语用法没有确切年代；它可能是在技术写作中独立构成，而非整体借入。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"Group one holds words from the same navigation family with different grammar; group two holds adjectives and ideas about guidance that do not mean the same thing.","cn":"第一组是同一 navigation 词族、语法角色不同的词；第二组是关于引导但不完全同义的形容词与概念。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"navigation","ipa":"/ˌnævɪˈɡeɪʃn/","tag":"the noun","definition":"The activity or system itself; navigational is the adjective that must attach to a noun such as aid or error.","definitionCN":"活动或系统本身；navigational 是必须依附 aid、error 等名词的形容词。"},{"word":"navigable","ipa":"/ˈnævɪɡəbl/","tag":"-able, not -al","definition":"Able to be sailed or steered; it describes the route's capacity, not its relation to navigation.","definitionCN":"可通航、可驾驶的；描述路线的能力，而非与导航的关系。"},{"word":"navigator","ipa":"/ˈnævɪɡeɪtə/","tag":"the person","definition":"One who navigates; the -or ending names an agent, while -al names a relation.","definitionCN":"导航的人；-or 结尾命名施动者，-al 命名关系。"},{"word":"navigability","ipa":"/ˌnævɪɡəˈbɪləti/","tag":"the abstract noun","definition":"The quality of being navigable; it belongs to the route, not to the instrument.","definitionCN":"可通航的性质；属于路线，而非仪器。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"directional","ipa":"/dəˈrekʃənl/","tag":"pointing, not guiding","definition":"Relating to direction or showing which way; it says nothing about fixing a position.","definitionCN":"与方向有关或指示方向；不涉及确定位置。"},{"word":"positional","ipa":"/pəˈzɪʃənl/","tag":"place only","definition":"Relating to position; it covers one half of navigation, without the route.","definitionCN":"与位置有关；只覆盖导航的一半，不含路线。"},{"word":"routing","ipa":"/ˈruːtɪŋ/","tag":"the path choice","definition":"The selection of a path, especially for data; it is a component of navigation, not the whole adjective's scope.","definitionCN":"路径选择，尤用于数据；是导航的一个组成部分，不等于该形容词的全部范围。"},{"word":"guiding","ipa":"/ˈɡaɪdɪŋ/","tag":"general help","definition":"Showing someone the way; broader and warmer than navigational, which is technical.","definitionCN":"给人指路；比技术性的 navigational 更宽、更亲切。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Normal associations: real morphemes, real collocations and real relatives, not invented rhymes.","cn":"正常联想：真实的构词成分、真实搭配与真实同族词，而非编造的顺口溜。"},"normal":[{"en":"navigation + -al: the suffix turns the activity into a description of anything that serves it.","cn":"navigation + -al：后缀把活动变成对一切服务该活动之物的描述。"},{"en":"The family runs navigation, navigate, navigator, navigable and navigability.","cn":"同族词包括 navigation、navigate、navigator、navigable 与 navigability。"},{"en":"Fixed phrases are mostly compounds with aids, charts, systems and errors.","cn":"固定搭配多与「设施、海图、系统、误差」构成复合词。"},{"en":"The adjective almost never stands alone; ask what noun it is marking.","cn":"这个形容词几乎从不单独使用；要问它标记的是哪个名词。"},{"en":"Navigational error is a standard phrase because instruments fail in characteristic ways.","cn":"「导航误差」是标准说法，因为仪器会以特定方式失灵。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture a chart covered with pencil lines, each one a corrected guess.","cn":"想象一张画满铅笔线的海图，每条线都是一次被修正的猜测。"},{"en":"Picture a row of lights on a coast, each saying the same thing: this way is safe.","cn":"想象海岸上一排灯，每盏都在说同一句话：这边安全。"},{"en":"Picture a menu bar as a compass rose laid flat on a screen.","cn":"想象菜单栏像一枚平放在屏幕上的罗盘玫瑰。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The crew checked every navigational aid before the fog closed in.","cn":"雾气合拢之前，船员检查了每一件导航设施。"},{"en":"A navigational error of two degrees sent the ship off course.","cn":"两度的导航误差使船偏离了航线。"},{"en":"The app's navigational design was tested with first-time users.","cn":"这款应用的导航设计以新用户进行了测试。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"拆词记忆 · 非词源","text":"navigation（导航）+ al（……的）——属于导航这件事的 → 导航的","word":"navigational"},"root":"navigation（拉丁 navigatio，navis 船 + agere 驾驶）+ 形容词后缀 -al（与……有关）。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses show the adjective labelling instruments, sea travel, animal senses, menus, spacecraft, aids, and finally a metaphor for guidance in general.","cn":"八个义项显示这个形容词依次标记仪器、海上航行、动物感官、菜单、航天器、助航设施，最后是泛指引导的比喻。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a chart overlaid with compass marks and a plotted track, all serving one voyage.","cn":"核心意象：一张叠着罗盘刻度与航迹线的海图，全都为同一次航行服务。"},"chain":["SEA","INSTRUMENT","FIX","CHART","GUIDE","ARRIVE"],"branches":[{"senses":"01 · 03","en":"THE SEA: the oldest setting supplies the charts, lights and the word itself.","cn":"海：最古老的场景提供海图、灯标与这个词本身。"},{"senses":"02 · 07","en":"INSTRUMENTS AND AIDS: devices are named by the job they serve.","cn":"仪器与助航：装置按所服务的任务命名。"},{"senses":"04","en":"ANIMALS: senses replace instruments but the questions stay the same.","cn":"动物：感官替代仪器，问题却不变。"},{"senses":"05 · 06","en":"NEW SPACES: menus and orbits both need a fix and a plotted line.","cn":"新空间：菜单与轨道都需要定位与一条画出的线。"},{"senses":"08","en":"METAPHOR: any guidance for a process can be called navigational.","cn":"比喻：对任何进程的引导都可称作导航性的。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Navigational is navigation plus -al; it adds no new root, only a relational suffix to a Latin compound already made of ship and drive.","cn":"navigational 是 navigation 加 -al；没有新增词根，只是给一个已由「船」与「驾驶」构成的拉丁复合词加上关系后缀。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Latin navis 'ship' and agere 'drive' give navigare and navigatio; English adds -al to form navigational, beside navigate, navigator and navigable.","cn":"拉丁 navis「船」与 agere「驾驶」生成 navigare 与 navigatio；英语加 -al 构成 navigational，与 navigate、navigator、navigable 并列。"},"items":[{"word":"navis","structure":"navis (Latin noun, third declension)","meaning":"ship, boat","meaningCN":"船；舟","example":"Navis is the first half of the compound.","exampleCN":"navis 是复合词的前一半。"},{"word":"agere","structure":"agere (Latin verb)","meaning":"to drive, steer","meaningCN":"驾驶；操舵","example":"Agere supplies the motion in navigation.","exampleCN":"agere 为 navigation 提供「动」的含义。"},{"word":"navigare","structure":"navis + agere","meaning":"to sail, steer a ship","meaningCN":"航行；驾船","example":"Navigare is the verb behind the noun.","exampleCN":"navigare 是名词背后的动词。"},{"word":"navigatio","structure":"navigare + -atio","meaning":"a sailing, a voyage","meaningCN":"航行；航程","example":"Navigatio became English navigation.","exampleCN":"navigatio 成为英语 navigation。"},{"word":"-al","structure":"-al (adjective suffix from Latin -alis)","meaning":"relating to","meaningCN":"与……有关的","example":"The suffix marks relation, not agency or capacity.","exampleCN":"这个后缀标记关系，而非施动或能力。"},{"word":"navigational","structure":"navigation + -al","meaning":"relating to navigation","meaningCN":"与导航有关的","example":"Navigational charts are revised yearly.","exampleCN":"导航海图每年修订。"},{"word":"navigate","structure":"navigare + English verb form","meaning":"to find and follow a route","meaningCN":"找到并沿着路线行进","example":"They navigated by the stars.","exampleCN":"他们靠星辰导航。"},{"word":"navigator","structure":"navigate + -or","meaning":"one who navigates","meaningCN":"导航员","example":"The navigator kept the log.","exampleCN":"领航员负责记录航行日志。"},{"word":"navigable","structure":"navigate + -able","meaning":"able to be sailed","meaningCN":"可通航的","example":"The canal is navigable all year.","exampleCN":"这条运河全年可通航。"},{"word":"navigation","structure":"navigatio through French","meaning":"the act of navigating","meaningCN":"导航的行为","example":"Navigation depends on a reliable fix.","exampleCN":"导航依赖可靠的定位。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"navis","structure":"navis, navis (f., third declension)","meaning":"ship","meaningCN":"船"},{"word":"agere","structure":"agere, egi, actum (verb, third conjugation)","meaning":"to drive, steer","meaningCN":"驾驶；操舵"},{"word":"navigare","structure":"navigare, navigavi, navigatum (verb, first conjugation)","meaning":"to sail","meaningCN":"航行"},{"word":"navigatio","structure":"navigatio, navigationis (f., third declension)","meaning":"a voyage","meaningCN":"航程"}]}},{"word":"echolocation","ipa_uk":"/ˌekəʊləʊˈkeɪʃn/","ipa_us":"/ˌekoʊloʊˈkeɪʃn/","definition_zh":"回声定位；生物或设备发出声波并依据回声判断方位与距离的能力","definition_en":"the ability to locate objects by emitting sound and interpreting the returning echoes","core_image":"黑暗中一束声脉冲撞到飞虫折返，蝙蝠凭返回的延迟描出猎物的位置","scene":"洞穴里没有一丝光，蝙蝠发出短促的尖啸，再凭折返的声音绕开岩壁。In a cave with no light at all the bat sends out a short cry and steers around the rock by the sound that comes back, a clear case of echolocation.","sceneCN":"这里 echolocation 指「发出声波并依据回声定位的能力」（第 1 个义项：用回声判断物体的方位与距离）；句意为全黑的洞穴里，蝙蝠靠发出尖啸并听取折返的声音绕开岩壁。图中可辨识物件：洞穴、蝙蝠、声波弧线、折返的回声。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"回声定位（不可数）"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"bat echolocation","zh":"蝙蝠的回声定位"},{"phrase":"echolocation calls","zh":"回声定位叫声"},{"phrase":"an echolocation system","zh":"回声定位系统"},{"phrase":"use echolocation","zh":"使用回声定位"},{"phrase":"an echolocation signal","zh":"回声定位信号"},{"phrase":"study echolocation","zh":"研究回声定位"}],"forms":[{"label":"动词","form":"echolocate"},{"label":"三单","form":"echolocates"},{"label":"过去式","form":"echolocated"},{"label":"现在分词","form":"echolocating"},{"label":"施动者名词","form":"echolocator"},{"label":"相关名词（回声）","form":"echo"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"echolocate","pos":"v.","zh":"用回声定位"},{"word":"echolocator","pos":"n.","zh":"使用回声定位的动物或装置"},{"word":"echolocating","pos":"adj.","zh":"进行回声定位的"},{"word":"echo","pos":"n./v.","zh":"回声；回响"},{"word":"location","pos":"n.","zh":"位置；定位"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Biological echolocation","titleCN":"生物的回声定位","definition":"the biological ability to locate objects by emitting sounds and reading their echoes","definitionCN":"发出声音并解读回声以确定物体位置的生物能力","example":"The bat steers around the rock by the sound that comes back.","exampleCN":"蝙蝠靠折返的声音绕开岩壁。","why":"echo plus location says the whole method: a sound returns, and its return is turned into a position.","whyCN":"echo 加 location 说出了整套方法：声音返回，而返回被换算成位置。"},{"no":"02","title":"The sonar mechanism","titleCN":"声呐式机制","definition":"the cycle of emitting a pulse, receiving its reflection and measuring delay and direction","definitionCN":"发出脉冲、接收反射并测量延迟与方向的循环","example":"A short pulse and a quick return mean a near object.","exampleCN":"短脉冲很快返回，说明物体很近。","why":"the mechanism is a clock and a compass built from sound: delay gives distance, direction gives bearing.","whyCN":"这套机制是用声音造出的钟与罗盘：延迟给距离，方向给方位。"},{"no":"03","title":"In bats","titleCN":"蝙蝠的回声定位","definition":"the high-frequency system bats use to hunt and avoid obstacles in darkness","definitionCN":"蝙蝠在黑暗中捕食与避障所用的高频系统","example":"Many bats hunt moths by echolocation.","exampleCN":"许多蝙蝠靠回声定位捕食飞蛾。","why":"bats are the classic case because their world is dark and their calls are ultrasonic, beyond human hearing.","whyCN":"蝙蝠是经典案例，因为它们的世界黑暗，叫声又是人耳听不到的高频。"},{"no":"04","title":"In marine mammals","titleCN":"海洋哺乳动物的回声定位","definition":"the system whales and dolphins use to navigate and find prey underwater","definitionCN":"鲸与海豚在水下导航和寻找猎物所用的系统","example":"Dolphins identify fish shapes by echolocation.","exampleCN":"海豚用回声定位辨认鱼的形状。","why":"water carries sound well, so the same method works over longer ranges than in air.","whyCN":"水传声良好，因此同一方法在水中的有效距离比在空气中更远。"},{"no":"05","title":"Human assistive echolocation","titleCN":"人类的辅助回声定位","definition":"the trained use of tongue clicks or devices to sense nearby objects","definitionCN":"经训练用舌响或装置感知近旁物体","example":"Some blind users learn echolocation with clicks.","exampleCN":"一些盲人使用者学会用舌响做回声定位。","why":"the method is not limited to animals; a human can learn to read echoes, though with coarser resolution.","whyCN":"这种方法并非动物专属；人也能学会解读回声，只是分辨率更粗。"},{"no":"06","title":"Biomimetic engineering","titleCN":"仿生工程中的回声定位","definition":"the design of sonar and sensing devices modelled on animal echolocation","definitionCN":"模仿动物回声定位设计声呐与传感装置","example":"The robot's echolocation maps a dark room.","exampleCN":"机器人的回声定位为暗室绘图。","why":"engineers copy the animal solution when light is unavailable, because sound works where cameras fail.","whyCN":"没有光时工程师就复制动物的方案，因为声音能在相机失效处工作。"},{"no":"07","title":"A recorded behavior in research","titleCN":"研究中被记录的行为","definition":"the observable call-and-return sequence scored by field biologists","definitionCN":"野外生物学家记录的「发声—返回」可观察序列","example":"The recorder logs every echolocation call for later analysis.","exampleCN":"记录仪把每次回声定位叫声存下供后续分析。","why":"research turns a private sense into a public signal: the call can be recorded even when the perception cannot.","whyCN":"研究把私人的感官变成公开的信号：叫声能被录下，哪怕感知无法直接观察。"},{"no":"08","title":"Acoustic surveys for conservation","titleCN":"保护生物学中的声学调查","definition":"the use of echolocation calls to detect and count species without capturing them","definitionCN":"用回声定位叫声在不捕捉的情况下发现并计数物种","example":"Bats are counted by echolocation in the valley each summer.","exampleCN":"每年夏天通过回声定位统计山谷里的蝙蝠。","why":"if a species announces itself by sound, then listening is a non-invasive census.","whyCN":"如果一个物种用声音宣告自己的存在，那么倾听就是一种非侵入式的普查。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Echolocation is an English coinage of the 1940s, joining Greek echo 'sound' to Latin location 'a placing'. Dates are approximate.","cn":"echolocation 是 20 世纪 40 年代的英语新造词，把希腊 echo「声音」与拉丁 location「放置」连在一起。年代为约数。"},"items":[{"era":"GREEK ĒKHŌ","en":"Ēkhō meant 'a sound, a ringing', and in myth named the nymph who could only repeat. English echo came through Latin and French.","cn":"ēkhō 意为「声音、回响」，在神话中是一位只能重复他人话语的仙女。英语 echo 经拉丁与法语而来。"},{"era":"LATIN LOCUS","en":"Locus meant 'place'; from it Latin built locare 'to place' and locatio 'a placing, a letting out'.","cn":"locus 意为「地方」；拉丁语由此构成 locare「放置」与 locatio「放置、出租」。"},{"era":"ENGLISH LOCATION","en":"English location, from locatio through French, dates from the sixteenth century and means the act of placing or the place itself.","cn":"英语 location 经法语来自 locatio，16 世纪出现，指放置的行为或所处的地点。"},{"era":"COINAGE, 1940s","en":"The compound echolocation was coined in the 1940s by researchers studying bats; it names a method rather than a single organ.","cn":"复合词 echolocation 由研究蝙蝠的学者在 20 世纪 40 年代造出；它命名一种方法，而非某个单一器官。"},{"era":"EXTENSION","en":"The word later spread to dolphins and whales, to human assistive training, and to engineered sonar that imitates the biological system.","cn":"这个词后来扩展到海豚与鲸、人类辅助训练，以及模仿生物系统的工程声呐。"},{"era":"UNCERTAIN DETAILS","en":"Source uncertain (first dates): accounts differ on the exact year and author of the coinage, and the claim that echo and location were consciously chosen as classical roots is not documented.","cn":"来源不确定（首见年代）：关于新造词的确切年份与作者，资料说法不一；「有意选用 echo 与 location 作为古典词根」这一点没有文献记录。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"Group one holds forms that look like parts of the word or closely related spellings; group two holds technologies and senses that overlap with it.","cn":"第一组是看似构词成分或拼写接近的形式；第二组是与之重叠的技术与感官词。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"echo","ipa":"/ˈekəʊ/","tag":"the returning sound","definition":"The reflected sound itself; echolocation is the method that uses it, not the sound.","definitionCN":"反射回来的声音本身；echolocation 是利用它的方法，而非声音。"},{"word":"location","ipa":"/ləʊˈkeɪʃn/","tag":"the place, not the method","definition":"A place or the act of placing; it supplies the second half of echolocation but means no sensing.","definitionCN":"地点或放置行为；只提供 echolocation 的后半，不含感知。"},{"word":"locate","ipa":"/ləʊˈkeɪt/","tag":"the verb","definition":"To find the place of something; echolocation is one way of locating, not the act of locating in general.","definitionCN":"找到某物的位置；echolocation 是定位的一种方式，不等于一般定位行为。"},{"word":"echo sounding","ipa":"/ˈekəʊ ˌsaʊndɪŋ/","tag":"the older technical phrase","definition":"Depth measurement by timing a sound pulse; it shares the pulse-and-return logic but measures depth, not a target's position.","definitionCN":"通过给声脉冲计时测深；共享「脉冲—返回」逻辑，但测的是深度，不是目标位置。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"sonar","ipa":"/ˈsəʊnɑː/","tag":"engineered system","definition":"An acronym for sound navigation and ranging, a device-based system; echolocation is the biological original.","definitionCN":"「声导航与测距」的缩略，指装置系统；echolocation 是生物学上的原型。"},{"word":"biosonar","ipa":"/ˈbaɪəʊsəʊnɑː/","tag":"biology's name for it","definition":"The biological sonar of animals; it is close to echolocation but stresses the sonar analogy.","definitionCN":"动物的生物声呐；与 echolocation 接近，但强调声呐类比。"},{"word":"ultrasound","ipa":"/ˈʌltrəsaʊnd/","tag":"the medium","definition":"Sound above human hearing; it is the frequency band many echolocators use, not the method itself.","definitionCN":"高于人耳范围的声波；是许多回声定位者使用的频段，而非方法本身。"},{"word":"navigation","ipa":"/ˌnævɪˈɡeɪʃn/","tag":"the larger goal","definition":"Finding and following a route; echolocation can serve navigation, but it is a sensing method.","definitionCN":"找到并沿路线行进；echolocation 可服务导航，但它是一种感知方法。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Normal associations: real morphemes, real collocations and real relatives, not invented rhymes.","cn":"正常联想：真实的构词成分、真实搭配与真实同族词，而非编造的顺口溜。"},"normal":[{"en":"echo 'returning sound' + location 'placing': the returning sound places the object.","cn":"echo「返回的声音」+ location「放置」：返回的声音把物体定位。"},{"en":"The family runs echolocate, echolocator, echolocating, echo and location.","cn":"同族词包括 echolocate、echolocator、echolocating、echo 与 location。"},{"en":"Fixed phrases mark the users: bat echolocation, echolocation calls, an echolocation system.","cn":"固定搭配标出使用者：蝙蝠回声定位、回声定位叫声、回声定位系统。"},{"en":"The physics is a clock plus a compass: delay for distance, direction for bearing.","cn":"物理原理是一个钟加一个罗盘：延迟给距离，方向给方位。"},{"en":"Echolocation is biological; sonar is the engineered imitation.","cn":"echolocation 是生物的，sonar 是工程的模仿。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture a shout in a dark room returning sooner from the near wall than the far one.","cn":"想象在暗室中喊一声，近墙的回声比远墙先回来。"},{"en":"Picture a blind walker tapping a cane and hearing the shape of the step ahead.","cn":"想象盲人用手杖敲击，凭声音听出前面台阶的形状。"},{"en":"Picture a cave where every rock casts a sound-shadow instead of a light-shadow.","cn":"想象一座洞穴，每块岩石投下的是声影而非光影。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"Bats use echolocation to catch insects in complete darkness.","cn":"蝙蝠在完全黑暗中用回声定位捕食昆虫。"},{"en":"The dolphin's echolocation can distinguish a fish from a rock of the same size.","cn":"海豚的回声定位能区分鱼与同样大小的石头。"},{"en":"Engineers built a robot that maps caves by echolocation.","cn":"工程师造出一台靠回声定位测绘洞穴的机器人。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"拆词记忆 · 非词源","text":"echo（回声）+ location（定位）——靠回声找出位置 → 回声定位","word":"echolocation"},"root":"echo（希腊 ēkhō「声音、回响」）+ location（拉丁 locus「地方」经 locare「放置」）；20 世纪 40 年代英语新造词。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses follow the pulse outward and back: the biological method, the clock-and-compass mechanism, bats, whales, blind users, robots, recorded calls, and acoustic censuses.","cn":"八个义项沿「发出再返回」展开：生物方法、钟与罗盘的机制、蝙蝠、鲸、盲人使用者、机器人、被录下的叫声，以及声学普查。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a pulse leaves, strikes, returns, and the delay draws a position in the dark.","cn":"核心意象：一次脉冲发出、撞上、返回，延迟在黑暗中画出一个位置。"},"chain":["PULSE","TRAVEL","REFLECT","RETURN","MEASURE","LOCATE"],"branches":[{"senses":"01 · 02","en":"THE METHOD: a pulse, a return, and a measured delay make a position.","cn":"方法：脉冲、返回与测得的延迟构成一个位置。"},{"senses":"03 · 04","en":"THE ANIMALS: bats in air and dolphins in water use the same physics at different ranges.","cn":"动物：空中的蝙蝠与水中的海豚在各自距离上使用同一物理原理。"},{"senses":"05","en":"THE HUMAN: a trained listener can read echoes, though at coarser resolution.","cn":"人：受过训练的听者能解读回声，只是分辨率更粗。"},{"senses":"06","en":"THE MACHINE: engineering copies the animal where light fails.","cn":"机器：在光失效处，工程复制动物。"},{"senses":"07 · 08","en":"THE RECORD: calls become data, and data becomes a non-invasive census.","cn":"记录：叫声变成数据，数据变成非侵入式普查。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Echolocation joins a Greek sound-word to a Latin place-word; the compound is modern, so each half keeps its own ancient family.","cn":"echolocation 把一个希腊「声音」词与一个拉丁「地方」词连在一起；复合词是现代构造，两半各自保留古老词族。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Latin locus 'place' gives locare and locatio, the source of English location and locate. Echo is Greek and has no Latin cognate, so it appears only as a borrowed first element.","cn":"拉丁 locus「地方」生成 locare 与 locatio，是英语 location 与 locate 的来源。echo 属希腊语，没有拉丁同族词，只作为借入的第一成分出现。"},"items":[{"word":"ēkhō","structure":"ēkhō (Greek noun, 'sound, echo')","meaning":"sound, ringing, echo","meaningCN":"声音；回响；回声","example":"English echo came through Latin and French.","exampleCN":"英语 echo 经拉丁与法语而来。"},{"word":"locus","structure":"locus, loci (Latin noun, second declension)","meaning":"place, spot","meaningCN":"地方；位置","example":"Locus is the root of location.","exampleCN":"locus 是 location 的词根。"},{"word":"locare","structure":"locare, locavi, locatum (Latin verb)","meaning":"to place, put","meaningCN":"放置；安置","example":"Locare supplies the verb of placing.","exampleCN":"locare 提供「放置」的动词义。"},{"word":"locatio","structure":"locare + -atio","meaning":"a placing; a letting out","meaningCN":"放置；出租","example":"Locatio became English location.","exampleCN":"locatio 成为英语 location。"},{"word":"echo","structure":"Greek ēkhō through Latin echo","meaning":"a reflected sound","meaningCN":"反射回来的声音","example":"An echo tells distance by its delay.","exampleCN":"回声用延迟说明距离。"},{"word":"location","structure":"locatio through French","meaning":"a place or the act of placing","meaningCN":"地点或放置行为","example":"The location of the target is the output.","exampleCN":"目标的位置就是输出。"},{"word":"echolocation","structure":"echo + location","meaning":"locating by reflected sound","meaningCN":"靠反射声定位","example":"Echolocation works where light fails.","exampleCN":"回声定位在光失效处仍有效。"},{"word":"echolocate","structure":"echolocation back-formed as a verb","meaning":"to locate by echolocation","meaningCN":"用回声定位","example":"The bat echolocates at high frequency.","exampleCN":"蝙蝠以高频进行回声定位。"},{"word":"echolocator","structure":"echolocate + -or","meaning":"an animal or device that echolocates","meaningCN":"进行回声定位的动物或装置","example":"The device is a simple echolocator.","exampleCN":"这个装置是一个简易的回声定位器。"},{"word":"biosonar","structure":"bio- (life) + sonar","meaning":"biological sonar","meaningCN":"生物声呐","example":"Biosonar is the engineer's name for echolocation.","exampleCN":"「生物声呐」是工程师对回声定位的叫法。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"locus","structure":"locus, loci (m., second declension)","meaning":"place, spot","meaningCN":"地方；位置"},{"word":"locare","structure":"locare, locavi, locatum (verb, first conjugation)","meaning":"to place, put","meaningCN":"放置；安置"},{"word":"locatio","structure":"locatio, locationis (f., third declension)","meaning":"a placing; a letting out","meaningCN":"放置；出租"}]}},{"word":"camouflage","ipa_uk":"/ˈkæməflɑːʒ/","ipa_us":"/ˈkæməflɑːʒ/","definition_zh":"伪装；使动物、装备或人不易被发现的体色、形态或掩饰手段","definition_en":"the colors, shapes or devices that make an animal, person or object hard to see or detect","core_image":"一只蛾的翅纹与树皮纹理完全重合，停上去就消失不见","scene":"树干上的蛾子把翅膀张开，翅面的斑纹与地衣的碎块几乎重合，寻找它的鸟从旁边飞过。The moth spreads its wings against the trunk until the patches match the lichen, and the bird hunting it passes by, a textbook example of camouflage.","sceneCN":"这里 camouflage 指「使动物不易被发现的体色与斑纹」（第 1 个义项：外形与背景融为一体）；句意为蛾子的翅纹与地衣几乎重合，捕食的鸟从旁边飞过也没发现它。图中可辨识物件：树干、地衣、展开翅膀的蛾、飞过的鸟。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"伪装；保护色；掩饰手段（不可数）"},{"tag":"v.","zh":"伪装；掩饰"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"natural camouflage","zh":"天然伪装"},{"phrase":"military camouflage","zh":"军事伪装"},{"phrase":"a camouflage pattern","zh":"伪装图案"},{"phrase":"a camouflage net","zh":"伪装网"},{"phrase":"perfect camouflage","zh":"完美的伪装"},{"phrase":"under camouflage","zh":"在伪装之下"}],"forms":[{"label":"三单（动词）","form":"camouflages"},{"label":"过去式","form":"camouflaged"},{"label":"现在分词","form":"camouflaging"},{"label":"形容词（已伪装的）","form":"camouflaged"},{"label":"施动者名词（罕见）","form":"camoufleur"},{"label":"口语缩略","form":"camo"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"camouflaged","pos":"adj.","zh":"伪装过的；隐蔽的"},{"word":"camouflaging","pos":"adj.","zh":"起伪装作用的"},{"word":"camoufleur","pos":"n.","zh":"伪装师（罕用）"},{"word":"camo","pos":"n./adj.","zh":"迷彩；迷彩的（口语）"},{"word":"camouflage net","pos":"n.","zh":"伪装网"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Animal protective coloration","titleCN":"动物的保护色与斑纹","definition":"the colors and patterns that let an animal blend into its background","definitionCN":"使动物与背景融为一体、难以被看见的颜色与图案","example":"The moth's wing patches match the lichen exactly.","exampleCN":"蛾翅上的斑块与地衣完全相合。","why":"the word first served hunters and naturalists describing animals that seem to vanish against bark, sand or leaves.","whyCN":"这个词最初服务于猎人与博物学者，用来描述在树皮、沙地或叶片前仿佛消失的动物。"},{"no":"02","title":"Concealment by behavior","titleCN":"靠行为的隐蔽","definition":"actions such as freezing, crouching or changing posture that reduce visibility","definitionCN":"静止、伏低或改变姿态等降低可见度的动作","example":"The fawn lies flat and does not move while the doe feeds.","exampleCN":"母鹿觅食时，幼鹿趴平不动。","why":"camouflage is not only worn; it is also done, and stillness can hide an animal whose colors already match.","whyCN":"伪装不只穿在身上，也做在动作里；静止能藏住一只颜色已相配的动物。"},{"no":"03","title":"Military camouflage","titleCN":"军事伪装","definition":"the disguising of troops, vehicles and positions to avoid detection","definitionCN":"使部队、车辆与阵地不被发现而进行的掩饰","example":"The battery was hidden under camouflage netting.","exampleCN":"炮兵连被伪装网遮住。","why":"modern warfare made the word famous: a gun that can be seen is a gun that will be hit.","whyCN":"现代战争让这个词广为人知：能被看见的火炮，就是会被击中的火炮。"},{"no":"04","title":"Camouflage clothing and material","titleCN":"迷彩服与伪装材料","definition":"the printed fabrics, nets and covers used to hide people or equipment","definitionCN":"用于隐藏人员或装备的印花布料、网与遮盖物","example":"The unit wore woodland camouflage in the forest.","exampleCN":"这支部队在森林里穿林地迷彩。","why":"metonymy turns the method into the kit: the pattern itself comes to be called camouflage.","whyCN":"转喻把方法变成装备：图案本身也被称作 camouflage。"},{"no":"05","title":"Figurative disguise of intent","titleCN":"比喻：掩饰真实意图","definition":"words or actions that hide one's real purpose or feeling","definitionCN":"掩盖真实目的或感受的言语与行动","example":"His calm tone was camouflage for panic.","exampleCN":"他平静的语气是对慌乱的掩饰。","why":"if a body can be hidden against a background, a motive can be hidden behind a manner.","whyCN":"如果身体能藏在背景前，动机也能藏在举止后面。"},{"no":"06","title":"Protective coloration as a term","titleCN":"保护色（术语）","definition":"the biological term for coloration that lowers the chance of detection by predators or prey","definitionCN":"指降低被天敌或猎物发现几率的体色的生物学术语","example":"Protective coloration is the scientific name for one kind of camouflage.","exampleCN":"保护色是某一类伪装在科学上的名称。","why":"science needed a narrower label, so camouflage became the umbrella and protective coloration one branch under it.","whyCN":"科学需要更窄的标签，于是 camouflage 成为伞名，保护色成为其下的一支。"},{"no":"07","title":"Resemblance to another object","titleCN":"与另一物体相似的伪装形态","definition":"shapes that make an organism resemble a leaf, twig, stone or another species","definitionCN":"使生物看起来像叶片、枝条、石头或另一物种的形态","example":"The insect's body mimics a dead twig.","exampleCN":"这只昆虫的身体模仿一根枯枝。","why":"blending in and looking like something else are neighboring strategies, and everyday usage often puts both under camouflage.","whyCN":"融入背景与长得像别的东西是相邻的策略，日常用法常把两者都归入 camouflage。"},{"no":"08","title":"Visual deception in design","titleCN":"设计中的视觉欺骗","definition":"the use of pattern and contrast to hide an object in plain sight, as in vehicles or buildings","definitionCN":"用图案与对比把物体藏在显眼处，如车辆或建筑","example":"The aircraft's paint breaks up its outline against the sky.","exampleCN":"飞机的涂装打散了它在天空中的轮廓。","why":"the principle is general: high-contrast false edges defeat the eye that looks for a continuous outline.","whyCN":"原理是通用的：高对比的假边缘能骗过寻找连续轮廓的眼睛。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Camouflage came into English from French during the First World War; French camoufler 'to disguise' probably goes back to Italian camuffare, whose deeper origin is uncertain. Dates are approximate.","cn":"camouflage 在第一次世界大战期间由法语进入英语；法语 camoufler「伪装」大概可追溯到意大利语 camuffare，其更早来源不确定。年代为约数。"},"items":[{"era":"FRENCH CAMOUFLER","en":"Camoufler meant 'to disguise, mask'; it was the verb used by French forces for hiding guns and positions from aerial observation.","cn":"camoufler 意为「伪装、遮掩」；法国军队用它指把火炮与阵地隐藏起来，避开空中观察。"},{"era":"ITALIAN CAMUFFARE","en":"Italian camuffare 'to disguise, trick' is the likely source of the French verb; the two languages shared the term in military and theatrical circles.","cn":"意大利语 camuffare「伪装、欺骗」是法语动词的可能来源；两种语言在军事与戏剧圈中共用这个词。"},{"era":"UNCERTAIN DEEPER ORIGIN","en":"Source uncertain: camuffare may involve capo 'head' plus muffare 'to muffle', but this is a suggestion, not an established derivation, and no reliable Latin root can be asserted.","cn":"来源不确定：camuffare 可能由 capo「头」与 muffare「包裹、闷住」组成，但这只是推测，并非确立的派生；无法断言可靠的拉丁词根。"},{"era":"ENGLISH, 1917","en":"English adopted camouflage during the First World War, first for the disguising of artillery and later for the painted patterns themselves.","cn":"英语在第一次世界大战期间借入 camouflage，最初指火炮的掩饰，后来指涂装图案本身。"},{"era":"WIDER USES","en":"In the twentieth century the word spread to animal coloration, hunting gear, fashion and figurative disguise of intention.","cn":"20 世纪，这个词扩展到动物体色、狩猎装备、时装，以及比喻性的意图掩饰。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"Group one holds forms built on camouflage itself; group two holds neighboring strategies of concealment and imitation.","cn":"第一组是 camouflage 本身构成的形式；第二组是相邻的隐蔽与模仿策略。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"camouflaged","ipa":"/ˈkæməflɑːʒd/","tag":"adjective or participle","definition":"Hidden by camouflage; the -ed form describes the object, while camouflage names the method or material.","definitionCN":"被伪装遮住的；-ed 形式描述对象，而 camouflage 命名方法或材料。"},{"word":"camoufleur","ipa":"/ˌkæməˈflɜː/","tag":"the person","definition":"A person who designs or applies camouflage, especially in the military; the French agent noun is rare in English.","definitionCN":"设计或实施伪装的人，尤指军中；这个法语施动名词在英语中罕用。"},{"word":"camouflage net","ipa":"/ˈkæməflɑːʒ net/","tag":"compound","definition":"A net printed or scrimmed to hide equipment; the compound narrows camouflage to one piece of kit.","definitionCN":"用于遮盖装备的印花或网眼织物；该复合词把 camouflage 收窄为一件装备。"},{"word":"camo","ipa":"/ˈkæməʊ/","tag":"clipping","definition":"The informal short form for camouflage pattern or clothing; it has lost the final syllables and most of the formal tone.","definitionCN":"伪装图案或服装的口语简称；省去末尾音节，也去掉了大部分正式语气。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"mimicry","ipa":"/ˈmɪmɪkri/","tag":"resembling another species","definition":"The evolved resemblance of one organism to another; camouflage hides an animal in its background, mimicry makes it look like something else.","definitionCN":"一种生物与另一种生物的演化相似；camouflage 把动物藏进背景，mimicry 让它看起来像别的东西。"},{"word":"disguise","ipa":"/dɪsˈɡaɪz/","tag":"changing appearance","definition":"A change of appearance meant to deceive; camouflage is one means of disguise, especially in the visual field.","definitionCN":"为欺骗而改变外观；camouflage 是伪装的一种手段，尤在视觉层面。"},{"word":"concealment","ipa":"/kənˈsiːlmənt/","tag":"hiding","definition":"The act of keeping something out of sight; it is the general purpose that camouflage serves.","definitionCN":"把某物藏在视线之外的行为；是 camouflage 所服务的一般目的。"},{"word":"protective coloration","ipa":"/prəˈtektɪv ˌkʌləˈreɪʃn/","tag":"the biological branch","definition":"Coloration that reduces detection; it is the scientific term for one kind of camouflage.","definitionCN":"降低被发现几率的体色；是某一类伪装在科学上的名称。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Normal associations: real morphemes, real collocations and real relatives, not invented rhymes.","cn":"正常联想：真实的构词成分、真实搭配与真实同族词，而非编造的顺口溜。"},"normal":[{"en":"The word is French military vocabulary adopted in 1917: first the act of masking guns, then the painted pattern.","cn":"这个词是 1917 年借入的法语军事词汇：先指遮蔽火炮的动作，后指涂装图案。"},{"en":"The family runs camouflage, camouflaged, camouflaging, camoufleur and the clipping camo.","cn":"同族词包括 camouflage、camouflaged、camouflaging、camoufleur 与缩略 camo。"},{"en":"Fixed phrases mark the uses: natural camouflage, military camouflage, camouflage pattern, camouflage net.","cn":"固定搭配标出用法：天然伪装、军事伪装、伪装图案、伪装网。"},{"en":"Camouflage hides by matching the background; mimicry hides by resembling another object or species.","cn":"camouflage 靠与背景相合来隐藏；mimicry 靠像另一物体或物种来隐藏。"},{"en":"Do not assert a Latin root: the deeper origin of camuffare is uncertain.","cn":"不要断言拉丁词根：camuffare 的更早来源不确定。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture a moth whose wings are a copy of the bark it rests on.","cn":"想象一只蛾，翅膀就是它所停树皮的复制品。"},{"en":"Picture a net painted with the same shadows as the ground it covers.","cn":"想象一张网，画着与所盖地面相同的阴影。"},{"en":"Picture a calm face that hides a racing pulse.","cn":"想象一张平静的脸，藏住飞快的脉搏。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The lizard's camouflage makes it almost invisible on the sand.","cn":"蜥蜴的伪装让它在沙地上几乎看不见。"},{"en":"Troops draped camouflage over the vehicles before dawn.","cn":"部队在黎明前给车辆盖上伪装。"},{"en":"His jokes were camouflage for a serious complaint.","cn":"他的玩笑是对一项严肃抱怨的掩饰。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"「卡目弗拉日」——把身形卡进背景里，让目光滑过去 → 伪装","word":"camouflage"},"root":"法语 camouflage ← camoufler「伪装」← 意大利语 camuffare「伪装、欺骗」；更早来源不确定，无可靠拉丁同族词。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses spread from one trick: match the background, then hold still, then hide troops, wear the pattern, mask a motive, name the biological branch, resemble another object, and deceive the eye in design.","cn":"八个义项从一个把戏展开：与背景相合、保持不动、藏住部队、穿上图案、掩盖动机、命名生物学分支、像另一物体，以及在设计中骗过眼睛。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: an outline that stops being an outline because the surface behind it is repeated on it.","cn":"核心意象：一个轮廓不再是轮廓，因为它表面重复了背后的纹理。"},"chain":["BACKGROUND","MATCH","BLEND","DISAPPEAR","DECEIVE","PROTECT"],"branches":[{"senses":"01 · 06 · 07","en":"THE BIOLOGY: matching the background, naming the branch, and resembling another object are three related tricks.","cn":"生物学：与背景相合、命名分支、像另一物体，是三个相关把戏。"},{"senses":"02","en":"STILLNESS: behavior completes what coloration begins.","cn":"静止：行为补全体色开始的事。"},{"senses":"03 · 04","en":"THE MILITARY: the word's modern fame comes from hiding guns and then wearing the pattern.","cn":"军事：这个词的现代名声来自藏炮，随后是穿上图案。"},{"senses":"05","en":"HIDDEN MOTIVE: words and actions disguise what is really intended.","cn":"隐藏的动机：言语与行动掩盖真实意图。"},{"senses":"08","en":"DESIGN: false edges defeat the eye that searches for a continuous outline.","cn":"设计：假边缘骗过寻找连续轮廓的眼睛。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Camouflage is a French noun in -age built on the verb camoufler. English adds -ed, -ing and a clipping, but the deeper morphology is not reliably recoverable.","cn":"camouflage 是法语中以 -age 结尾的名词，由动词 camoufler 构成。英语加上 -ed、-ing 与一个缩略形式，但更早的形态无法可靠还原。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Camouflage has no reliable Latin cognate, so latinEntries is left empty; the likely Italian source camuffare is itself of uncertain origin.","cn":"camouflage 没有可靠的拉丁同族词，因此拉丁词条留空；可能的意大利语来源 camuffare 本身来源不明。"},"items":[{"word":"camoufler","structure":"French verb, 'to disguise, mask'","meaning":"to disguise","meaningCN":"伪装；遮掩","example":"French units camouflaged their guns in 1915.","exampleCN":"法军部队在 1915 年伪装火炮。"},{"word":"camuffare","structure":"Italian verb, probable source of camoufler","meaning":"to disguise, trick","meaningCN":"伪装；欺骗","example":"The Italian verb is the likely origin, not a proven one.","exampleCN":"这个意大利语动词是可能来源，而非已证来源。"},{"word":"-age","structure":"-age (French noun suffix from Latin -aticum)","meaning":"an action or a collective result","meaningCN":"动作或集合结果","example":"The suffix turns the verb into the name of the practice.","exampleCN":"这个后缀把动词变成实践的名称。"},{"word":"camouflage","structure":"camoufler + -age","meaning":"the act or material of disguising","meaningCN":"伪装的行为或材料","example":"Camouflage hid the battery from the air.","exampleCN":"伪装把炮兵连从空中藏了起来。"},{"word":"camouflaged","structure":"camouflage + -ed","meaning":"hidden by camouflage","meaningCN":"被伪装遮住的","example":"The truck was fully camouflaged.","exampleCN":"卡车被完全伪装起来。"},{"word":"camouflaging","structure":"camouflage + -ing","meaning":"serving to hide","meaningCN":"起伪装作用的","example":"Camouflaging paint breaks the outline.","exampleCN":"伪装涂料打散了轮廓。"},{"word":"camoufleur","structure":"French camoufleur (agent noun)","meaning":"one who camouflages","meaningCN":"伪装者；伪装师","example":"A camoufleur designed the netting.","exampleCN":"一位伪装师设计了这些网。"},{"word":"camo","structure":"camouflage clipped to camo","meaning":"camouflage pattern or clothing","meaningCN":"迷彩图案或服装","example":"He wore camo in the field.","exampleCN":"他在野外穿迷彩。"},{"word":"camouflage net","structure":"camouflage + net (compound)","meaning":"a net used to hide equipment","meaningCN":"用于遮盖装备的网","example":"They spread a camouflage net over the trench.","exampleCN":"他们在战壕上铺开伪装网。"},{"word":"counter-camouflage","structure":"counter- (against) + camouflage","meaning":"methods for detecting disguised objects","meaningCN":"用于发现被伪装物体的方法","example":"Thermal cameras serve as counter-camouflage.","exampleCN":"热成像相机可作反伪装手段。"}],"latinEntries":[]}}]);
